53:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: CSRF origin validation now checks effective request scheme (#12)\n\nThe checkOrigin function previously accepted both http:// and https://\nfor the same host, meaning an HTTPS deployment would accept an http://\norigin. Now derives the effective scheme from r.TLS and X-Forwarded-Proto\nand only matches against that exact scheme+host. TrustedOrigins and bare\nhost matching continue to work as before.\n\nCloses #1","tree":{"sha":"5e48215fb7a383ef630857e098bd8d03c4049884","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/dorman/git/trees/5e48215fb7a383ef630857e098bd8d03c4049884"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/dorman/git/commits/88f3be8c44aea0af06835df5a026b3fb8391f406","verification":{"payload":"tree 5e48215fb7a383ef630857e098bd8d03c4049884\nparent 4eac7e2d07541c8acdca7f413e65b218e513b5ac\nauthor Meow Honk <21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com> 1775573587 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1775573587 -0500\n\nfix: CSRF origin validation now checks effective request scheme (#12)\n\nThe checkOrigin function previously accepted both http:// and https://\nfor the same host, meaning an HTTPS deployment would accept an http://\norigin. Now derives the effective scheme from r.TLS and X-Forwarded-Proto\nand only matches against that exact scheme+host. TrustedOrigins and bare\nhost matching continue to work as before.\n\nCloses #1","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp1RpTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAX/AQAHtWe9ZCh0pRRHmXVQu5CEVT\nlfisp3GxYVvVHEyHARCEW5pfjcUQVqWLKJuGeum7K3j+6dNQgyyWll/jRAipfrag\nbCoF7b2pUBJU2CmpLtGt1NKOcW0+X6oKYOAo3DEt87BTl3cp0MMeRvFOXmH2tXXe\n9xDISQuC5d/3WcHPeWKSeliuERLVlzvgrsYPQAolDLsqYFqg94RI3MQ+BtIGMGvY\nAqi0YA+OIw9dnsQYB2rXaICIfxVK86z79qn6gOc6nwT5I2whE7jaDmyjaBz8vpKA\n6lhD8riypqv2/RgVgUM6VTP0gqJ0+qyz9sBZ0+IGOWkfhJz5G1l3EyrsPD5pPR51\nRRQ5T05OnToc/XJMormCyj8punflmQHe0MuxHezRBi94JAtsGn9ZqGvkhJKBFMHt\npFPCY/H69CHQ26y//ts0/Ojq+FXOXpzg+hTcP