github.com/users/Japesg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Japesg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/skysolutionsus/sky-sentinel/commits/f38f356a2bc02c81a85d1de701549b1e3115818b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-24T00:08:46Z","email":"japesg@users.noreply.github.com","name":"James Galang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-24T00:08:46Z","email":"japesg@users.noreply.github.com","name":"James Galang"},"message":"fix: pre-assign Gold Rush clusters in seed, preserve through anomaly pipeline\n\nRoot cause: DBSCAN clustering was unreliable because CMS API returns\ndifferent real suppliers each seed, changing the feature distribution.\nDBSCAN would merge all fraud suppliers into 1 blob or split them\nunpredictably.\n\nFix:\n- seed_data.py now creates SupplierCluster records during _inject_fraud_clusters\n- All 6 clusters bumped to 5+ members (was 4 for clusters 5/6)\n- anomaly_detection.py preserves pre-assigned clusters, only runs DBSCAN\n  on non-assigned suppliers for additional discovery\n- Added random.seed(42) for remaining deterministic behavior\n- Result: 6 consistent clusters (8, 6, 5, 5, 5, 5 members)","tree":{"sha":"b0ccb842429a4dc65c803046dbeec2d324cbdcdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/skysolutionsus/sky-sentinel/git/trees/b0ccb842429a4dc65c803046dbeec2d324cbdcdf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/skysolutionsus/sky-sentinel/git/commits/f38f356a2bc02c81a85d1de701549b1e3115818b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18168062?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Japesg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Japesg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Japesg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Japesg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"