ubusercontent.com/u/256992008?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madrobotnet/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madrobotnet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madrobotnet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madrobotnet/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/madrobotnet","id":256992008,"login":"madrobotnet","node_id":"U_kgDOD1FjCA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madrobotnet/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madrobotnet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madrobotnet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madrobotnet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madrobotnet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/madrobotnet","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/commits/445e29ec942b6db5cb11bb39d7ddb1eb848e817f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-31T02:15:44Z","email":"madrobot@gmail.com","name":"Kyungwoo Seo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-31T02:15:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"i18n(ko): complete Korean translation — add 273 missing keys (#521)\n\nSections added:\n- agentDetail (149 keys): agent lifecycle, SOUL, tools, sandbox, memory\n- logViewer (29 keys): real-time log stream UI\n- debug (28 keys): gateway diagnostics panel\n- gatewayConfig (20 keys): configuration panel\n- agentHistory (15 keys): activity timeline\n- documents (13 keys): document viewer\n- pipeline (13 keys): pipeline management\n- orchestration (2 keys), AGENTDETAIL (4 keys)\n\nTranslation notes:\n- Follows existing ko.json tone (concise UI labels, no honorifics)\n- deny → 거부 (aligned with existing execApproval/auditTrail usage)\n- busy → 사용 중 (aligned with agentSquad.busy)\n- Technical terms kept as-is: SOUL, OpenClaw, JSON, API, ID\n- All interpolation variables preserved\n\nCoverage: 86.6% → 100% (1768/2041 → 2041/2041 keys)","tree":{"sha":"7753a141a0a0de0af5cd47e13948d4993f6355a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/git/trees/7753a141a0a0de0af5cd47e13948d4993f6355a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/git/commits/445e29ec942b6db5cb11bb39d7ddb1eb848e817f","verification":{"payload":"tree 7753a141a0a0de0af5cd47e13948d4993f6355a6\nparent 3bd462c1cbea9992eb5fabebe4e729a78a228a2a\nauthor Kyungwoo Seo <madrobot@gmail.com> 1774923344 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774923344 +0700\n\ni18n(ko): complete Korean translation — add 273 missing keys (#521)\n\nSections added:\n- agentDetail (149 keys): agent lifecycle, SOUL, tools, sandbox, memory\n- logViewer (29 keys): real-time log stream UI\n- debug (28 keys): gateway diagnostics panel\n- gatewayConfig (20 keys): configuration panel\n- agentHistory (15 keys): activity timeline\n- documents (13 keys): document viewer\n- pipeline (13 keys): pipeline management\n- orchestration (2 keys), AGENTDETAIL (4 keys)\n\nTranslation notes:\n- Follows existing ko.json tone (concise UI labels, no honorifics)\n- deny → 거부 (aligned with existing execApproval/auditTrail usage)\n- busy → 사용 중 (aligned with agentSquad.busy)\n- Technical terms kept as-is: SOUL, OpenClaw, JSON, API, ID\n- All interpolation variables preserved\n\nCoverage: 86.6% → 100% (1768/2041 → 2041/2041 keys)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpyy5QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm3sQAEqpRlc8lUVa2GVrULNnl6IP\nw4uBjMtPRbXjk+j73R0pKB7CysbURjlES05yOyzn47NJggf78UaToG8zKFM1v6bR\n2RL3q+1uY/4kp5PxKplNfvrPwWr3UKUP4JglfhkDR0HTpWeHGhOQaL0QFNgKSQYx\nPg2B8h43eH1GjxBMlqnX+sQbEkcXI4lR6bbIFOuRUKx21MnD0bmedy1strpKmrgx\nAuix7S6TGVFYi0STIiNETuDKqvm5PGinyeUxPSItaGTDXJwcjTEun1a7QN1bERWN\nrqJCi8pqBQJ8cWF596Q8MCMwDbP+6yb8Ju9tWEITdS1Twwot+AqwGfRxjHJNu6L/\nRRnmj2DYzvJ5cv+49ao/4OmVQoDKsoBW9Ts49zKxlcsM6Z3UVJNlsGjFTJvjK+xZ\nPg8Exkd4mtlTeBA6XEIgsiwalwhE6pzzC5exGDBL36psHSE1Q1QSxb35FDiKGxND\n29sJBvRIjAO9BWQf8Q+JuHRg+YfjVfxACpNoxnZmFxnqRxf/0/LahFEE0QI2G2Sy\nT2eUmphIq7fzieOx7YOHP0b2FB+xEL5FNlexbjKGapeoubWnOXmbX2pPVxOiEE4C\nUv41m/2lVEwudev6qC/VhNbRMZj0YSb1uUCEZ4zdlQoc4Ll5u+cEIX9iGTfUDnw3\nBd/hMtB9sulbdQKajuzy\n=KCte\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-08T03:58:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/khamis1992/mission-control/commit/445e29ec942b6db5cb11bb39d7ddb1eb848e817f","node_id":"C_kwDOR8sI2toAKDQ0NWUyOWVjOTQyYjZkYjVjYjExYmIzOWQ3ZGRiMWViODQ4ZTgxN2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/khamis1992/mission-control/commit/3bd462c1cbea9992eb5fabebe4e729a78a228a2a","sha":"3bd462c1cbea9992eb5fabebe4e729a78a228a2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/commits/3bd462c1cbea9992eb5fabebe4e729a78a228a2a"}],"sha":"445e29ec942b6db5cb11bb39d7ddb1eb848e817f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/commits/445e29ec942b6db5cb11bb39d7ddb1eb848e817f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4118421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Shipu","id":4118421,"login":"Shipu","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMTg0MjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/commits/3bd462c1cbea9992eb5fabebe4e729a78a228a2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-31T02:15:40Z","email":"shipuahamed01@gmail.com","name":"Shipu Ahamed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-31T02:15:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: detect Claude Code auth via ~/.claude.json OAuth account (#510)\n\nClaude Code''s claude.ai subscription login does not write a credential\nfile inside ~/.claude/. Instead, the OAuth account is stored in\n~/.claude.json under the oauthAccount key, with the actual access token\nmanaged by the OS keychain.\n\nThe previous detection logic checked for:\n  - ~/.claude/credentials.json\n  - ~/.claude/.credentials\n  - ~/.claude/settings.json\n\nNone of these files are created by the default claude.ai login flow,\ncausing Mission Control to always report Claude as unauthenticated even\nwhen the user was fully logged in.\n\nFix: use a three-tier detection strategy:\n  1. Read ~/.claude.json and check oauthAccount.emailAddress (covers all\n     claude.ai subscription logins — the most common case)\n  2. Read ~/.claude/.credentials.json and check claudeAiOauth.accessToken\n     or apiKey (covers Anthropic Console / older OAuth installs)\n  3. Fall back to `claude auth status --json` (covers ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\n     env-var auth and any future auth mechanisms)\n\nFixes: Claude Code runtime always showing unauthenticated status in the\nonboarding wizard and runtime card despite successful login.","tree":{"sha":"b26b10cc8080e27ad123d9d33fb43a62b42b7387","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/git/trees/b26b10cc8080e27ad123d9d33fb43a62b42b7387"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/git/commits/3bd462c1cbea9992eb5fabebe4e729a78a228a2a","verification":{"payload":"tree b26b10cc8080e27ad123d9d33fb43a62b42b7387\nparent 581fbf13db4a84463649b671dafee53dc52f91d6\nauthor Shipu Ahamed <shipuahamed01@gmail.com> 1774923340 +0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774923340 +0700\n\nfix: detect Claude Code auth via ~/.claude.json OAuth account (#510)\n\nClaude Code''s claude.ai subscription login does not write a credential\nfile inside ~/.claude/. Instead, the OAuth account is stored in\n~/.claude.json under the oauthAccount key, with the actual access token\nmanaged by the OS keychain.\n\nThe previous detection logic checked for:\n  - ~/.claude/credentials.json\n  - ~/.claude/.credentials\n  - ~/.claude/settings.json\n\nNone of these files are created by the default claude.ai login flow,\ncausing Mission Control to always report Claude as unauthenticated even\nwhen the user was fully logged in.\n\nFix: use a three-tier detection strategy:\n  1. Read ~/.claude.json and check oauthAccount.emailAddress (covers all\n     claude.ai subscription logins — the most common case)\n  2. Read ~/.claude/.credentials.json and check claudeAiOauth.accessToken\n     or apiKey (covers Anthropic Console / older OAuth installs)\n  3. Fall back to `claude auth status --json` (covers ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\n     env-var auth and any future auth mechanisms)\n\nFixes: Claude Code runtime always showing unauthenticated status in the\nonboarding wizard and runtime card despite successful login.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpyy5MCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPiUQAGfJ7SzJcMbc4QLb5y5xSSPp\n3sFCHNnPkCYyoyJcYewkzBk36ZSV0itJlLPUKo/09jeIS6qejUKFT26t67DutGha\nJZXjHtlaGon+jC+l3t2SiASyd0+VDIVkRAC8AlhSUm66mEcynU/893SxBH8s+opa\nSutABlqA8/EfbTgYanfOwta55csihmnSCxOV2X5RELhJ2+bv6HWDZ+CSsDyU59tV\nYGUV/HBIjzurEJbtkPf8rYk77rhmhwcGqfrdC4g2jT7+lPY/4yDKgRvQWDLmi3Sj\nJmEgDtYyLbxwscVNjBiPrz3F+wQnqJG05keygVg2ohg88SaqVzFvAO9A/KQ7xUKa\nmMS+uMMDgh/FcGNu8BNIFTOobko1gfQQ3MhPXbJNdtyvqr2n++9BCi0DFxXwfwiz\ni9NAr93okk15A9FUy7CrI4rwTwzqSUnY+qCYa8p+OtxhnAeExRXiootBsOVKWgRd\nFcQE+iFZ+3s+ZG2D4aoXvDteDGwZORSww6Sy6iAaTJHhFnu3x2bFqJthOgHvMrE0\n5reas2zXXkFw7G2/eLLPa+Lf2yfyEHNhMnspJzkwWV4G4CjVY9cQ5Q3SoN4+APCh\nUnCKgeXLIII67yZalrm7snFQftHOD6vOfTqheXWvWPZG/gVvljEcYdS4nWKi5gqm\ngYNmn50mGXfGXM1cjdpj\n=5Dx8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-08T03:58:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/khamis1992/mission-control/commit/3bd462c1cbea9992eb5fabebe4e729a78a228a2a","node_id":"C_kwDOR8sI2toAKDNiZDQ2MmMxY2JlYTk5OTJlYjVmYWJlYmU0ZTcyOWE3OGEyMjhhMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/khamis1992/mission-control/commit/581fbf13db4a84463649b671dafee53dc52f91d6","sha":"581fbf13db4a84463649b671dafee53dc52f91d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/commits/581fbf13db4a84463649b671dafee53dc52f91d6"}],"sha":"3bd462c1cbea9992eb5fabebe4e729a78a228a2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/commits/3bd462c1cbea9992eb5fabebe4e729a78a228a2a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4118421?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Shipu","id":4118421,"login":"Shipu","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMTg0MjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shipu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/commits/581fbf13db4a84463649b671dafee53dc52f91d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-31T02:15:35Z","email":"shipuahamed01@gmail.com","name":"Shipu Ahamed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-31T02:15:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve OPENCLAW_HOME double-nesting and standalone server data loss on rebuild (#508)\n\n* fix: pass OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR explicitly in runOpenClaw to prevent double-nesting\n\nWhen OPENCLAW_HOME is set to the state directory directly (e.g. /root/.openclaw),\nthe OpenClaw CLI interprets it as a parent home directory and appends ''.openclaw'',\nresulting in a double-nested path like /root/.openclaw/.openclaw/credentials.\n\nFix: always inject OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR into the child process environment in\nrunOpenClaw() so the CLI uses the exact resolved path rather than deriving it\nfrom OPENCLAW_HOME.\n\nFixes: ''OAuth dir not present ($OPENCLAW_HOME/.openclaw/credentials)'' warning\nshown in Mission Control when OPENCLAW_HOME=/root/.openclaw is configured.\n\n* docs: clarify OPENCLAW_HOME vs OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR and data persistence\n\n- Add OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR and MISSION_CONTROL_DB_PATH to env tables in\n  README.md and docs/deployment.md\n- Document the OPENCLAW_HOME double-nesting bug and recommended workaround\n- Add configuration note explaining that MISSION_CONTROL_DB_PATH /\n  MISSION_CONTROL_DATA_DIR should use absolute paths when running the\n  Next.js standalone server to survive rebuilds\n\n* docs: simplify data config — MISSION_CONTROL_DATA_DIR is sufficient\n\nMISSION_CONTROL_DB_PATH defaults to DATA_DIR/mission-control.db, so\nsetting DATA_DIR alone is enough for most deployments. Only use\nMISSION_CONTROL_DB_PATH if the DB needs to live in a separate location.\n\nAlso removed it from the recommended .env example.\n\n* docs: remove MISSION_CONTROL_DB_PATH from all docs and examples\n\nMISSION_CONTROL_DATA_DIR is sufficient for all standard deployments.\nThe DB path is automatically derived as DATA_DIR/mission-control.db.\n\nRemoved MISSION_CONTROL_DB_PATH from:\n- README.md\n- docs/deployment.md\n- .env.example\n- SKILL.md\n- CLAUDE.md\n\nThe env var still works in code as an escape hatch for advanced use cases\n(e.g. DB on a separate volume), but it should not be documented as a\nrequired or recommended setting.","tree":{"sha":"bae668a4335085e23d1d7d63ee13c3154b9ca242","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/git/trees/bae668a4335085e23d1d7d63ee13c3154b9ca242"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/git/commits/581fbf13db4a84463649b671dafee53dc52f91d6","verification":{"payload":"tree bae668a4335085e23d1d7d63ee13c3154b9ca242\nparent 30ecc3d2a9b6733e4a99f185f5627d14c9b31bba\nauthor Shipu Ahamed <shipuahamed01@gmail.com> 1774923335 +0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774923335 +0700\n\nfix: resolve OPENCLAW_HOME double-nesting and standalone server data loss on rebuild (#508)\n\n* fix: pass OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR explicitly in runOpenClaw to prevent double-nesting\n\nWhen OPENCLAW_HOME is set to the state directory directly (e.g. /root/.openclaw),\nthe OpenClaw CLI interprets it as a parent home directory and appends ''.openclaw'',\nresulting in a double-nested path like /root/.openclaw/.openclaw/credentials.\n\nFix: always inject OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR into the child process environment in\nrunOpenClaw() so the CLI uses the exact resolved path rather than deriving it\nfrom OPENCLAW_HOME.\n\nFixes: ''OAuth dir not present ($OPENCLAW_HOME/.openclaw/credentials)'' warning\nshown in Mission Control when OPENCLAW_HOME=/root/.openclaw is configured.\n\n* docs: clarify OPENCLAW_HOME vs OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR and data persistence\n\n- Add OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR and MISSION_CONTROL_DB_PATH to env tables in\n  README.md and docs/deployment.md\n- Document the OPENCLAW_HOME double-nesting bug and recommended workaround\n- Add configuration note explaining that MISSION_CONTROL_DB_PATH /\n  MISSION_CONTROL_DATA_DIR should use absolute paths when running the\n  Next.js standalone server to survive rebuilds\n\n* docs: simplify data config — MISSION_CONTROL_DATA_DIR is sufficient\n\nMISSION_CONTROL_DB_PATH defaults to DATA_DIR/mission-control.db, so\nsetting DATA_DIR alone is enough for most deployments. Only use\nMISSION_CONTROL_DB_PATH if the DB needs to live in a separate location.\n\nAlso removed it from the recommended .env example.\n\n* docs: remove MISSION_CONTROL_DB_PATH from all docs and examples\n\nMISSION_CONTROL_DATA_DIR is sufficient for all standard deployments.\nThe DB path is automatically derived as DATA_DIR/mission-control.db.\n\nRemoved MISSION_CONTROL_DB_PATH from:\n- README.md\n- docs/deployment.md\n- .env.example\n- SKILL.md\n- CLAUDE.md\n\nThe env var still works in code as an escape hatch for advanced use cases\n(e.g. DB on a separate volume), but it should not be documented as a\nrequired or recommended setting.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpyy5HCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYK0QAGzPhXG9vheHe9UmZQo75o0Z\nDrVuR7DYPBQfHFchHjzRfMTyTq5LhDkGeZ5ny2cvaxfOYVo5Pcv631Ic1klRXH9l\nHBjyXbBHGkjvP1t+A/xbHgSRWW1PxN/8b0qep8Xa3VVs2jW1LaG5y+j4h3HtCcMO\nCE9dXPTH4cf+F+u6uS4q2mPcZY2qWURwoQvY6776dseldtBbH+ddmSrJUOLplAnl\n1yXfeHDabGiIuzxkpz495XPnq6ARSFR2ibcdVNSAt9OjInHHOIlYZV2oTj5UEzB1\n0uTrb1nC+owhsxPrL1ZXnFDIOsFzgRVi5BcUsBQSE/aAqZJSwzGfln/prXkZTpYK\nVwnJ846IYVJwlDMxwDWo7Glh+AChIWmob+A47R3NAWgPiPGHpfEDU7V2PyFZziN6\n2egJcbU64G7YUUNHE5Xa7A9HqTRNT9yV3sv3jJykQX8ZMepkpJfT+mcf1BJsg4DT\n87hBJS0LgJMphdMFw7vJWCEoNf3Ufmcruyjl6Js2mBhdwJtnHjk9uRCJjX2lCA0p\no13uOOD2OD2Ge14J8tVcIh2Siz1I1iLdcX/XFujdkVlUKqTMpgyUyKPbomrLj/Sx\nrJrbVlmKh4bx/zSApOQd0fkImoprFl3fZ0/6oO4Uu/pC7tWujnuf6bMEalSYHnRL\nqCbo0o5qja03H1mE+a0q\n=sQHk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-08T03:58:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url