g2NzVhMWNiODljNDIzODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/khamis1992/mission-control/commit/21345190c840d081abb46b437162e516843a2709","sha":"21345190c840d081abb46b437162e516843a2709","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/commits/21345190c840d081abb46b437162e516843a2709"}],"sha":"7ba1e7765779d8e1e7724df68675a1cb89c42380","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/commits/7ba1e7765779d8e1e7724df68675a1cb89c42380"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200090596?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copp1723/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copp1723/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copp1723/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copp1723/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/copp1723","id":200090596,"login":"copp1723","node_id":"U_kgDOC-0j5A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copp1723/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copp1723/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copp1723/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copp1723/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copp1723/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/copp1723","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/commits/21345190c840d081abb46b437162e516843a2709/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-23T07:59:48Z","email":"200090596+copp1723@users.noreply.github.com","name":"copp1723"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-23T07:59:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Twin chat workspace for Mission Control (#483)\n\n* feat: build Mission Control command console Phase 1\n\nMajor changes:\n- Remove all HERMES integrations (hermes-*.ts, /api/hermes/*, hermes-logo.png)\n- Add dispatch-form.tsx: hero component for operation dispatch\n- Add JARVIS integrations: /api/jarvis/{agents,schedule,review-queue}\n- Add callback-payload.ts: parser for agent callback rendering\n- Add command-console-wireframe.html: design specs and layout\n\nThe dispatch form wires to:\n  - GET /api/jarvis/agents: live Twin registry\n  - POST /api/jarvis/schedule: natural language schedule parsing\n  - Agent webhook_url: direct webhook dispatch\n\nReview queue renders agent callback payloads (answer, files, task URLs) with\napprove/redirect buttons. Ambient sidebar shows agent heartbeats, upcoming\nschedules, activity feed.\n\nThis is the operator console for a single-person fleet orchestration system.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: Phase 1  strip dark themes, fix color tokens, warm palettefoundation\n\n- Rewrite themes.ts: single ''Operator''s Desk'' light theme, remove 9 dark themes\n- Rewrite globals.css: remove ~370 lines of dark theme overrides, void/neon/glow utilities\n60\n- Replace destructive with warm terracotta instead of red\n- Add CSS custom properties for agent status dots (sage/amber/kraft)\n- Update button.tsx: destructive/success variants use semantic tokens\n- Update agent-squad-panel: all status colors use semantic tokens (no red/green)\n- Restyle dispatch-form.tsx from dark theme to Operator''s Desk\n- Simplify theme-selector to no-op stub (single theme, no toggle)\n- Simplify theme-background to just remove dark class\n\n* Phase 2: Replace NavRail+HeaderBar+LiveFeed with OpsStrip+BridgePage+LabPage two-tab shell\n\n- New OpsStrip header: 4 metrics (agents, tasks, review, gateway), Bridge/Lab tab switcher, clock, Cmd+K search, notifications\n- BridgePage: agent player card grid with status dots, task stats, detail overlay; ambient sidebar with activity, sessions, connection\n- LabPage: dispatch form hero, review queue, schedules table, operations log\n LabPage\n var() in tailwind.config.js for OKLCH token compatibility\n- Added void-* CSS variable fallbacks for backward compat\n- Added glow-cyan and command-palette-in utility classes\n- Removed NavRail, HeaderBar, LiveFeed from shell (components preserved for reference)\n\n* Phase 4: Add keyboard shortcuts (Cmd+Enter dispatch, 1/2 tab switch, Cmd+K search)\n\n- Dispatch form: Cmd/Ctrl+Enter submits, placeholder updated with hint\n- OpsStrip: 1 = Bridge, 2 = Lab when not typing in input\n- Refactored switchView to useCallback for proper dependency tracking\n\n* fix: remove tailwindcss-animate plugin (not installed)\n\n* fix: replace text-foreground/80 with text-muted-foreground (Tailwind v3 compat)\n\n* feat: add Chat button + keyboard shortcut (3) to OpsStrip\n\n- Chat icon button between search and notifications in the right section\n- Press 3 (when not typing) to jump to Chat\n- ChatIcon SVG component added\n\n* feat: operator intelligence  briefing-first agent cards, identity map, intent-based navigation, meaningful empty statesredesign\n\nBridge Page:\n- Agent cards now answer 3 questions: What''s your job? What did you do? What can I do?\n ''Codebase Intelligence'')\n- Cards sorted by relevance: active agents first, stale/no-runs to bench section\n- 4px ambient health dot replaces online/offline as primary status\n- Stale visual cue: accent border dims if last action >24h\n- Capability tags visible on every card\n- Quick action buttons route to chat/lab per agent\n- Schedules table as first-class section\n- Briefing sidebar: ''Needs Your Attention'', ''Next Up'', ''What Happened''\n\nLab Page:\n- Meaningful empty state with 3-step onboarding guidance\n- Operational language throughout (''dispatch an instruction'', ''needs your sign-off'')\n- Sections only appear when they have data\n\nOpsStrip:\n- ''need review'' metric is clickable and routes to Lab\n- Intent-based tooltips on tabs\n- Quick Jump chips in command palette\n\nNew file: src/lib/agent-identity.ts\n- Maps every known agent slug to role title, one-liner, capabilities, quick action\n- Graceful fallback for unknown agents\n- isAgentStale() and getFreshnessLabel() utilities\n\n* feat: fleet tiers (primary/devtools/operator/hidden), identity map for all agents, dispatch form uses store agents with grouped dropdown\n\n* feat: add Perplexity Computer static card + full operation schedule table\n\n- Add Perplexity Computer to agent identity map as ''external'' tier\n- Add PerplexityComputerCard component with schedule, capabilities, external link\n- Add OPERATION_SCHEDULES with 10 static entries covering the full operation surface:\n  Perplexity Computer (morning/afternoon), Engineering Summary, jarvisv2 crons,\n  Airweave sync, Granola, OpenClaw\n- Expand schedules table to 5 columns: When, Days, What, Agent, Source\n- Add OperationScheduleRow component with color-coded source badges\n- Handle external links in quick action buttons across all card types\n- Add ''external'' fleet tier for platforms without live heartbeat data\n\n* feat: Lucide icons replace emoji, last_summary bullets on agent cards\n\n- Replace all emoji icon strings with Lucide icon name references in agent-identity.ts\n- Add AgentIcon component with ICON_MAP lookup in bridge-page.tsx\n- Fix unicode escape rendering bug in PerplexityComputerCard (Clock icon)\n- Render config.last_summary bullets on agent cards (up to 3 on card, full in overlay)\n- Render config.last_run_at timestamp on agent cards\n- Also check config.card_summary as alias for last_summary\n- AgentDetailOverlay shows full summary list under ''Last Report'' section\n\n* feat: full 13-entry operation  4 OpenClaw autonomous loops addedschedule\n\nSchedule now includes:\n- 7:15 AM CT  Morning brief + Gmail drafts (Perplexity Computer)\n- 9:00 AM CT  Stale commitment watchdog (OpenClaw)\n- 11:30 AM CT Ali engineering sync prep (OpenClaw)\n- 2:00 PM CT  Afternoon email scan + drafts (Perplexity Computer)\n- 5:30 PM CT  Daily engineering summary (Engineering Summary)\n- 6:00 PM CT  End-of-day wrap (OpenClaw)\n- Every 15 min Pre-meeting intelligence brief (OpenClaw)\n- Every 30 min OpenClaw heartbeat\n- Every 5 min  Airweave ClickUp + GitHub sync\n- Every 15 min Email intelligence sync (jarvisv2)\n- Every 1 min  Due actions executor (jarvisv2)\n- On webhook   Zoom -> meeting notes -> ClickUp (jarvisv2 + Twin)\n- During meetings Live meeting transcription (Granola)\n\n* chore: add lucide-react dependency for Operator''s Desk icons\n\n* feat: add Intelligence Council morning + evening sessions to schedule (15 entries)\n\n- 9:00 AM CT Mon-Fri: Intelligence  morning session (OpenClaw)Council\n- 5:00 PM CT Mon-Fri: Intelligence  evening session (OpenClaw)Council\n\n* feat: OpenClaw panel + conversation thread + 6-fix brief\n\nOpenClaw Integration panel (Bridge > Lab > OpenClaw tab):\n- Cron Jobs: list with Run Now / Delete buttons\n- Skills: list with Enable/Disable toggles\n- Memory: read-only workspace file browser\n- Gateway: connection status + reconnect\n\nConversation thread in Lab (replaces Operations Log):\n- Dispatches render as right-aligned terracotta bubbles\n- Agent replies render left with avatar, handle, timestamp\n- cardSummary bullets + expandable full answer\n- Inline Approve/Redirect buttons on reviewable items\n- Auto-polls review-queue every 15s\n\n6-fix brief:\n ClickUp Orchestrator rename\n2. Static Twin agents always appear in dispatch picker\n3. Inline dispatch feedback with 10s auto-clear\n4. Review queue empty state copy\n5. (ops log replaced by conversation thread)\n6. Server-side schedule parse preview with debounce\n\nNavigation:\n- Bridge | Lab | OpenClaw 3-tab switcher\n- Keyboard shortcuts: 1=Bridge, 2=Lab, 3=OpenClaw, 4=Chat\n- Quick Jump updated in command palette\n\n* chore: ignore runtime logs\n\n* fix: remove all Hermes references, add boot data loading for activities + tasks, enhance agent cards with activity fallback\n\n- Remove Hermes from: loader, session-kind-brand, conversation-list, chat-workspace,\n  dashboard, widget-primitives, metric-cards-widget, runtime-health-widget,\n  session-workbench-widget, settings-panel, task-board-panel, memory-browser-panel\n- Add initial fetch for /api/activities (200 items) and /api/tasks (100 items) on boot\n  so event history and conversation thread persist across page refreshes\n- Agent cards now fall back to activities store when no last_summary/last_activity exists\n  (matches by agent name in actor or description fields)\n\n* feat: shape Twin chat workspace for Mission Control\n\n* test: align themes tests with single-light Operator''s Desk model\n\n* fix: restore hermes API compatibility routes for existing clients\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Josh Copp <josh@onekeel.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Nyk <0xnykcd@googlemail.com>","tree":{"sha":"99b16aab43016cd320faf6fc4188890afebe7b82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/git/trees/99b16aab43016cd320faf6fc4188890afebe7b82"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/git/commits/21345190c840d081abb46b437162e516843a2709","verification":{"payload":"tree 99b16aab43016cd320faf6fc4188890afebe7b82\nparent 0f82e23c2e26fe9756625e0d22790e5e899bd1ce\nauthor copp1723 <200090596+copp1723@users.noreply.github.com> 1774252788 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774252788 +0700\n\nfeat: Twin chat workspace for Mission Control (#483)\n\n* feat: build Mission Control command console Phase 1\n\nMajor changes:\n- Remove all HERMES integrations (hermes-*.ts, /api/hermes/*, hermes-logo.png)\n- Add dispatch-form.tsx: hero component for operation dispatch\n- Add JARVIS integrations: /api/jarvis/{agents,schedule,review-queue}\n- Add callback-payload.ts: parser for agent callback rendering\n- Add command-console-wireframe.html: design specs and layout\n\nThe dispatch form wires to:\n  - GET /api/jarvis/agents: live Twin registry\n  - POST /api/jarvis/schedule: natural language schedule parsing\n  - Agent webhook_url: direct webhook dispatch\n\nReview queue renders agent callback payloads (answer, files, task URLs) with\napprove/redirect buttons. Ambient sidebar shows agent heartbeats, upcoming\nschedules, activity feed.\n\nThis is the operator console for a single-person fleet orchestration system.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: Phase 1  strip dark themes, fix color tokens, warm palettefoundation\n\n- Rewrite themes.ts: single ''Operator''s Desk'' light theme, remove 9 dark themes\n- Rewrite globals.css: remove ~370 lines of dark theme overrides, void/neon/glow utilities\n60\n- Replace destructive with warm terracotta instead of red\n- Add CSS custom properties for agent status dots (sage/amber/kraft)\n- Update button.tsx: destructive/success variants use semantic tokens\n- Update agent-squad-panel: all status colors use semantic tokens (no red/green)\n- Restyle dispatch-form.tsx from dark theme to Operator''s Desk\n- Simplify theme-selector to no-op stub (single theme, no toggle)\n- Simplify theme-background to just remove dark class\n\n* Phase 2: Replace NavRail+HeaderBar+LiveFeed with OpsStrip+BridgePage+LabPage two-tab shell\n\n- New OpsStrip header: 4 metrics (agents, tasks, review, gateway), Bridge/Lab tab switcher, clock, Cmd+K search, notifications\n- BridgePage: agent player card grid with status dots, task stats, detail overlay; ambient sidebar with activity, sessions, connection\n- LabPage: dispatch form hero, review queue, schedules table, operations log\n LabPage\n var() in tailwind.config.js for OKLCH token compatibility\n- Added void-* CSS variable fallbacks for backward compat\n- Added glow-cyan and command-palette-in utility classes\n- Removed NavRail, HeaderBar, LiveFeed from shell (components preserved for reference)\n\n* Phase 4: Add keyboard shortcuts (Cmd+Enter dispatch, 1/2 tab switch, Cmd+K search)\n\n- Dispatch form: Cmd/Ctrl+Enter submits, placeholder updated with hint\n- OpsStrip: 1 = Bridge, 2 = Lab when not typing in input\n- Refactored switchView to useCallback for proper dependency tracking\n\n* fix: remove tailwindcss-animate plugin (not installed)\n\n* fix: replace text-foreground/80 with text-muted-foreground (Tailwind v3 compat)\n\n* feat: add Chat button + keyboard shortcut (3) to OpsStrip\n\n- Chat icon button between search and notifications in the right section\n- Press 3 (when not typing) to jump to Chat\n- ChatIcon SVG component added\n\n* feat: operator intelligence  briefing-first agent cards, identity map, intent-based navigation, meaningful empty statesredesign\n\nBridge Page:\n- Agent cards now answer 3 questions: What''s your job? What did you do? What can I do?\n ''Codebase Intelligence'')\n- Cards sorted by relevance: active agents first, stale/no-runs to bench section\n- 4px ambient health dot replaces online/offline as primary status\n- Stale visual cue: accent border dims if last action >24h\n- Capability tags visible on every card\n- Quick action buttons route to chat/lab per agent\n- Schedules table as first-class section\n- Briefing sidebar: ''Needs Your Attention'', ''Next Up'', ''What Happened''\n\nLab Page:\n- Meaningful empty state with 3-step onboarding guidance\n- Operational language throughout (''dispatch an instruction'', ''needs your sign-off'')\n- Sections only appear when they have data\n\nOpsStrip:\n- ''need review'' metric is clickable and routes to Lab\n- Intent-based tooltips on tabs\n- Quick Jump chips in command palette\n\nNew file: src/lib/agent-identity.ts\n- Maps every known agent slug to role title, one-liner, capabilities, quick action\n- Graceful fallback for unknown agents\n- isAgentStale() and getFreshnessLabel() utilities\n\n* feat: fleet tiers (primary/devtools/operator/hidden), identity map for all agents, dispatch form uses store agents with grouped dropdown\n\n* feat: add Perplexity Computer static card + full operation schedule table\n\n- Add Perplexity Computer to agent identity map as ''external'' tier\n- Add PerplexityComputerCard component with schedule, capabilities, external link\n- Add OPERATION_SCHEDULES with 10 static entries covering the full operation surface:\n  Perplexity Computer (morning/afternoon), Engineering Summary, jarvisv2 crons,\n  Airweave sync, Granola, OpenClaw\n- Expand schedules table to 5 columns: When, Days, What, Agent, Source\n- Add OperationScheduleRow component with color-coded source badges\n- Handle external links in quick action buttons across all card types\n- Add ''external'' fleet tier for platforms without live heartbeat data\n\n* feat: Lucide icons replace emoji, last_summary bullets on agent cards\n\n- Replace all emoji icon strings with Lucide icon name references in agent-identity.ts\n- Add AgentIcon component with ICON_MAP lookup in bridge-page.tsx\n- Fix unicode escape rendering bug in PerplexityComputerCard (Clock icon)\n- Render config.last_summary bullets on agent cards (up to 3 on card, full in overlay)\n- Render config.last_run_at timestamp on agent cards\n- Also check config.card_summary as alias for last_summary\n- AgentDetailOverlay shows full summary list under ''Last Report'' section\n\n* feat: full 13-entry operation  4 OpenClaw autonomous loops addedschedule\n\nSchedule now includes:\n- 7:15 AM CT  Morning brief + Gmail drafts (Perplexity Computer)\n- 9:00 AM CT  Stale commitment watchdog (OpenClaw)\n- 11:30 AM CT Ali engineering sync prep (OpenClaw)\n- 2:00 PM CT  Afternoon email scan + drafts (Perplexity Computer)\n- 5:30 PM CT  Daily engineering summary (Engineering Summary)\n- 6:00 PM CT  End-of-day wrap (OpenClaw)\n- Every 15 min Pre-meeting intelligence brief (OpenClaw)\n- Every 30 min OpenClaw heartbeat\n- Every 5 min  Airweave ClickUp + GitHub sync\n- Every 15 min Email intelligence sync (jarvisv2)\n- Every 1 min  Due actions executor (jarvisv2)\n- On webhook   Zoom -> meeting notes -> ClickUp (jarvisv2 + Twin)\n- During meetings Live meeting transcription (Granola)\n\n* chore: add lucide-react dependency for Operator''s Desk icons\n\n* feat: add Intelligence Council morning + evening sessions to schedule (15 entries)\n\n- 9:00 AM CT Mon-Fri: Intelligence  morning session (OpenClaw)Council\n- 5:00 PM CT Mon-Fri: Intelligence  evening session (OpenClaw)Council\n\n* feat: OpenClaw panel + conversation thread + 6-fix brief\n\nOpenClaw Integration panel (Bridge > Lab > OpenClaw tab):\n- Cron Jobs: list with Run Now / Delete buttons\n- Skills: list with Enable/Disable toggles\n- Memory: read-only workspace file browser\n- Gateway: connection status + reconnect\n\nConversation thread in Lab (replaces Operations Log):\n- Dispatches render as right-aligned terracotta bubbles\n- Agent replies render left with avatar, handle, timestamp\n- cardSummary bullets + expandable full answer\n- Inline Approve/Redirect buttons on reviewable items\n- Auto-polls review-queue every 15s\n\n6-fix brief:\n ClickUp Orchestrator rename\n2. Static Twin agents always appear in dispatch picker\n3. Inline dispatch feedback with 10s auto-clear\n4. Review queue empty state copy\n5. (ops log replaced by conversation thread)\n6. Server-side schedule parse preview with debounce\n\nNavigation:\n- Bridge | Lab | OpenClaw 3-tab switcher\n- Keyboard shortcuts: 1=Bridge, 2=Lab, 3=OpenClaw, 4=Chat\n- Quick Jump updated in command palette\n\n* chore: ignore runtime logs\n\n* fix: remove all Hermes references, add boot data loading for activities + tasks, enhance agent cards with activity fallback\n\n- Remove Hermes from: loader, session-kind-brand, conversation-list, chat-workspace,\n  dashboard, widget-primitives, metric-cards-widget, runtime-health-widget,\n  session-workbench-widget, settings-panel, task-board-panel, memory-browser-panel\n- Add initial fetch for /api/activities (200 items) and /api/tasks (100 items) on boot\n  so event history and conversation thread persist across page refreshes\n- Agent cards now fall back to activities store when no last_summary/last_activity exists\n  (matches by agent name in actor or description fields)\n\n* feat: shape Twin chat workspace for Mission Control\n\n* test: align themes tests with single-light Operator''s Desk model\n\n* fix: restore hermes API compatibility routes for existing clients\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Josh Copp <josh@onekeel.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Nyk <0xnykcd@googlemail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpwPL0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdFUQAE2hzikBHgWuoX3wz/dMLAlR\nCudLpb40MywDFiFjlujZruOg2NDQOIy9jCStugmha6QsSJyq9GTrN0ecF1ernU+9\nGeLZFRmwgBpbHhCJ6lf5u9B6CjKgt7uZakULx+1IgQ/vVCap1gd+y+UiCno5IDQN\nKpgOYwZBNwLPNCyZ+q7dLxZv/cml2diGQPilh+ZCqW7wZapYrwfFXf5ButtD2YBD\nEXRvVhc3MCQ79SLcjpbdiaVufIC9jcNgEZo/AoBZewhIgGEWN2G98MaqNGFEREI3\nDDGXIp2Uqjuhbb94mYqtZjuNgWS9tB8/3lDEyFGkuOk44OW6xKQ/YeranDvWe8lo\nJsyuUQ5MMs6FFsk14lUrv9W61A7I9zC5LSsblFOD1IrPQWGzFByvwpBQTFS5Pgyv\nwBTQ/TKUNnGiPo9tG9cSYSQrdbFxYFVtD6qep9E7ET3fFONjR/G+PY76VrloIoLo\noDoJ/KElRLgdzkxMVVoMpSaG4Hwprt0xllJ3OVxdGV1xcimKhYV3tV8kT8EbRPEL\nr9yiB4FKV/U0vYfbucTiUdMpCV7BwzBBy25i/9qmaZjCnghMPx82HjTroQ7BgZqD\nV/HEVN+47J9aQ4RrAb6LsuTuMqOndTJvdqN3k/ukJquNMyDldODggAd3lx8LxM5f\nbpt05O1mjm3aMlV54Pwn\n=VW4m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-08T03:58:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/khamis1992/mission-control/commit/21345190c840d081abb46b437162e516843a2709","node_id":"C_kwDOR8sI2toAKDIxMzQ1MTkwYzg0MGQwODFhYmI0NmI0MzcxNjJlNTE2ODQzYTI3MDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/khamis1992/mission-control/commit/0f82e23c2e26fe9756625e0d22790e5e899bd1ce","sha":"0f82e23c2e26fe9756625e0d22790e5e899bd1ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/commits/0f82e23c2e26fe9756625e0d22790e5e899bd1ce"}],"sha":"21345190c840d081abb46b437162e516843a2709","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/commits/21345190c840d081abb46b437162e516843a2709"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204787723?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomaswillner/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomaswillner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomaswillner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomaswillner/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thomaswillner","id":204787723,"login":"thomaswillner","node_id":"U_kgDODDTQCw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomaswillner/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomaswillner/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomaswillner/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomaswillner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomaswillner/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomaswillner","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/commits/0f82e23c2e26fe9756625e0d22790e5e899bd1ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-23T06:21:09Z","email":"thomas.willner@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Willner"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-23T06:21:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gateway): use /health instead of /api/health for health probes (#481)\n\nThe gateway health probe in `buildGatewayProbeUrl()` hardcodes `/api/health`\nas the probe endpoint, but the OpenClaw gateway serves its health check on\n`/health`. This causes the server-side health probe to always return HTTP 404,\nmarking gateways as offline/error even when they are healthy and responsive.\n\nChanged the probe endpoint from `/api/health` to `/health` in:\n- `src/app/api/gateways/health/route.ts` (buildGatewayProbeUrl)\n- `src/app/api/channels/route.ts` (isGatewayReachable)\n\nCo-authored-by: Thomas Willner <B0tmaster@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0655a4465857073101dffab12809d51a567ac3d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/git/trees/0655a4465857073101dffab12809d51a567ac3d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khamis1992/mission-control/git/commits/0f82e23c2e26fe9756625e0d22790e5e899bd1ce","verification":{"payload":"tree 0655a4465857073101dffab12809d51a567ac3d2\nparent f3192a93016b77369f03fd23f8f1e37433e06a63\nauthor Thomas Willner <thomas.willner@gmail.com> 1774246869 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774246869 +0700\n\nfix(gateway): use /health instead of /api/health for health probes (#481)\n\nThe gateway health probe in `buildGatewayProbeUrl()` hardcodes `/api/health`\nas the probe endpoint, but the OpenClaw gateway serves its health check on\n`/health`. This causes the server-side health probe to always return HTTP 404,\nmarking gateways as offline/error even when they are healthy and responsive.\n\nChanged the probe endpoint from `/api/health` to `/health` in:\n- `src/app/api/gateways/health/route.ts` (buildGatewayProbeUrl)\n- `src/app/api/channels/route.ts` (isGatewayReachable)\n\nCo-authored-by: Thomas Willner <B0tmaster@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpwNvVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/ZkQABL6kAN6n3uYZiwhadftbMkZ\njTPacqYz34hI6bwjh+Q9uKtRw0sl1A1A8DWFiBeJ7sMADxr17c6ocS/6TYRZCkH+\nmmycpe2nshD5uCXdG/t0/kd4foWaKJeMFU9J+Uz8vxYjBjOT/4R68ko3lJxbv6ix\nnhodYFdtK4fUKT2SGWrClvbZLQlGTN9/otTO3XXRUzqmGOysN5kkHniZGmwYUjzl\nqhUoeLRcXNKIqlj343iXhRT1LSJFExFetNiXlvmidw4D9qMSAhNysA6i6jwKlFqC\ni5o4Du0TEIKlKFDkhUeABPLykTom25VmgalHddSyX8TzC1xiq4POl6iBIIE1S+HN\nxShO0Y3/lSJkHfP2VEDyMo2Mqk54y02ykMYnWtIVywi4X0Y59vwVbR1Hw1SIjlry\nlJbFhir+LISeUDsA10nAE+vWeDQ91HXYTECfg8AEPGR4DQH9wntV7xfgG4SB8VLm\nQjSdacwBPZuKfct/wGepZQGGVbMRbOePkHmsJWNTXmX+yKpi5dSu5zwByHic0sry\nqQnidYRtF0bOcigdcFi2GcXPqvKMUYLHO4S+uqqssc9bhAR5cR2R1/GtXVM4nQAD\nHkM0z/UI/DQvWFhzq4cypzBHc6UDJMmUuoQaFCm3vxooS/vah/e1QsObUIiIVGCI\n4hCufIE7M6N3V8jBmCfl\n=mR+d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-08T03:58:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github