hub.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/52198e28a5d74af5c85f39d255667cb7a05c397b","sha":"52198e28a5d74af5c85f39d255667cb7a05c397b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/52198e28a5d74af5c85f39d255667cb7a05c397b"}],"sha":"b66ccd61cc3ad4dbc456f4f28d44748e3dbd9efe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/b66ccd61cc3ad4dbc456f4f28d44748e3dbd9efe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/52198e28a5d74af5c85f39d255667cb7a05c397b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T21:15:11Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T21:15:11Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix: give back the console permit when the plugin is already stopping\n\nWriting tests for the relay''s untested paths turned one up. The console\nhandler checks twice whether there is still anything to relay to: once\nbefore Portainer is contacted at all, and once after the exec socket and\nthe upstream handshake have been awaited. The second check releases the\nstream permit and removes the session; the first only closed the browser\nsocket and returned, despite the comment above it claiming the session is\nremoved on every path that does not reach the relay.\n\nNothing else gives them back on that path. The permit is otherwise\nreleased by the relay''s onEnd, and no relay is ever created — so each\ntime this fires a console slot is gone for the lifetime of the plugin,\nand with the default ceiling three of them is a console that refuses\nevery attempt until Signal K restarts.\n\nThe tests that found it came from the coverage gap in the two files that\ncarry the console: execrelay.ts was at 71% of statements and 61% of\nbranches, console.ts at 79% and 68%, and the uncovered lines were the\nplaces a relay actually misbehaves rather than the happy path. Now\ncovered, each verified by removing the guard it rests on:\n\n- a single message past the megabyte cap, which arrives before\n  bufferedAmount has anything to say about it\n- a receiver already past the hard limit, where pausing cannot recover\n- the drain loop pausing, holding while the queue is above the low mark,\n  and resuming once it is not\n- a paused receiver whose queue grows anyway, which means gone not slow\n- the heartbeat pinging both ends, tolerating an answer, and terminating\n  a half-open socket that answers nothing for two rounds\n- Portainer closing with a code of its own, which is not the shell\n  exiting and should not be reported as though it were\n- a socket that fails the upgrade outright rather than stalling, where\n  the permit and session have to come back as they do on the timeout\n- binary keystrokes held before the shell exists, in each shape ws\n  delivers one: bytes, an ArrayBuffer, and the pieces of a fragmented\n  message\n\nexecrelay.ts and console.ts are both at 100% of lines; the suite is 1107\ntests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd","tree":{"sha":"ced2f59c05489aceb203b06619a31a8a544d47b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/ced2f59c05489aceb203b06619a31a8a544d47b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/52198e28a5d74af5c85f39d255667cb7a05c397b","verification":{"payload":"tree ced2f59c05489aceb203b06619a31a8a544d47b5\nparent 9bf8b15fc63c792fea9afa842a5f537bb7a234ed\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789247711 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789247711 +0000\n\nfix: give back the console permit when the plugin is already stopping\n\nWriting tests for the relay''s untested paths turned one up. The console\nhandler checks twice whether there is still anything to relay to: once\nbefore Portainer is contacted at all, and once after the exec socket and\nthe upstream handshake have been awaited. The second check releases the\nstream permit and removes the session; the first only closed the browser\nsocket and returned, despite the comment above it claiming the session is\nremoved on every path that does not reach the relay.\n\nNothing else gives them back on that path. The permit is otherwise\nreleased by the relay''s onEnd, and no relay is ever created — so each\ntime this fires a console slot is gone for the lifetime of the plugin,\nand with the default ceiling three of them is a console that refuses\nevery attempt until Signal K restarts.\n\nThe tests that found it came from the coverage gap in the two files that\ncarry the console: execrelay.ts was at 71% of statements and 61% of\nbranches, console.ts at 79% and 68%, and the uncovered lines were the\nplaces a relay actually misbehaves rather than the happy path. Now\ncovered, each verified by removing the guard it rests on:\n\n- a single message past the megabyte cap, which arrives before\n  bufferedAmount has anything to say about it\n- a receiver already past the hard limit, where pausing cannot recover\n- the drain loop pausing, holding while the queue is above the low mark,\n  and resuming once it is not\n- a paused receiver whose queue grows anyway, which means gone not slow\n- the heartbeat pinging both ends, tolerating an answer, and terminating\n  a half-open socket that answers nothing for two rounds\n- Portainer closing with a code of its own, which is not the shell\n  exiting and should not be reported as though it were\n- a socket that fails the upgrade outright rather than stalling, where\n  the permit and session have to come back as they do on the timeout\n- binary keystrokes held before the shell exists, in each shape ws\n  delivers one: bytes, an ArrayBuffer, and the pieces of a fragmented\n  message\n\nexecrelay.ts and console.ts are both at 100% of lines; the suite is 1107\ntests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKIo3Vrg\nyPHCgVw1ifa739UeZl0Qoxx+aDMSWlzln0KHHqwl7MdVN+UE2NjNIEsJxexcXmTmi87JR/QC53G1\nUwE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T21:15:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/52198e28a5d74af5c85f39d255667cb7a05c397b","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDUyMTk4ZTI4YTVkNzRhZjVjODVmMzlkMjU1NjY3Y2I3YTA1YzM5N2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/9bf8b15fc63c792fea9afa842a5f537bb7a234ed","sha":"9bf8b15fc63c792fea9afa842a5f537bb7a234ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/9bf8b15fc63c792fea9afa842a5f537bb7a234ed"}],"sha":"52198e28a5d74af5c85f39d255667cb7a05c397b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/52198e28a5d74af5c85f39d255667cb7a05c397b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/9bf8b15fc63c792fea9afa842a5f537bb7a234ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T21:09:15Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T21:09:15Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"chore: clear the qs advisories and refresh what the ranges already allow\n\nbody-parser 1.20.6 carried a qs with two moderate advisories — an\narray-limit bypass through bracket-key comma parsing, and a denial of\nservice through an attacker-controlled isBuffer. The plugin parses\nrequest bodies from the admin UI, so that sits on a live path rather\nthan in the test tooling.\n\nLockfile only: every version here was already permitted by package.json,\nso this is body-parser to 1.20.8 and qs to 6.16.0, with react, webpack,\ntypescript-eslint and the rest moving to the latest their ranges allow.\nnpm audit reports nothing outstanding.\n\nLeft alone deliberately, each for a reason rather than an oversight:\n\nexpress 4 to 5 and body-parser 1 to 2, because signalk-server itself\ndepends on express ^4.22.2 and body-parser ^1.20.5 and hands this plugin\nthe router it registers on. Testing against express 5 would exercise a\nrouter the plugin will never run on, which is less fidelity, not more.\n\ntypescript 5.9 to 7, because ts-jest requires typescript >=4.3 <7 and\ntypescript-eslint requires >=4.8.4 <6.1.0. It would take the test runner\nand the linter down with it.\n\nundici 7 to 8, because 8 requires Node >=22.19.0 while this plugin\nsupports >=22.0.0. There is no advisory against 7.29.1 and nothing here\nneeds an 8 feature, so the only effect would be raising the floor under\nboats already running an older 22.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd","tree":{"sha":"ca8bd9de95e3b43f35077561a3dd9249d6011224","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/ca8bd9de95e3b43f35077561a3dd9249d6011224"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/9bf8b15fc63c792fea9afa842a5f537bb7a234ed","verification":{"payload":"tree ca8bd9de95e3b43f35077561a3dd9249d6011224\nparent 49eb5ea01807cc588f1d5fa5ccbfcd12e4c3d47f\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789247355 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789247355 +0000\n\nchore: clear the qs advisories and refresh what the ranges already allow\n\nbody-parser 1.20.6 carried a qs with two moderate advisories — an\narray-limit bypass through bracket-key comma parsing, and a denial of\nservice through an attacker-controlled isBuffer. The plugin parses\nrequest bodies from the admin UI, so that sits on a live path rather\nthan in the test tooling.\n\nLockfile only: every version here was already permitted by package.json,\nso this is body-parser to 1.20.8 and qs to 6.16.0, with react, webpack,\ntypescript-eslint and the rest moving to the latest their ranges allow.\nnpm audit reports nothing outstanding.\n\nLeft alone deliberately, each for a reason rather than an oversight:\n\nexpress 4 to 5 and body-parser 1 to 2, because signalk-server itself\ndepends on express ^4.22.2 and body-parser ^1.20.5 and hands this plugin\nthe router it registers on. Testing against express 5 would exercise a\nrouter the plugin will never run on, which is less fidelity, not more.\n\ntypescript 5.9 to 7, because ts-jest requires typescript >=4.3 <7 and\ntypescript-eslint requires >=4.8.4 <6.1.0. It would take the test runner\nand the linter down with it.\n\nundici 7 to 8, because 8 requires Node >=22.19.0 while this plugin\nsupports >=22.0.0. There is no advisory against 7.29.1 and nothing here\nneeds an 8 feature, so the only effect would be raising the floor under\nboats already running an older 22.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaG