"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"test: say what createMockAgent does now that it counts\n\nThe only function in this file without a comment, and no longer the\nobvious one: it installs the agent as the global dispatcher and also\nwraps registration so the count exists for expectAllConsumed to check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd","tree":{"sha":"1f465326142c64cdaeceff5b5e867e177cad589b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/1f465326142c64cdaeceff5b5e867e177cad589b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/ec2c53c93d727de77ae496733f18f731513ac625","verification":{"payload":"tree 1f465326142c64cdaeceff5b5e867e177cad589b\nparent b5951038efc1cf644da4fab9214824fde984bb8d\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789244656 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789244656 +0000\n\ntest: say what createMockAgent does now that it counts\n\nThe only function in this file without a comment, and no longer the\nobvious one: it installs the agent as the global dispatcher and also\nwraps registration so the count exists for expectAllConsumed to check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLw5NqW9\nqqXtg57RAop2YVa7aN36SWp81elaB+x2Rh7CPPrd0E8UDXE+yaCSRUh56hVUwqwOj4BnCmvhTUW+\n4QA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T20:24:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/ec2c53c93d727de77ae496733f18f731513ac625","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGVjMmM1M2M5M2Q3MjdkZTc3YWU0OTY3MzNmMThmNzMxNTEzYWM2MjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/b5951038efc1cf644da4fab9214824fde984bb8d","sha":"b5951038efc1cf644da4fab9214824fde984bb8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/b5951038efc1cf644da4fab9214824fde984bb8d"}],"sha":"ec2c53c93d727de77ae496733f18f731513ac625","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/ec2c53c93d727de77ae496733f18f731513ac625"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/b5951038efc1cf644da4fab9214824fde984bb8d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T20:22:58Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T20:22:58Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"test: assert the reads that precede a refusal went unmade too\n\nBoth of these registered the environment lookup and said in their own\ncomments that it was there so the refusal could be asserted, then never\nasserted it. A guard that resolved the environment before refusing would\nconsume that interceptor and leave the mutation pending, and every one of\nthese tests would still have passed — the same gap this branch is about,\none level in.\n\nThe six container and image guards now assert the environment lookup is\nunconsumed as well, which pins the refusal as happening before Portainer\nis contacted at all rather than merely before the write. The stack create\ndoes the same for all three reads a create would start with, since the\nname is read before any of them.\n\nVerified by reordering the lifecycle route to resolve the environment\nahead of the control gate: the mutations stay pending and the new\nassertion is what fails.\n\nReported by CodeRabbit on #58.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd","tree":{"sha":"19f5bc428db800cae1f14ff2211ce04d9c3f8e72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/19f5bc428db800cae1f14ff2211ce04d9c3f8e72"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/b5951038efc1cf644da4fab9214824fde984bb8d","verification":{"payload":"tree 19f5bc428db800cae1f14ff2211ce04d9c3f8e72\nparent 01dc9d3a0d16b8489e0b73c0bb0fbab4d9c73cbe\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789244578 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789244578 +0000\n\ntest: assert the reads that precede a refusal went unmade too\n\nBoth of these registered the environment lookup and said in their own\ncomments that it was there so the refusal could be asserted, then never\nasserted it. A guard that resolved the environment before refusing would\nconsume that interceptor and leave the mutation pending, and every one of\nthese tests would still have passed — the same gap this branch is about,\none level in.\n\nThe six container and image guards now assert the environment lookup is\nunconsumed as well, which pins the refusal as happening before Portainer\nis contacted at all rather than merely before the write. The stack create\ndoes the same for all three reads a create would start with, since the\nname is read before any of them.\n\nVerified by reordering the lifecycle route to resolve the environment\nahead of the control gate: the mutations stay pending and the new\nassertion is what fails.\n\nReported by CodeRabbit on #58.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG1N0muG\nEW6SDw44Oui9ad4SnODxIX2CgwsfpfcxNKD9QDRxl0W6HGXVn7LmaC/vhJp0FM3AcAGAC5F8sSK8\nLQQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T20:23:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/b5951038efc1cf644da4fab9214824fde984bb8d","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGI1OTUxMDM4ZWZjMWNmNjQ0ZGE0ZmFiOTIxNDgyNGZkZTk4NGJiOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/01dc9d3a0d16b8489e0b73c0bb0fbab4d9c73cbe","sha":"01dc9d3a0d16b8489e0b73c0bb0fbab4d9c73cbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/01dc9d3a0d16b8489e0b73c0bb0fbab4d9c73cbe"}],"sha":"b5951038efc1cf644da4fab9214824fde984bb8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/b5951038efc1cf644da4fab9214824fde984bb8d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/01dc9d3a0d16b8489e0b73c0bb0fbab4d9c73cbe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:51:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:51:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"test: register the requests the facade guards must prevent\n\nThe same empty assertion as the stack routes, in the rest of the route\nand handler tests: a refusal that claimed \"nothing was asked of\nPortainer\" while registering no interceptor, so the pending set was\nempty whatever the guard did. Several of the comments said as much\noutright.\n\nEach now registers the upstream request the guard stands in front of —\nand, where the guard runs after the environment is resolved, that lookup\ntoo, so a guard that fired too late is caught by the lookup having been\nconsumed — and asserts each was left over. The Signal K self-protection\ntest asserts it once per action rather than once for the loop.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd","tree":{"sha":"46d924fafac6afc49aa275779e3eb993d4956299","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/46d924fafac6afc49aa275779e3eb993d4956299"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/01dc9d3a0d16b8489e0b73c0bb0fbab4d9c73cbe","verification":{"payload":"tree 46d924fafac6afc49aa275779e3eb993d4956299\nparent 01b37d4dead2c61a9c282a721cad60410412fa39\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789242665 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789242665 +0000\n\ntest: register the requests the facade guards must prevent\n\nThe same empty assertion as the stack routes, in the rest of the route\nand handler tests: a refusal that claimed \"nothing was asked of\nPortainer\" while registering no interceptor, so the pending set was\nempty whatever the guard did. Several of the comments said as much\noutright.\n\nEach now registers the upstream request the guard stands in front of —\nand, where the guard runs after the environment is resolved, that lookup\ntoo, so a guard that fired too late is caught by the lookup having been\nconsumed — and asserts each was left over. The Signal K self-protection\ntest asserts it once per action rather than once for the loop.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIrfU2Sc\nUriZKxisRxNnpgAbkF1Axc30wuhYJfE67vb0e5EJ7JDgLnejWiT2bw902l1oyAyAJXVIEOb7VwKU\n3w0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T19:51:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","typ