t: give the stack route refusals something to assert\n\nEvery one of these registered no interceptor at all, so the pending set\nwas empty however the guard behaved and the assertion beside the status\ncode said nothing. Each now registers the upstream write the guard is\nthere to prevent — read off the route and the client, query string and\nall — and asserts it was left over.\n\nThe unknown-action test moved from stack 3 to stack 5 for the same\nreason at one remove: an unknown action falls into the redeploy branch,\nand stack 3 has no repository, so a handler that stopped refusing would\nhave been caught by the git check instead and the new assertion would\nstill have held. Stack 5 is the git-backed fixture, so the refusal is\nthe only thing standing between the request and Portainer.\n\nThe remaining sites, which do register what they consume, now say\nexpectAllConsumed, which refuses a test that registered nothing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd","tree":{"sha":"7274ee5e38d29f87dbba562fddf30aa1281bad33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/7274ee5e38d29f87dbba562fddf30aa1281bad33"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/01b37d4dead2c61a9c282a721cad60410412fa39","verification":{"payload":"tree 7274ee5e38d29f87dbba562fddf30aa1281bad33\nparent 47d1b7be3c1236a272ed5b73d306578704500f77\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789242419 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789242419 +0000\n\ntest: give the stack route refusals something to assert\n\nEvery one of these registered no interceptor at all, so the pending set\nwas empty however the guard behaved and the assertion beside the status\ncode said nothing. Each now registers the upstream write the guard is\nthere to prevent — read off the route and the client, query string and\nall — and asserts it was left over.\n\nThe unknown-action test moved from stack 3 to stack 5 for the same\nreason at one remove: an unknown action falls into the redeploy branch,\nand stack 3 has no repository, so a handler that stopped refusing would\nhave been caught by the git check instead and the new assertion would\nstill have held. Stack 5 is the git-backed fixture, so the refusal is\nthe only thing standing between the request and Portainer.\n\nThe remaining sites, which do register what they consume, now say\nexpectAllConsumed, which refuses a test that registered nothing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOKmfjBK\nBtoQhpraUrdXr03N01fad7rjG6xJxznXrw5iR739UyeJd6tmu+dJ9LZoRUMmRtpboh/za+5NKpjz\nuQU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T19:47:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/01b37d4dead2c61a9c282a721cad60410412fa39","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDAxYjM3ZDRkZWFkMmM2MWE5YzI4MmE3MjFjYWQ2MDQxMDQxMmZhMzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/47d1b7be3c1236a272ed5b73d306578704500f77","sha":"47d1b7be3c1236a272ed5b73d306578704500f77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/47d1b7be3c1236a272ed5b73d306578704500f77"}],"sha":"01b37d4dead2c61a9c282a721cad60410412fa39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/01b37d4dead2c61a9c282a721cad60410412fa39"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/47d1b7be3c1236a272ed5b73d306578704500f77/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:43:50Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:43:50Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"test: make assertions that claimed nothing actually bite\n\nSeveral tests asserted that a request was never made by filtering the\nmock agent''s pending interceptors for its path and expecting nothing.\nThat passes when no interceptor for the path was ever registered, which\nwas the case everywhere it was used: the assertion held whether or not\nthe guard it was written to prove still worked. Two were found in the\nstale-cache fix, when an unrelated change disturbed them; these are the\nrest of that shape outside the route tests.\n\nThe refusals now register the write that must not happen, and the fresh\nstack read that must not be reached, and assert both were left over.\nRemoving the guard from the cached record fails all three on the new\nassertion rather than on a neighbouring one.\n\nTwo helpers replace the idiom so it cannot come back. expectAllConsumed\ncounts registrations, so it refuses a test that registered nothing;\nexpectNotRequested requires the path to be registered and still pending,\nso a renamed route fails rather than silently matching nothing. Both are\npinned in both directions by a test of their own.\n\nElsewhere: the console relay''s no-ticket refusal now sends a message\nbefore asserting the upstream saw none, the panel''s aborted-read test is\nasserted on a mounted tree instead of after unmount (where queryByRole\nreturns null however the panel behaved) and against a replacement read\nthat never answers, since a successful one clears the error first, and\nthe environment gate is asserted on what was requested rather than on\ntext that could not have appeared on that tab.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd","tree":{"sha":"54596baec0dc303a87ac76ce84606401db1a35c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/54596baec0dc303a87ac76ce84606401db1a35c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/47d1b7be3c1236a272ed5b73d306578704500f77","verification":{"payload":"tree 54596baec0dc303a87ac76ce84606401db1a35c6\nparent 2c9de494d487762662f8e7ad37eaa62f92371db1\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789242230 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789242230 +0000\n\ntest: make assertions that claimed nothing actually bite\n\nSeveral tests asserted that a request was never made by filtering the\nmock agent''s pending interceptors for its path and expecting nothing.\nThat passes when no interceptor for the path was ever registered, which\nwas the case everywhere it was used: the assertion held whether or not\nthe guard it was written to prove still worked. Two were found in the\nstale-cache fix, when an unrelated change disturbed them; these are the\nrest of that shape outside the route tests.\n\nThe refusals now register the write that must not happen, and the fresh\nstack read that must not be reached, and assert both were left over.\nRemoving the guard from the cached record fails all three on the new\nassertion rather than on a neighbouring one.\n\nTwo helpers replace the idiom so it cannot come back. expectAllConsumed\ncounts registrations, so it refuses a test that registered nothing;\nexpectNotRequested requires the path to be registered and still pending,\nso a renamed route fails rather than silently matching nothing. Both are\npinned in both directions by a test of their own.\n\nElsewhere: the console relay''s no-ticket refusal now sends a message\nbefore asserting the upstream saw none, the panel''s aborted-read test is\nasserted on a mounted tree instead of after unmount (where queryByRole\nreturns null however the panel behaved) and against a replacement read\nthat never answers, since a successful one clears the error first, and\nthe environment gate is asserted on what was requested rather than on\ntext that could not have appeared on that tab.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKNLSd29\nYIhly/+TlfsJrIiVVCazs8LyBYo+LWzjR3aYY2p2CqWHjQXYoUTkPTex2SWqsadFXnsUrFxE0QWB\njQw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T19:43:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/47d1b7be3c1236a272ed5b73d306578704500f77","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDQ3ZDFiN2JlM2MxMjM2YTI3MmVkNWI3M2QzMDY1Nzg3MDQ1MDBmNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/2c9de494d487762662f8e7ad37eaa62f92371db1","sha":"2c9de494d487762662f8e7ad37eaa62f92371db1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/2c9de494d487762662f8e7ad37eaa62f92371db1"}],"sha":"47d1b7be3c1236a272ed5b73d306578704500f77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/47d1b7be3c1236a272ed5b73d306578704500f77"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/use