5759ae69647d892c7b268a8969334211","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/67c6c4695759ae69647d892c7b268a8969334211"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/24185858dede3ff77d87df5adff285742d93e95e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T17:52:18Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"KEGustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T17:52:18Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"KEGustafsson"},"message":"Read the stack fresh everywhere its record is echoed back\n\nThe auto-update write was fixed in the last change; the update and the\nredeploy had the same hazard and are the rest of it.\n\nBoth echo fields back to preserve them — the environment for an update,\nand the branch, environment and stored git credentials for a redeploy —\nbecause Portainer''s routes rewrite each from the payload with no field\nmeaning \"leave that alone\". Both were reading them from the stack list,\nwhich is cached for fifteen seconds. A stack write does retire that key,\nbut only after sending, so a variable or a branch changed in Portainer''s\nown UI moments earlier was reverted by the very request written to keep\nit. Both now read the stack itself; the ownership refusal still comes\nfrom the cached list, which is what can name the stacks the environment\ndoes have.\n\nTwo tests turned out to be asserting nothing, and both were hiding\nbehind the same trick. One meant \"a stack in another environment is\nnever read from directly\" but filtered a pending-interceptor list for a\npath no interceptor had been registered for, which is empty whether or\nnot the read happens. The other meant \"self-management skips the\ncontainer list\" but asserted the whole pending set was empty, which only\nheld while the fixtures registered exactly what was consumed. Each now\nregisters the request that must not be made and asserts it went\nunconsumed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd","tree":{"sha":"391d4139c104d5eee1223db8a2bafbca788a8de3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/391d4139c104d5eee1223db8a2bafbca788a8de3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/24185858dede3ff77d87df5adff285742d93e95e","verification":{"payload":"tree 391d4139c104d5eee1223db8a2bafbca788a8de3\nparent b2d88a8c7ac9f24d9477d2f7553cf7c422a8c47c\nauthor KEGustafsson <ke.gustafsson@gmail.com> 1789235538 +0000\ncommitter KEGustafsson <ke.gustafsson@gmail.com> 1789235538 +0000\n\nRead the stack fresh everywhere its record is echoed back\n\nThe auto-update write was fixed in the last change; the update and the\nredeploy had the same hazard and are the rest of it.\n\nBoth echo fields back to preserve them — the environment for an update,\nand the branch, environment and stored git credentials for a redeploy —\nbecause Portainer''s routes rewrite each from the payload with no field\nmeaning \"leave that alone\". Both were reading them from the stack list,\nwhich is cached for fifteen seconds. A stack write does retire that key,\nbut only after sending, so a variable or a branch changed in Portainer''s\nown UI moments earlier was reverted by the very request written to keep\nit. Both now read the stack itself; the ownership refusal still comes\nfrom the cached list, which is what can name the stacks the environment\ndoes have.\n\nTwo tests turned out to be asserting nothing, and both were hiding\nbehind the same trick. One meant \"a stack in another environment is\nnever read from directly\" but filtered a pending-interceptor list for a\npath no interceptor had been registered for, which is empty whether or\nnot the read happens. The other meant \"self-management skips the\ncontainer list\" but asserted the whole pending set was empty, which only\nheld while the fixtures registered exactly what was consumed. Each now\nregisters the request that must not be made and asserts it went\nunconsumed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHQm01ea\nTPU/kg3o2OAgn63rAxXdu8tQBld6W7eKBFrxMh1GLDWo+J8aRE3Gt6TI1Z/GiDCR1aph3MoABdSq\nBQk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://git