":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/5e2a82477de4c4dff8c918cb017c8ec8dedeb532","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDVlMmE4MjQ3N2RlNGM0ZGZmOGM5MThjYjAxN2M4ZWM4ZGVkZWI1MzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/c5da0199e26b0fd2ac9545836f3c49478dc8b287","sha":"c5da0199e26b0fd2ac9545836f3c49478dc8b287","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/c5da0199e26b0fd2ac9545836f3c49478dc8b287"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/d2e1303a90983d5be01805e86001a56813a9c7d4","sha":"d2e1303a90983d5be01805e86001a56813a9c7d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/d2e1303a90983d5be01805e86001a56813a9c7d4"}],"sha":"5e2a82477de4c4dff8c918cb017c8ec8dedeb532","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/5e2a82477de4c4dff8c918cb017c8ec8dedeb532"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/d2e1303a90983d5be01805e86001a56813a9c7d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T14:58:08Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"KEGustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T14:58:08Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"KEGustafsson"},"message":"Read a registry id rather than whatever Number() coerces\n\nTwo ways a registry could end up being the wrong one.\n\nThe facade read `registryId` through `Number()`, which is willing to\nturn far more than an id into one: `true` becomes 1, `false` and an\nempty array become 0, and \"0x7\" becomes 7. Every one of those is an id\nPortainer may really have issued, so a body naming no registry at all\npulled through whichever registry it coerced to instead of being\nrefused. Read the way the stack id already is: a number, or digits that\nsurvive the round trip.\n\nIn the panel, the registry list outlived the environment that offered\nit. The read is guarded against the operator switching Portainer, but an\nenvironment switch leaves the panel on the same Portainer, so a read\nstill in flight passed that guard and put the old environment''s list\nback after it had been discarded. The next dialog then opened offering\nids that name something else, or nothing, here. The list is now cleared\nbefore each read and the read carries a sequence of its own, so an\nanswer to a dialog that is gone reaches nothing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd","tree":{"sha":"8aa0dee726471a0bc0a1d25124f8d18e6b938f8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/8aa0dee726471a0bc0a1d25124f8d18e6b938f8a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/d2e1303a90983d5be01805e86001a56813a9c7d4","verification":{"payload":"tree 8aa0dee726471a0bc0a1d25124f8d18e6b938f8a\nparent c9f820bc54d536d43f2f08434d1b3fb85401639b\nauthor KEGustafsson <ke.gustafsson@gmail.com> 1789225088 +0000\ncommitter KEGustafsson <ke.gustafsson@gmail.com> 1789225088 +0000\n\nRead a registry id rather than whatever Number() coerces\n\nTwo ways a registry could end up being the wrong one.\n\nThe facade read `registryId` through `Number()`, which is willing to\nturn far more than an id into one: `true` becomes 1, `false` and an\nempty array become 0, and \"0x7\" becomes 7. Every one of those is an id\nPortainer may really have issued, so a body naming no registry at all\npulled through whichever registry it coerced to instead of being\nrefused. Read the way the stack id already is: a number, or digits that\nsurvive the round trip.\n\nIn the panel, the registry list outlived the environment that offered\nit. The read is guarded against the operator switching Portainer, but an\nenvironment switch leaves the panel on the same Portainer, so a read\nstill in flight passed that guard and put the old environment''s list\nback after it had been discarded. The next dialog then opened offering\nids that name something else, or nothing, here. The list is now cleared\nbefore each read and the read carries a sequence of its own, so an\nanswer to a dialog that is gone reaches nothing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKoQ+H65\n81LFxxV2bM2GgVFHIr79j7Ocna6pdCHy3qZeFF8AMtp9C85a8zHGiE4HpvN2JmUjZie4sR8QNQKh\nzQY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/d2e1303a90983d5be01805e86001a56813a9c7d4","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGQyZTEzMDNhOTA5ODNkNWJlMDE4MDVlODYwMDFhNTY4MTNhOWM3ZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/c9f820bc54d536d43f2f08434d1b3fb85401639b","sha":"c9f820bc54d536d43f2f08434d1b3fb85401639b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/c9f820bc54d536d43f2f08434d1b3fb85401639b"}],"sha":"d2e1303a90983d5be01805e86001a56813a9c7d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/d2e1303a90983d5be01805e86001a56813a9c7d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/c9f820bc54d536d43f2f08434d1b3fb85401639b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T14:45:11Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T14:45:11Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Pull from a private registry without handling its password\n\nThe pull added two releases ago could only reach a registry that needed no\nlogin: it worked for Docker Hub and failed with a registry error for anything\nof the operator''s own, with nothing in the panel to do about it. It was also\nAPI-only — there was no way to pull from the panel at all.\n\nPortainer already holds the credentials, and will use them without handing\nthem over. Its Docker proxy intercepts `/images/create`, reads a registry id\nout of the `X-Registry-Auth` header and replaces the whole header with\ncredentials from its own store before Docker sees the request. So the plugin\nsends a reference, never a secret, and the worst a wrong id can do is fail to\nauthenticate.\n\n- `pullImage(reference, registryId?)` sends that header when a registry is\n  named, and nothing at all when one is not — an anonymous pull is the request\n  it always was.\n- `registries()` reads `GET /endpoints/{id}/registries`, not Portainer''s\n  global `GET /registries`. The global one is administrator-only and answers\n  403 for the scoped token this README recommends; its own error message says\n  to use the environment route instead. The record is narrowed on the way\n  through to id, name, address and whether credentials exist — the raw one\n  carries GitLab, Quay, ECR and access-policy blocks the panel has no use for.\n- `GET /registries` on the facade offers that list, and `POST /images/pull`\n  takes an optional `registryId`, validated as an id rather than passed on to\n  be refused by Portainer with a message about its own internals. The audit\n  records which registry was used, because that is a use of stored credentials.\n- A **Fetch image** dialog on the Images tab, gated on control but not on\n  destructive — a pull takes nothing away. The reference is checked against\n  the facade''s own grammar as it is typed, anonymous is the default, and a\n  registry Portainer holds no credentials for says so, because choosing it\n  changes nothing. A registry list that cannot be read is reported inside the\n  dialog rather than stopping the anonymous pull that never needed it.\n\n11 new tests, 1048 in all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd","tree":{"sha":"de83131df48a4e9de836c6ddc4d55eb4ae2bd9d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/de83131df48a4e9de836c6ddc4d55eb4ae2bd9d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/c9f820bc54d536d43f2f08434d1b3fb85401639b","verification":{"payload":"tree de83131df48a4e9de836c6ddc4d55eb4ae2bd9d8\nparent c5da0199e26b0fd2ac9545836f3c49478dc8b287\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789224311 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789224311 +0000\n\nPull from a private registry without handling its password\n\nThe pull added two releases ago could only reach a registry that needed no\nlogin: it worked for Docker Hub and failed with a registry error for anything\nof the operator''s own, with nothing in the panel to do about it. It was also\nAPI-only — there was no way to pull from the panel at all.\n\nPortainer already holds the credentials, and will use them without handing\nthem over. Its Docker proxy intercepts `/images/create`, reads a registry id\nout of the `X-Registry-Auth` header and replaces the whole header with\ncredentials from its own store before Docker sees the request. So the plugin\nsends a reference, never a secret, and the worst a wrong id can do is fail to\nauthenticate.\n\n- `pullImage(reference, registryId?)` sends that header when a registry is\n  named, and nothing at all when one is not — an anonymous pull is the request\n  it always was.\n- `registries()` reads `GET /endpoints/{id}/registries`, not Portainer''s\n  global `GET /registries`. The global one is administrator-only and answers\n  403 for the scoped token this README recommends; its own error message says\n  to use the environment route instead. The record is narrowed on the way\n  through to id, name, address and whether credentials exist — the raw one\n  carries GitLab, Quay, ECR and access-policy blocks the panel has no use for.\n- `GET /registries` on the facade offers that list, and `POST /images/pull`\n  takes an optional `registryId`, validated as an id rather than passed on to\n  be refused by Portainer with a message about its own internals. The audit\n  records which registry was used, because that is a use of stored credentials.\n- A **Fetch image** dialog on the Images tab, gated on control but not on\n  destructive — a pull takes nothing away. The reference is checked against\n  the facade''s own grammar as it is typed, anonymous is the default, and a\n  registry Portainer holds no credentials for says so, because choosing it\n  changes nothing. A registry list that cannot be read is reported inside the\n  dialog rather than stopping the anonymous pull that never needed it.\n\n11 new tests, 1048 in all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFVc04x+\nq7IBqbfS03ihcM9fKW/uwRYbAJeHfztwDKYREMuWX+D9jwuRF/VNdCxJ0ZDz5ayfDbcKJbidV8Ra\nlAQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T14:45:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/c9f820bc54d536d43f2f08434d1b3fb85401639b","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGM5ZjgyMGJjNTRkNTM2ZDQzZjJmMDg0MzRkMWIzZmI4NTQwMTYzOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/c5da0199e26b0fd2ac9545836f3c49478dc8b287","sha":"c5da0199e26b0fd2ac9545836f3c49478dc8b287","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/c5da0199e26b0fd2ac9545836f3c49478dc8b287"}],"sha":"c9f820bc54d536d43f2f08434d1b3fb85401639b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/c9f820bc54d536d43f2f08434d1b3fb8540163