e":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/c5da0199e26b0fd2ac9545836f3c49478dc8b287","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGM1ZGEwMTk5ZTI2YjBmZDJhYzk1NDU4MzZmM2M0OTQ3OGRjOGIyODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/596cf4762d2f0b91b5f3995325b8f670ed65a170","sha":"596cf4762d2f0b91b5f3995325b8f670ed65a170","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/596cf4762d2f0b91b5f3995325b8f670ed65a170"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/47477980a2b08c2e8380e0020139693f0a95df8a","sha":"47477980a2b08c2e8380e0020139693f0a95df8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/47477980a2b08c2e8380e0020139693f0a95df8a"}],"sha":"c5da0199e26b0fd2ac9545836f3c49478dc8b287","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/c5da0199e26b0fd2ac9545836f3c49478dc8b287"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/47477980a2b08c2e8380e0020139693f0a95df8a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T13:47:21Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T13:47:21Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Make the subscription earn its recovery, and the newer read win\n\nCodeRabbit''s review of the event stream. Four of its five findings were real;\nthe fifth would break a documented setup.\n\n**A handshake is not recovery.** `failures` and `quiet` were cleared as soon as\nthe stream opened, so a proxy that answers 200 and closes the body at once\nreset the backoff every cycle — the retry never slowed past its first step, and\neach cycle logged that events had \"resumed\" when nothing had. Recovery is now\nan event arriving, or the stream holding open for 30s; a stream that dies\nbefore either keeps the outage it was already in.\n\n**The newer read wins.** `refresh()` and `poll()` guarded themselves\nseparately, so a slow interval read of an instance could land after a fast\nevent-driven one and publish the older Docker over the newer — putting a\ncontainer back the way it was until something read again. Reads now take a\nticket in the order they start, and a read whose ticket is older than the\nnewest published is dropped. An event that arrives mid-read is no longer\ndropped either: it records one trailing read, which runs when the current one\nfinishes.\n\n**`null` is valid JSON.** It parsed, the cast did not catch it, and the first\nread of `.Type` threw — tearing down a healthy stream over one line something\nin the middle wrote. Only non-null objects are yielded now.\n\n**The docs oversold the logging.** A stream that *fails* is logged once per\noutage; one that simply ends reconnects without a word. Both README and\nchangelog now say which is which.\n\nNot changed: refusing an `http://` base URL for the event stream. The README\ndocuments `http://192.168.1.10:9000` and the config validator accepts `http:`\ndeliberately — Portainer''s default HTTP port on the same Pi is the ordinary\nboat setup. Every other authenticated call already goes over that same base\nURL with the same credential, so refusing it in this one method would break a\nsupported configuration while changing nothing about the exposure. If TLS\nshould be required, that belongs in config validation for all traffic, as its\nown change.\n\n1037 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd","tree":{"sha":"305f7ac272fe0f9e64fb99d1fd150d448376e39a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/305f7ac272fe0f9e64fb99d1fd150d448376e39a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/47477980a2b08c2e8380e0020139693f0a95df8a","verification":{"payload":"tree 305f7ac272fe0f9e64fb99d1fd150d448376e39a\nparent e511fd0ff06343671ed35080baac428ea8008ebb\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789220841 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789220841 +0000\n\nMake the subscription earn its recovery, and the newer read win\n\nCodeRabbit''s review of the event stream. Four of its five findings were real;\nthe fifth would break a documented setup.\n\n**A handshake is not recovery.** `failures` and `quiet` were cleared as soon as\nthe stream opened, so a proxy that answers 200 and closes the body at once\nreset the backoff every cycle — the retry never slowed past its first step, and\neach cycle logged that events had \"resumed\" when nothing had. Recovery is now\nan event arriving, or the stream holding open for 30s; a stream that dies\nbefore either keeps the outage it was already in.\n\n**The newer read wins.** `refresh()` and `poll()` guarded themselves\nseparately, so a slow interval read of an instance could land after a fast\nevent-driven one and publish the older Docker over the newer — putting a\ncontainer back the way it was until something read again. Reads now take a\nticket in the order they start, and a read whose ticket is older than the\nnewest published is dropped. An event that arrives mid-read is no longer\ndropped either: it records one trailing read, which runs when the current one\nfinishes.\n\n**`null` is valid JSON.** It parsed, the cast did not catch it, and the first\nread of `.Type` threw — tearing down a healthy stream over one line something\nin the middle wrote. Only non-null objects are yielded now.\n\n**The docs oversold the logging.** A stream that *fails* is logged once per\noutage; one that simply ends reconnects without a word. Both README and\nchangelog now say which is which.\n\nNot changed: refusing an `http://` base URL for the event stream. The README\ndocuments `http://192.168.1.10:9000` and the config validator accepts `http:`\ndeliberately — Portainer''s default HTTP port on the same Pi is the ordinary\nboat setup. Every other authenticated call already goes over that same base\nURL with the same credential, so refusing it in this one method would break a\nsupported configuration while changing nothing about the exposure. If TLS\nshould be required, that belongs in config validation for all traffic, as its\nown change.\n\n1037 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMa7p+oE\npje1+jjjJbZJ2hNq8fXJS4+zX9nX+1ZsQ2lCI8hXKlc7BsLKqahFKnaP8ZVIKgBGw1/4wwjkBdkP\nagQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T13:47:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/47477980a2b08c2e8380e0020139693f0a95df8a","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDQ3NDc3OTgwYTJiMDhjMmU4MzgwZTAwMjAxMzk2OTNmMGE5NWRmOGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/e511fd0ff06343671ed35080baac428ea8008ebb","sha":"e511fd0ff06343671ed35080baac428ea8008ebb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/e511fd0ff06343671ed35080baac428ea8008ebb"}],"sha":"47477980a2b08c2e8380e0020139693f0a95df8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/47477980a2b08c2e8380e0020139693f0a95df8a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/e511fd0ff06343671ed35080baac428ea8008ebb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T13:32:34Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T13:32:34Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Let Docker say when a container changed, instead of asking\n\nThe poller asks every instance every interval whether anything moved. On a\nboat that is the wrong question twice over: most intervals nothing has moved,\nand the intervals where something did are the ones somebody is waiting on. A\ncontainer that died at 02:00:01 raised its alarm at 02:00:10, and cost a\ncontainer listing across the radio link every ten seconds to find that out.\n\nDocker will say so instead. `DockerApi.eventStream` subscribes to\n`/events?filters={\"type\":[\"container\"]}` through Portainer''s proxy — the same\nbounded-handshake, unbounded-body shape `logStream` already uses — and\n`ContainerEvents` holds one per instance, asking the poller to read that\ninstance when something happens that could change what the plugin publishes.\n\nThe interval keeps running underneath. This is a prompt to look early, never\nthe only thing that looks, which is what makes it safe to add:\n\n- An environment with no Docker API behind it — Kubernetes, an async Edge\n  agent — never opens a stream and keeps exactly the interval it had.\n- A stream that drops or ends reconnects with a backoff to a 60s ceiling, and\n  is logged once per outage rather than once per attempt: an unreachable\n  Portainer is already on the status line, and repeating it every two seconds\n  would bury the log an operator reads for anything else.\n- `refresh(instance)` contains its own failures, will not run twice for the\n  same instance at once, and leaves the health report to the timer — \"1 of 2\n  reachable\" is a statement about the instances together and cannot be\n  assembled from one of them.\n- Only the actions that change published state cause a read. A console\n  session''s `exec_create` and `exec_start` fire constantly and are ignored;\n  `health_status: healthy` is matched on the verb before the colon; a stack\n  deploy''s burst settles for 400ms and becomes one read rather than one per\n  container.\n\nSo the interval now bounds how long a *missed* change can go unnoticed rather\nthan how long every change waits, and a metered link can afford a longer one.\n\n20 new tests, 1033 in all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd","tree":{"sha":"bb70bea413bf7c9cc569aed6ae77e01d68b21ac9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/bb70bea413bf7c9cc569aed6ae77e01d68b21ac9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/e511fd0ff06343671ed35080baac428ea8008ebb","verification":{"payload":"tree bb70bea413bf7c9cc569aed6ae77e01d68b21ac9\nparent 596cf4762d2f0b91b5f3995325b8f670ed65a170\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789219954 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789219954 +0000\n\nLet Docker say when a container changed, instead of asking\n\nThe poller asks every instance every interval whether anything moved. On a\nboat that is the wrong question twice over: most intervals nothing has moved,\nand the intervals where something did are the ones somebody is waiting on. A\ncontainer that died at 02:00:01 raised its alarm at 02:00:10, and cost a\ncontainer listing across the radio link every ten seconds to find that out.\n\nDocker will say so instead. `DockerApi.eventStream` subscribes to\n`/events?filters={\"type\":[\"container\"]}` through Portainer''s proxy — the same\nbounded-handshake, unbounded-body shape `logStream` already uses — and\n`ContainerEvents` holds one per instance, asking the poller to read that\ninstance when something happens that could change what the plugin publishes.\n\nThe interval keeps running underneath. This is a prompt to look early, never\nthe only thing that looks, which is what makes it safe to add:\n\n- An environment with no Docker API behind it — Kubernetes, an async Edge\n  agent — never opens a stream and keeps exactly the interval it had.\n- A stream that drops or ends reconnects with a backoff to a 60s ceiling, and\n  is logged once per outage rather than once per attempt: an unreachable\n  Portainer is already on the status line, and repeating it every two seconds\n  would bury the log an operator reads for anything else.\n- `refresh(instance)` contains its own failures, will not run twice for the\n  same instance at once, and leaves the health report to the timer — \"1 of 2\n  reachable\" is a statement about the instances together and cannot be\n  assembled from one of them.\n- Only the actions that change published state cause a read. A console\n  session''s `exec_create` and `exec_start` fire constantly and are ignored;\n  `health_status: healthy` is matched on the verb before the colon; a stack\n  deploy''s burst settles for 400ms and becomes one read rather than one per\n  container.\n\nSo the interval now bounds how long a *missed* change can go unnoticed rather\nthan how long every change waits, and a metered link can afford a longer one.\n\n20 new tests, 1033 in all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFQeDj3b\n5hNHzVFkz4R45taYSufSwualkNLb8T4i4iJIMex/8KnZwb3RnHHG8cOHecrvF7SFxRU3JmmCQV2F\nUwg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T13:32:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/e511fd0ff06343671ed35080baac428ea8008ebb","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGU1MTFmZDBmZjA2MzQzNjcxZWQzNTA4MGJhYWM0MjhlYTgwMDhlYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/596cf4762d2f0b91b5f3995325b8f670ed65a170","sha":"596cf4762d2f0b91b5f3995325b8f670ed65a170","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/596cf4762d2f0b91b5f3995325b8f670ed65a170"}],"sha":"e511fd0ff06343671ed35080baac428ea8008ebb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/e511fd0ff06343671ed35080baac428ea8008ebb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other