":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/562b53dafe0ff871d07175129e6036612577e704","sha":"562b53dafe0ff871d07175129e6036612577e704","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/562b53dafe0ff871d07175129e6036612577e704"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/acec1d5712f56a86ae7360e1f47f500c95c8325b","sha":"acec1d5712f56a86ae7360e1f47f500c95c8325b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/acec1d5712f56a86ae7360e1f47f500c95c8325b"}],"sha":"596cf4762d2f0b91b5f3995325b8f670ed65a170","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/596cf4762d2f0b91b5f3995325b8f670ed65a170"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/acec1d5712f56a86ae7360e1f47f500c95c8325b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T12:36:06Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T12:36:06Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Refuse a pull that reported nothing, and answers for a Portainer left behind\n\nThe refreshed review, now against 2142d0c. Two of its three findings were\nreal; the third would have introduced the bug it was trying to prevent.\n\n**A pull with no readable progress is no longer a success.** Docker answers\n`/images/create` with a progress stream and nothing else — an image already\ncurrent still says \"Status: Image is up to date for …\" — so an answer carrying\nno parseable record came from something in between: a proxy that buffered the\nbody away, a tunnel that dropped it. `ok: true` for that told the operator an\nimage was there when nothing had said so. A body-less answer, a stream with no\nprogress record in it, and an unterminated line past the hold limit are all\n502s now, with a hint saying the pull may or may not have happened.\n\n**A completion scoped to the instance it started on.** The request already\nwent to the right host and the table refresh was already guarded, but the\nresult banner, the dialog it closed and the busy mark it lifted were not: a\nslow stop on one Portainer announced itself over another, cleared a\nconfirmation the operator had opened since, and re-enabled a button whose own\nrequest was still open. `stillOn` now gates every completion write in\nrunAction, runImage, runStack, loadControl and selectEnvironment, and a switch\nclears the busy set and the busy stack — nothing else was going to.\n\n**Not changed: the watchdog''s down-poll count across an unreachable poll.**\nClearing it there is what turns a flaky link into silence — unreachable,\nmissing, unreachable, missing never reaches two in a row, so the alarm never\nfires however long the container has been gone. Keeping the count means two\nobservations of \"missing\" with more time between them than two consecutive\npolls, which is the debounce doing its job rather than failing it. A test now\npins that.\n\n1013 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd","tree":{"sha":"0be7d76dcbb08fde08c9e427e52af4d8b687b6aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/0be7d76dcbb08fde08c9e427e52af4d8b687b6aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/acec1d5712f56a86ae7360e1f47f500c95c8325b","verification":{"payload":"tree 0be7d76dcbb08fde08c9e427e52af4d8b687b6aa\nparent 2142d0cd2af40c421e75e56aa35b34d13178636c\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789216566 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789216566 +0000\n\nRefuse a pull that reported nothing, and answers for a Portainer left behind\n\nThe refreshed review, now against 2142d0c. Two of its three findings were\nreal; the third would have introduced the bug it was trying to prevent.\n\n**A pull with no readable progress is no longer a success.** Docker answers\n`/images/create` with a progress stream and nothing else — an image already\ncurrent still says \"Status: Image is up to date for …\" — so an answer carrying\nno parseable record came from something in between: a proxy that buffered the\nbody away, a tunnel that dropped it. `ok: true` for that told the operator an\nimage was there when nothing had said so. A body-less answer, a stream with no\nprogress record in it, and an unterminated line past the hold limit are all\n502s now, with a hint saying the pull may or may not have happened.\n\n**A completion scoped to the instance it started on.** The request already\nwent to the right host and the table refresh was already guarded, but the\nresult banner, the dialog it closed and the busy mark it lifted were not: a\nslow stop on one Portainer announced itself over another, cleared a\nconfirmation the operator had opened since, and re-enabled a button whose own\nrequest was still open. `stillOn` now gates every completion write in\nrunAction, runImage, runStack, loadControl and selectEnvironment, and a switch\nclears the busy set and the busy stack — nothing else was going to.\n\n**Not changed: the watchdog''s down-poll count across an unreachable poll.**\nClearing it there is what turns a flaky link into silence — unreachable,\nmissing, unreachable, missing never reaches two in a row, so the alarm never\nfires however long the container has been gone. Keeping the count means two\nobservations of \"missing\" with more time between them than two consecutive\npolls, which is the debounce doing its job rather than failing it. A test now\npins that.\n\n1013 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBQbJBEx\n9lWIIgEMnjI6SF793TD+2lphblA47U7yq0/5LJJ5UGphS+LFXT+yRzVsrAoIrGEAfnzsXF17iJga\nkgU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T12:36:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/acec1d5712f56a86ae7360e1f47f500c95c8325b","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGFjZWMxZDU3MTJmNTZhODZhZTczNjBlMWY0N2Y1MDBjOTVjODMyNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/2142d0cd2af40c421e75e56aa35b34d13178636c","sha":"2142d0cd2af40c421e75e56aa35b34d13178636c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/2142d0cd2af40c421e75e56aa35b34d13178636c"}],"sha":"acec1d5712f56a86ae7360e1f47f500c95c8325b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/acec1d5712f56a86ae7360e1f47f500c95c8325b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/2142d0cd2af40c421e75e56aa35b34d13178636c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T11:36:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T11:36:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Say what three helpers do that their names do not\n\n`sleep` is unreferenced so a settle poll cannot keep Signal K from exiting,\n`messageSize` takes every shape `ws` hands a message over in, and\n`compareVersions` treats a missing segment as zero so 2.42 and 2.42.0 are the\nsame release. None of that is in the names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd","tree":{"sha":"0d97c160931b76bcd490a2843de234f1153baf31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/0d97c160931b76bcd490a2843de234f1153baf31"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/2142d0cd2af40c421e75e56aa35b34d13178636c","verification":{"payload":"tree 0d97c160931b76bcd490a2843de234f1153baf31\nparent aec576845f6eee72f44d771e17ed69397b8f8947\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789212965 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789212965 +0000\n\nSay what three helpers do that their names do not\n\n`sleep` is unreferenced so a settle poll cannot keep Signal K from exiting,\n`messageSize` takes every shape `ws` hands a message over in, and\n`compareVersions` treats a missing segment as zero so 2.42 and 2.42.0 are the\nsame release. None of that is in the names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQN21CGyN\nQK+fZ5VjkS8fb/PwzW885E1Jd3QZcvUdror4G+hYUzLqLfDDdAIyTqOr9pDsYW8vcKkiMhJ8fg8T\nfgE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T11:36:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/2142d0cd2af40c421e75e56aa35b34d13178636c","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDIxNDJkMGNkMmFmNDBjNDIxZTc1ZTU2YWEzNWIzNGQxMzE3ODYzNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/aec576845f6eee72f44d771e17ed69397b8f8947","sha":"aec576845f6eee72f44d771e17ed69397b8f8947","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/aec576845f6eee72f44d771e17ed69397b8f8947"}],"sha":"2142d0cd2af40c421e75e56aa35b34d13178636c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/2142d0cd2af40c421e75e56aa35b34d13178636c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/aec576845f6eee72f44d771e17ed69397b8f8947/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T11:30:38Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T11:30:38Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Answer the review: a traversal, two bounds and a budget\n\nCodeRabbit''s line-by-line pass over the robustness PR. Fifteen findings and a\nnitpick; thirteen were real and are fixed here, two were not and are answered\non the thread.\n\nThe one that matters: an image reference kept its slashes so Docker would read\nthe name whole, which made a `..` among them a path segment the URL parser\nacted on. `DELETE /images/../../../stacks/3` resolved to `/api/stacks/3` and\ndeleted a stack, past the ownership guard and the audit that route has. Empty,\n`.` and `..` segments are refused now.\n\nThe rest, by layer:\n\n- The console backlog measured only what it was already holding, so the first\n  message through — on a socket whose ticket had not been checked — was kept\n  whatever its size.\n- One drain timer belonged to whichever relay direction congested first; the\n  other could not pause its sender and ran to the hard limit.\n- A watchdog alarm that changes while staying an alarm is published again, so\n  a container that goes from exited to paused stops sounding.\n- A stack write and the deploy it waits for share one budget; the settle\n  deadline started when the write was answered.\n- URL userinfo with no password is a forge token, and is redacted whole.\n- A value typed against a blank name is refused rather than dropped, in the\n  helper and in the editor that never used it.\n- A press of Select counts once: the stopPropagation the gated button lost\n  when it replaced a plain one is back.\n- The panel keeps one polling timer, not one per visibility change.\n- A pull''s progress stream is read a line at a time, bounded.\n- The redeploy drops `RepositoryGitCredentialID`, which Portainer''s redeploy\n  payload has never had a field for on any 2.x release, and `StackRedeploy`\n  drops `tlsSkipVerify` for the same reason — TLS skip comes from the stack''s\n  stored git config.\n- The README says what 2.17 is actually needed for.\n\nAnswered rather than changed: the redeploy route takes no `SourceID` in any\nrelease, and starts from the stored credentials in the Sources model too; and\nan instance name cannot be both dropped and active, because the row that\nfailed claimed the name before it failed.\n\nTen new tests, 1010 in all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd","tree":{"sha":"ec2e0f6c0c6a363e7e1a0f9fdbb55fdccc460732","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/ec2e0f6c0c6a363e7e1a0f9fdbb55fdccc460732"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/aec576845f6eee72f44d771e17ed69397b8f8947","verification":{"payload":"tree ec2e0f6c0c6a363e7e1a0f9fdbb55fdccc460732\nparent 7528a0d56abf37ed885db9a4615e644698d5e242\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789212638 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789212638 +0000\n\nAnswer the review: a traversal, two bounds and a budget\n\nCodeRabbit''s line-by-line pass over the robustness PR. Fifteen findings and a\nnitpick; thirteen were real and are fixed here, two were not and are answered\non the thread.\n\nThe one that matters: an image reference kept its slashes so Docker would read\nthe name whole, which made a `..` among them a path segment the URL parser\nacted on. `DELETE /images/../../../stacks/3` resolved to `/api/stacks/3` and\ndeleted a stack, past the ownership guard and the audit that route has. Empty,\n`.` and `..` segments are refused now.\n\nThe rest, by layer:\n\n- The console backlog measured only what it was already holding, so the first\n  message through — on a socket whose ticket had not been checked — was kept\n  whatever its size.\n- One drain timer belonged to whichever relay direction congested first; the\n  other could not pause its sender and ran to the hard limit.\n- A watchdog alarm that changes while staying an alarm is published again, so\n  a container that goes from exited to paused stops sounding.\n- A stack write and the deploy it waits for share one budget; the settle\n  deadline started when the write was answered.\n- URL userinfo with no password is a forge token, and is redacted whole.\n- A value typed against a blank name is refused rather than dropped, in the\n  helper and in the editor that never used it.\n- A press of Select counts once: the stopPropagation the gated button lost\n  when it replaced a plain one is back.\n- The panel keeps one polling timer, not one per visibility change.\n- A pull''s progress stream is read a line at a time, bounded.\n- The redeploy drops `RepositoryGitCredentialID`, which Portainer''s redeploy\n  payload has never had a field for on any 2.x release, and `StackRedeploy`\n  drops `tlsSkipVerify` for the same reason — TLS skip comes from the stack''s\n  stored git config.\n- The README says what 2.17 is actually needed for.\n\nAnswered rather than changed: the redeploy route takes no `SourceID` in any\nrelease, and starts from the stored credentials in the Sources model too; and\nan instance name cannot be both dropped and active, because the row that\nfailed claimed the name before it failed.\n\nTen new tests, 1010 in all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGGa7SIw\nGMtVgOPkTWtZJV7F576U0voHWYE/bBq5UhFYdCOjD3tPiEAZQr0jZ06HAr2mfBwYG+NKXMTBOu36\nUwM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T11:30:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/aec576845f6eee72f44d771e17ed69397b8f8947","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGFlYzU3Njg0NWY2ZWVlNzJmNDRkNzcxZTE3ZWQ2OTM5N2I4Zjg5NDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/7528a0d56abf37ed885db9a4615e644698d5e242","sha":"7528a0d56abf37ed885db9a4615e644698d5e242","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/7528a0d56abf37ed885db9a4615e644698d5e242"}],"sha":"aec576845f6eee72f44d771e17ed69397b8f8947","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/aec576845f6eee72f44d771e17ed69397b8f8947"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/7528a0d56abf37ed885db9a4615e644698d5e242/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T11:05:36Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T11:05:36Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Refuse an oversized body on what arrived, not on what was announced\n\nAnswering 413 off the declared content-length replies while the client is\nstill writing, and the connection breaks under it: the answer the operator\nneeded is the one that gets lost. macOS saw it as EPIPE in CI.\n\nbody-parser already refuses on the declared length for a body it parses\nitself, and it does it without that race. What it cannot do is refuse a\nbody somebody else parsed — which is every request in production, since the\nSignal K server runs its own JSON parser over every route before a plugin''s\nrouter sees one, with a ten-megabyte limit of its own. That is the case\nthis check is for, and the test now mounts a host parser to prove it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd","tree":{"sha":"a0bf67675653d10988d463a66a8cdbb36b9bea5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/a0bf67675653d10988d463a66a8cdbb36b9bea5a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/7528a0d56abf37ed885db9a4615e644698d5e242","verification":{"payload":"tree a0bf67675653d10988d463a66a8cdbb36b9bea5a\nparent 4be82f440c9c44648904f070cdb7482ebf9ead83\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789211136 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789211136 +0000\n\nRefuse an oversized body on what arrived, not on what was announced\n\nAnswering 413 off the declared content-length replies while the client is\nstill writing, and the connection breaks under it: the answer the operator\nneeded is the one that gets lost. macOS saw it as EPIPE in CI.\n\nbody-parser already refuses on the declared length for a body it parses\nitself, and it does it without that race. What it cannot do is refuse a\nbody somebody else parsed — which is every request in production, since the\nSignal K server runs its own JSON parser over every route before a plugin''s\nrouter sees one, with a ten-megabyte limit of its own. That is the case\nthis check is for, and the test now mounts a host parser to prove it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQERarlWn\n9so/BvC58cFfuetdR6pRlKOpJKQuxczPpnJU8Dnh8vs8Pj3eIH27c3U/WfdOx1bnGJMYvkjAAwKy\nYAw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T11:05:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clau