s://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/4be82f440c9c44648904f070cdb7482ebf9ead83/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T11:01:04Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T11:01:04Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Make the plugin hold up, and reach the Portainer API it was missing\n\nFive reviews of the whole codebase — the Portainer client, the REST facade\nand plugin lifecycle, the streaming and console relay, the browser panel, and\nthe API surface against Portainer''s and Docker''s own sources — and the\nfindings worth acting on.\n\nThe one that matters most on a real boat: a Signal K installed on the host\nbeside Docker has every running container''s mounts in its own mount table,\nand self-protection read the first id it found there as its own. It then\nrefused to stop that container, which is usually Portainer itself. The mount\ntable is read as a table now.\n\nBeyond the fixes, the calls an operator kept having to leave the panel for:\none reading of what a container costs, the processes inside it, fetching an\nimage, and recreating a container onto a newer one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd","tree":{"sha":"414b2d27b49ffdd7a99c31c20f28e5be4655cd71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/414b2d27b49ffdd7a99c31c20f28e5be4655cd71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/4be82f440c9c44648904f070cdb7482ebf9ead83","verification":{"payload":"tree 414b2d27b49ffdd7a99c31c20f28e5be4655cd71\nparent 562b53dafe0ff871d07175129e6036612577e704\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789210864 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789210864 +0000\n\nMake the plugin hold up, and reach the Portainer API it was missing\n\nFive reviews of the whole codebase — the Portainer client, the REST facade\nand plugin lifecycle, the streaming and console relay, the browser panel, and\nthe API surface against Portainer''s and Docker''s own sources — and the\nfindings worth acting on.\n\nThe one that matters most on a real boat: a Signal K installed on the host\nbeside Docker has every running container''s mounts in its own mount table,\nand self-protection read the first id it found there as its own. It then\nrefused to stop that container, which is usually Portainer itself. The mount\ntable is read as a table now.\n\nBeyond the fixes, the calls an operator kept having to leave the panel for:\none reading of what a container costs, the processes inside it, fetching an\nimage, and recreating a container onto a newer one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9fDtyuD5qoERSx31HHEbd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLUq6PT5\n2Ar1ofvM7GIiBx/pGnnxHP1md2069vEdD7jaZq2AlSBMIGRj03tEIau5XhNunvoax1rtQ3QegB/J\nFgw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T11:01:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.