/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/696b1e144629d24dc913bf3779126e631f413a31/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T12:24:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T12:24:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Release 0.1.2\n\nThe changelog''s Unreleased section was already the notes for this release, so\nit is cut as 0.1.2: the same-site check that refused every write behind a\nreverse proxy, and the image delete and prune that give an operator a way to\nfree the disk before a full SD card takes Signal K down.\n\nThe lint work the release also carries goes under Changed — the ten type-aware\nrules staged at ''warn'' are errors now that their backlog is clear, and the one\nsubstantive finding among those 272, Express 4 being handed an async route\nhandler whose promise it ignores, is written in as the gap it closed rather\nthan as a defect it fixed.\n\nThe README''s tarball name follows the version.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LkzqXCtZyxUiXjgdLMcKdQ","tree":{"sha":"8729690e850aaa972d7b8e73a19e298d5b061968","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/8729690e850aaa972d7b8e73a19e298d5b061968"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/696b1e144629d24dc913bf3779126e631f413a31","verification":{"payload":"tree 8729690e850aaa972d7b8e73a19e298d5b061968\nparent 929c59dd4e0b5d63f16b8fc902fbfbab0eaf7237\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787574272 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787574272 +0000\n\nRelease 0.1.2\n\nThe changelog''s Unreleased section was already the notes for this release, so\nit is cut as 0.1.2: the same-site check that refused every write behind a\nreverse proxy, and the image delete and prune that give an operator a way to\nfree the disk before a full SD card takes Signal K down.\n\nThe lint work the release also carries goes under Changed — the ten type-aware\nrules staged at ''warn'' are errors now that their backlog is clear, and the one\nsubstantive finding among those 272, Express 4 being handed an async route\nhandler whose promise it ignores, is written in as the gap it closed rather\nthan as a defect it fixed.\n\nThe README''s tarball name follows the version.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LkzqXCtZyxUiXjgdLMcKdQ\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMYe8vfA\naqRDHnMBQ7DuEmFAYxUA/AfbI8WFAc3rxrUHLII97XQJQqd9lu+pmeSsVSVbrC5DwpPDA4zwpOIA\nLgw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T12:24:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"http