b.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/e03bb87608491b936f9cbc2db0e650bfe923d554","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGUwM2JiODc2MDg0OTFiOTM2ZjljYmMyZGIwZTY1MGJmZTkyM2Q1NTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/48d156dc153ca24488d4b8c69ad762b3bab431fc","sha":"48d156dc153ca24488d4b8c69ad762b3bab431fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/48d156dc153ca24488d4b8c69ad762b3bab431fc"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/83181b2c23c9fe3816a2c0002c84ed0d3d74aeb7","sha":"83181b2c23c9fe3816a2c0002c84ed0d3d74aeb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/83181b2c23c9fe3816a2c0002c84ed0d3d74aeb7"}],"sha":"e03bb87608491b936f9cbc2db0e650bfe923d554","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/e03bb87608491b936f9cbc2db0e650bfe923d554"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/83181b2c23c9fe3816a2c0002c84ed0d3d74aeb7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T08:08:36Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T08:08:36Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Stop a stale disk read, and count a held image''s shared base as held\n\nThree things the review found on the images work.\n\nThe reclaimable figure counted a shared base layer as space a prune\nwould return. An image a container holds keeps every layer it needs on\ndisk, including the base it happens to share with something else, so\nsubtracting only its exclusive bytes offered back space the prune cannot\ntouch: the fixture of two images off one 400 MB base reported 500 MB\nreclaimable where a prune frees 100. The whole size of an image in use\nis subtracted now. Two held images off one base have that base counted\ntwice, which understates the figure — the direction worth being wrong\nin, and the one the comment already claimed.\n\nThe /df read applied whatever landed last. The read the Images tab opens\nwith is often still in flight when a prune finishes, and it is an\naccount of the disk from before the prune ran; landing second it put the\npre-prune total and its badges back, so the prune read as having done\nnothing. Reads are sequenced now, and the effect retires the sequence on\nteardown as well as aborting — the prune''s own read carries no signal,\nso the abort alone would not stop it answering for an instance or tab\nthe operator has left. Covered by a test that resolves the two reads in\nreverse.\n\nThe prune cache test named the disk usage in its title and only\nexercised the image list; it reads /system/df either side of the prune\nnow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019FmoVDLow4N1mo8qwcmVZr","tree":{"sha":"0f19b9f7b23de07be9bae8b62011e5cc529e74fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/0f19b9f7b23de07be9bae8b62011e5cc529e74fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/83181b2c23c9fe3816a2c0002c84ed0d3d74aeb7","verification":{"payload":"tree 0f19b9f7b23de07be9bae8b62011e5cc529e74fc\nparent 48d156dc153ca24488d4b8c69ad762b3bab431fc\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787558916 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787558916 +0000\n\nStop a stale disk read, and count a held image''s shared base as held\n\nThree things the review found on the images work.\n\nThe reclaimable figure counted a shared base layer as space a prune\nwould return. An image a container holds keeps every layer it needs on\ndisk, including the base it happens to share with something else, so\nsubtracting only its exclusive bytes offered back space the prune cannot\ntouch: the fixture of two images off one 400 MB base reported 500 MB\nreclaimable where a prune frees 100. The whole size of an image in use\nis subtracted now. Two held images off one base have that base counted\ntwice, which understates the figure — the direction worth being wrong\nin, and the one the comment already claimed.\n\nThe /df read applied whatever landed last. The read the Images tab opens\nwith is often still in flight when a prune finishes, and it is an\naccount of the disk from before the prune ran; landing second it put the\npre-prune total and its badges back, so the prune read as having done\nnothing. Reads are sequenced now, and the effect retires the sequence on\nteardown as well as aborting — the prune''s own read carries no signal,\nso the abort alone would not stop it answering for an instance or tab\nthe operator has left. Covered by a test that resolves the two reads in\nreverse.\n\nThe prune cache test named the disk usage in its title and only\nexercised the image list; it reads /system/df either side of the prune\nnow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019FmoVDLow4N1mo8qwcmVZr\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNo4oABs\n32Rt7nQPHEwWc/wA5njbiTinUHSYy07T69/jb3zPf4BnTM6FcvjAZyuraXN4/uFJvG7TppAbT8EW\nxwM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T08:09:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/83181b2c23c9fe3816a2c0002c84ed0d3d74aeb7","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDgzMTgxYjJjMjNjOWZlMzgxNmEyYzAwMDJjODRlZDBkM2Q3NGFlYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/48d156dc153ca24488d4b8c69ad762b3bab431fc","sha":"48d156dc153ca24488d4b8c69ad762b3bab431fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/48d156dc153ca24488d4b8c69ad762b3bab431fc"}],"sha":"83181b2c23c9fe3816a2c0002c84ed0d3d74aeb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/83181b2c23c9fe3816a2c0002c84ed0d3d74aeb7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/3d56bd5a8fdf9b0412837fe91d9c42a03418b52f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T06:44:46Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T06:44:46Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Take the forwarded scheme as the only one, not one of two\n\nCrossing every scheme with every host accepted an origin the proxy had\nalready contradicted. Where TLS ends at nginx, `req.protocol` is http while\nX-Forwarded-Proto says https, and the cross product offered\nhttp://boat.example alongside https://boat.example. A browser too old to\nsend Sec-Fetch-Site, on a page served at that plain-http address — which\nanyone sharing the marina wifi can serve, there being no certificate to\nforge — was then treated as the admin UI.\n\nThe scheme is now single: the forwarded one where a proxy states it,\notherwise the one the request arrived on. A request that came directly\ncarries no forwarding headers, so there is nothing to prefer over what\narrived. Hosts stay a set, because a proxy commonly names the browser''s\naddress in one header and the internal one in the other and both spell the\nsame server, and no scheme is invented for them.\n\nFound by CodeRabbit on #48.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EpuhM9ZU7z6kcsvbBrvWTQ","tree":{"sha":"32def2ad56e920f2470bed0729ad04a0c7addf55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/32def2ad56e920f2470bed0729ad04a0c7addf55"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/3d56bd5a8fdf9b0412837fe91d9c42a03418b52f","verification":{"payload":"tree 32def2ad56e920f2470bed0729ad04a0c7addf55\nparent 4a07208f1ad9877454a998e7126ad6a1c09f7ec6\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787553886 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787553886 +0000\n\nTake the forwarded scheme as the only one, not one of two\n\nCrossing every scheme with every host accepted an origin the proxy had\nalready contradicted. Where TLS ends at nginx, `req.protocol` is http while\nX-Forwarded-Proto says https, and the cross product offered\nhttp://boat.example alongside https://boat.example. A browser too old to\nsend Sec-Fetch-Site, on a page served at that plain-http address — which\nanyone sharing the marina wifi can serve, there being no certificate to\nforge — was then treated as the admin UI.\n\nThe scheme is now single: the forwarded one where a proxy states it,\notherwise the one the request arrived on. A request that came directly\ncarries no forwarding headers, so there is nothing to prefer over what\narrived. Hosts stay a set, because a proxy commonly names the browser''s\naddress in one header and the internal one in the other and both spell the\nsame server, and no scheme is invented for them.\n\nFound by CodeRabbit on #48.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EpuhM9ZU7z6kcsvbBrvWTQ\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAEgF4Gv\nN1+ELRjL8yjCFrSQjSp/JqNksC9S2OGJUu/8yweWOZRIf1s5rfmMckM0eRrVQsDMujP789nKpEKc\nyAA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T06:44:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/3d56bd5a8fdf9b0412837fe91d9c42a03418b52f","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDNkNTZiZDVhOGZkZjliMDQxMjgzN2ZlOTFkOWM0MmEwMzQxOGI1MmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/4a07208f1ad9877454a998e7126ad6a1c09f7ec6","sha":"4a07208f1ad9877454a998e7126ad6a1c09f7ec6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/4a07208f1ad9877454a998e7126ad6a1c09f7ec6"}],"sha":"3d56bd5a8fdf9b0412837fe91d9c42a03418b52f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/3d56bd5a8fdf9b0412837fe91d9c42a03418b52f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/4a07208f1ad9877454a998e7126ad6a1c09f7ec6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T05:55:19Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T05:55:19Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Let a write through when a reverse proxy is in front of Signal K\n\nEvery mutating route was refused with 403 behind nginx: the guard compared\nthe browser''s Origin against `${req.protocol}://${req.get(''host'')}`, which\nis the address of the last hop. The browser used\nhttps://boat.example:4443; what arrived said http://127.0.0.1:3000, so the\nadmin UI''s own environment picker, container buttons and stack deploys were\ntreated as another site.\n\nSec-Fetch-Site now decides whenever the browser sends one. It is the\nbrowser''s verdict about the address the page was really loaded from, so no\nproxy can spoil it, and it cannot be forged by page script. The Origin\ncomparison stays as the fallback for browsers too old to send one (Safari\nbefore 16.4, Firefox before 90), widened to count the forwarded address as\nours: X-Forwarded-Proto, X-Forwarded-Host, X-Forwarded-Port and the RFC\n7239 Forwarded header, with ports the scheme implies normalised away.\nThose headers are not CORS-safelisted, so a cross-site fetch cannot add\none without a preflight Signal K never answers.\n\nA cross-site write is still refused, and a refusal now names both addresses\nthrough app.debug, so a proxy missing a header is visible on the Log page\nrather than only as a 403 the page is not allowed to read.\n\nThe README gains a \"Behind a reverse proxy\" section: the headers this check\nneeds, the WebSocket upgrade the console needs, and the buffering the live\nlog stream needs, with a worked nginx block.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EpuhM9ZU7z6kcsvbBrvWTQ","tree":{"sha":"88085a62cc298ed320de06c05a2ace34c9b5f574","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/88085a62cc298ed320de06c05a2ace34c9b5f574"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/4a07208f1ad9877454a998e7126ad6a1c09f7ec6","verification":{"payload":"tree 88085a62cc298ed320de06c05a2ace34c9b5f574\nparent c97bb6e824901ad15f4e925de5ff6c7a6463f0ed\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787550919 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787550919 +0000\n\nLet a write through when a reverse proxy is in front of Signal K\n\nEvery mutating route was refused with 403 behind nginx: the guard compared\nthe browser''s Origin against `${req.protocol}://${req.get(''host'')}`, which\nis the address of the last hop. The browser used\nhttps://boat.example:4443; what arrived said http://127.0.0.1:3000, so the\nadmin UI''s own environment picker, container buttons and stack deploys were\ntreated as another site.\n\nSec-Fetch-Site now decides whenever the browser sends one. It is the\nbrowser''s verdict about the address the page was really loaded from, so no\nproxy can spoil it, and it cannot be forged by page script. The Origin\ncomparison stays as the fallback for browsers too old to send one (Safari\nbefore 16.4, Firefox before 90), widened to count the forwarded address as\nours: X-Forwarded-Proto, X-Forwarded-Host, X-Forwarded-Port and the RFC\n7239 Forwarded header, with ports the scheme implies normalised away.\nThose headers are not CORS-safelisted, so a cross-site fetch cannot add\none without a preflight Signal K never answers.\n\nA cross-site write is still refused, and a refusal now names both addresses\nthrough app.debug, so a proxy missing a header is visible on the Log page\nrather than only as a 403 the page is not allowed to read.\n\nThe README gains a \"Behind a reverse proxy\" section: the headers this check\nneeds, the WebSocket upgrade the console needs, and the buffering the live\nlog stream needs, with a worked nginx block.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EpuhM9ZU7z6kcsvbBrvWTQ\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJqU0BsV\nBliDaNk6tz/WT+bjV51xkNJrX/j3+JzD5uzMAQvvSLEB5CI5IuDf0bt/oWrs20jnC71M7eaKKAEv\nTQU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T05:55:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/4a07208f1ad9877454a998e7126ad6a1c09f7ec6","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDRhMDcyMDhmMWFkOTg3NzQ1NGE5OThlNzEyNmFkNmExYzA5ZjdlYzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/c97bb6e824901ad15f4e925de5ff6c7a6463f0ed","sha":"c97bb6e824901ad15f4e925de5ff6c7a6463f0ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/c97bb6e824901ad15f4e925de5ff6c7a6463f0ed"}],"sha":"4a07208f1ad9877454a998e7126ad6a1c09f7ec6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/4a07208f1ad9877454a998e7126ad6a1c09f7ec6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/48d156dc153ca24488d4b8c69ad762b3bab431fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T21:57:06Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T21:57:06Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Let an operator reclaim image space, and leave volumes and networks alone\n\nA season of redeploys on a Raspberry Pi fills the SD card with layers\nnothing can be deployed from, and a full card takes Signal K down with\nit. Until now the panel could show that happening and do nothing about\nit: images, volumes and networks were all read-only.\n\nImages stop being. The tab gains a per-row Delete and a Reclaim space\nbutton, both behind \"Allow destructive operations\", and a summary line\nsaying what the images cost and what a prune would free. Those two\nfigures come from Docker''s own /system/df arithmetic rather than a sum\nof the row sizes — two images built on one base share those layers, and\nadding both counts them twice. That read is made when the tab opens and\nafter a prune, deliberately not on the ten-second poll: it walks the\nlayer store, which is seconds of work each time.\n\nA prune removes untagged layers by default. A checkbox widens it to\nevery image no container is using, off by default for the reason\nremoveVolumes is: that set includes the previous tag of anything\nrecently updated, and getting one back means pulling it again over\nwhatever connection the boat has.\n\nNothing is forced. Docker refuses to remove an image any container\nreferences, stopped ones included, and that refusal is what keeps the\nimage Signal K itself runs from out of reach — the plugin never has to\nwork out which one that is. Forcing would step over exactly that guard.\n\nVolumes and networks stay read-only, and the code now says why: a\ndeleted volume is the one loss nothing in the panel can undo, and a\nnetwork detached from a running container leaves it reporting \"running\"\nwhile being unreachable, with a shell on the host as the way out. An\nimage is the one of the three that can be fetched again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EwBTVqWrStTo4Hy2TYQL88","tree":{"sha":"ce8b1466daeffe339ca7e057cd81b852258d0f2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/ce8b1466daeffe339ca7e057cd81b852258d0f2c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/48d156dc153ca24488d4b8c69ad762b3bab431fc","verification":{"payload":"tree ce8b1466daeffe339ca7e057cd81b852258d0f2c\nparent c97bb6e824901ad15f4e925de5ff6c7a6463f0ed\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787522226 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787522226 +0000\n\nLet an operator reclaim image space, and leave volumes and networks alone\n\nA season of redeploys on a Raspberry Pi fills the SD card with layers\nnothing can be deployed from, and a full card takes Signal K down with\nit. Until now the panel could show that happening and do nothing about\nit: images, volumes and networks were all read-only.\n\nImages stop being. The tab gains a per-row Delete and a Reclaim space\nbutton, both behind \"Allow destructive operations\", and a summary line\nsaying what the images cost and what a prune would free. Those two\nfigures come from Docker''s own /system/df arithmetic rather than a sum\nof the row sizes — two images built on one base share those layers, and\nadding both counts them twice. That read is made when the tab opens and\nafter a prune, deliberately not on the ten-second poll: it walks the\nlayer store, which is seconds of work each time.\n\nA prune removes untagged layers by default. A checkbox widens it to\nevery image no container is using, off by default for the reason\nremoveVolumes is: that set includes the previous tag of anything\nrecently updated, and getting one back means pulling it again over\nwhatever connection the boat has.\n\nNothing is forced. Docker refuses to remove an image any container\nreferences, stopped ones included, and that refusal is what keeps the\nimage Signal K itself runs from out of reach — the plugin never has to\nwork out which one that is. Forcing would step over exactly that guard.\n\nVolumes and networks stay read-only, and the code now says why: a\ndeleted volume is the one loss nothing in the panel can undo, and a\nnetwork detached from a running container leaves it reporting \"running\"\nwhile being unreachable, with a shell on the host as the way out. An\nimage is the one of the three that can be fetched again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EwBTVqWrStTo4Hy2TYQL88\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMRi1QJY\nrDZbHJV9WZ2ZWObUAXIEMv5KvSKRljWDD1qR5BdlMCnEnMsQB8ZJvT3tvgYa55RfqYlFxx8SmFNu\n6gQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T21:57:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"h