b5e244fe80c23","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGExMWViNGE1MzZkNzc2ZGUwNjAzMmRjMGVhNWI1ZTI0NGZlODBjMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/181529306e415190254f77fbe7698db90e6c18cf","sha":"181529306e415190254f77fbe7698db90e6c18cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/181529306e415190254f77fbe7698db90e6c18cf"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/02606050379bc60b869d1272e12a5297b1051d97","sha":"02606050379bc60b869d1272e12a5297b1051d97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/02606050379bc60b869d1272e12a5297b1051d97"}],"sha":"a11eb4a536d776de06032dc0ea5b5e244fe80c23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/a11eb4a536d776de06032dc0ea5b5e244fe80c23"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/02606050379bc60b869d1272e12a5297b1051d97/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:51:55Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:51:55Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Address the review: allowlist typos, inert styling, and weak tests\n\nFrom CodeRabbit''s review of this PR. Two of its findings — the request\ndeadline and the unpinned actions — were already fixed in e2d613d.\n\nA PUT allowlist naming an instance that does not exist was accepted\nsilently. Since the allowlist is only consulted while it has entries, a\nsingle typo refused every container with nothing said. The name is now\nchecked and reported. I did not take the suggested repair of skipping the\nentry: an allowlist whose last bad entry is dropped becomes empty, and an\nempty allowlist allows everything, so skipping turns a typo into an open\ndoor. Kept, the entry goes on matching nothing and the operator is told\nwhy.\n\nGatedButton lost its visual inert state. Dropping the native `disabled`\nattribute to keep the control focusable also dropped Bootstrap''s dimming,\nso an inert button looked identical to a live one and a sighted operator\npressed it for nothing — trading one accessibility problem for another.\nIt now carries the `disabled` class, with pointer events restored so the\ntooltip still works.\n\nA new stack''s dirty check looked at the compose file and the repository\nURL only, so an operator who had filled in just the environment rows lost\nthem to Close without being asked.\n\ndocs/plan.md still said `off` polls nothing at all; it polls when a\nwatchdog is configured or PUT control is on, and drops the values.\n\nFour tests could not fail the way they were written: the cache race let\nthe replacement load resolve before the superseded one, so it passed even\nif stale cleanup deleted the newer entry; the duplicate-instance test\ncompared names that both normalise to the same string, so keeping the\nwrong row passed; FakeSocket swallowed an ''error'' with no listener, which\nis the one thing a real ws socket will not do, so the test could not see\na missing pre-relay handler; and four suites closed their MockAgent\nwithout restoring undici''s global dispatcher.\n\nAlso folds the two copies of the stack-control refusal into one exported\nconstant, so the panel and the row buttons cannot come to explain the\nsame switch differently.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86","tree":{"sha":"e97bfadbec19612a40cf1dfe238ae978c77ad911","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/e97bfadbec19612a40cf1dfe238ae978c77ad911"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/02606050379bc60b869d1272e12a5297b1051d97","verification":{"payload":"tree e97bfadbec19612a40cf1dfe238ae978c77ad911\nparent e2d613d8efbefa67353a36065386b3cc856d2cde\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787514715 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787514715 +0000\n\nAddress the review: allowlist typos, inert styling, and weak tests\n\nFrom CodeRabbit''s review of this PR. Two of its findings — the request\ndeadline and the unpinned actions — were already fixed in e2d613d.\n\nA PUT allowlist naming an instance that does not exist was accepted\nsilently. Since the allowlist is only consulted while it has entries, a\nsingle typo refused every container with nothing said. The name is now\nchecked and reported. I did not take the suggested repair of skipping the\nentry: an allowlist whose last bad entry is dropped becomes empty, and an\nempty allowlist allows everything, so skipping turns a typo into an open\ndoor. Kept, the entry goes on matching nothing and the operator is told\nwhy.\n\nGatedButton lost its visual inert state. Dropping the native `disabled`\nattribute to keep the control focusable also dropped Bootstrap''s dimming,\nso an inert button looked identical to a live one and a sighted operator\npressed it for nothing — trading one accessibility problem for another.\nIt now carries the `disabled` class, with pointer events restored so the\ntooltip still works.\n\nA new stack''s dirty check looked at the compose file and the repository\nURL only, so an operator who had filled in just the environment rows lost\nthem to Close without being asked.\n\ndocs/plan.md still said `off` polls nothing at all; it polls when a\nwatchdog is configured or PUT control is on, and drops the values.\n\nFour tests could not fail the way they were written: the cache race let\nthe replacement load resolve before the superseded one, so it passed even\nif stale cleanup deleted the newer entry; the duplicate-instance test\ncompared names that both normalise to the same string, so keeping the\nwrong row passed; FakeSocket swallowed an ''error'' with no listener, which\nis the one thing a real ws socket will not do, so the test could not see\na missing pre-relay handler; and four suites closed their MockAgent\nwithout restoring undici''s global dispatcher.\n\nAlso folds the two copies of the stack-control refusal into one exported\nconstant, so the panel and the row buttons cannot come to explain the\nsame switch differently.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNX9pf39\nnxtW46IsGoexFRDnPnEkEYRDMK7mEEHk4GlgavBEMh1TIi/K7PiFnBsGVqbK0Cj5EpFCz3tmPbhu\nkAc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T19:51:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/02606050379bc60b869d1272e12a5297b1051d97","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDAyNjA2MDUwMzc5YmM2MGI4NjlkMTI3MmUxMmE1Mjk3YjEwNTFkOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/e2d613d8efbefa67353a36065386b3cc856d2cde","sha":"e2d613d8efbefa67353a36065386b3cc856d2cde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/e2d613d8efbefa67353a36065386b3cc856d2cde"}],"sha":"02606050379bc60b869d1272e12a5297b1051d97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/02606050379bc60b869d1272e12a5297b1051d97"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/e2d613d8efbefa67353a36065386b3cc856d2cde/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:46:35Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:46:35Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Keep the request deadline armed until the body has been read\n\nfetch resolves when the headers arrive, not when the body does. The\ndeadline was released in a finally around the fetch alone, so\nresponse.json() then ran with no deadline at all: a server that answered\nand stalled mid-body held the row''s buttons disabled with no error and no\nway back — precisely the failure the deadline was added to prevent. The\nsame defect class this branch fixes in the Portainer client, where the\nbody reads sat outside the guarded region.\n\nThe request now runs inside one try whose finally releases the deadline\nafter the body has been consumed, and a deadline that fires during the\nbody read is reported as the timeout it is rather than as a parse\nfailure. A caller''s own abort is still passed through untouched.\n\nFound by CodeRabbit on this PR. The regression test hangs for the full\ndeadline and fails without the fix; the existing \"never answers\" test\npasses either way, which is why it did not catch this.\n\nAlso pins actions/checkout and actions/setup-node to commit SHAs, which\nCodeRabbit raised alongside it. The reusable workflow was already pinned\nbecause it runs arbitrary steps against this repo with the token; these\ntwo are first-party but cost nothing to pin, and the github-actions\ndependabot entry added here keeps all three current.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86","tree":{"sha":"5806937ece595b03d8b3ac0efa60c026e34740e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/5806937ece595b03d8b3ac0efa60c026e34740e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/e2d613d8efbefa67353a36065386b3cc856d2cde","verification":{"payload":"tree 5806937ece595b03d8b3ac0efa60c026e34740e0\nparent e4ae27132184cd2822b2ac2553ebc3ced68176dd\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787514395 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787514395 +0000\n\nKeep the request deadline armed until the body has been read\n\nfetch resolves when the headers arrive, not when the body does. The\ndeadline was released in a finally around the fetch alone, so\nresponse.json() then ran with no deadline at all: a server that answered\nand stalled mid-body held the row''s buttons disabled with no error and no\nway back — precisely the failure the deadline was added to prevent. The\nsame defect class this branch fixes in the Portainer client, where the\nbody reads sat outside the guarded region.\n\nThe request now runs inside one try whose finally releases the deadline\nafter the body has been consumed, and a deadline that fires during the\nbody read is reported as the timeout it is rather than as a parse\nfailure. A caller''s own abort is still passed through untouched.\n\nFound by CodeRabbit on this PR. The regression test hangs for the full\ndeadline and fails without the fix; the existing \"never answers\" test\npasses either way, which is why it did not catch this.\n\nAlso pins actions/checkout and actions/setup-node to commit SHAs, which\nCodeRabbit raised alongside it. The reusable workflow was already pinned\nbecause it runs arbitrary steps against this repo with the token; these\ntwo are first-party but cost nothing to pin, and the github-actions\ndependabot entry added here keeps all three current.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIHYYOPp\nQeo1AWVATZOM2vAiIUHt4PFf6Yo38zYoHayc2Htbpmtr9bbzR2EYh47yrDP/ML5h02YWzBIRUeJk\nKQs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T19:46:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/e2d613d8efbefa67353a36065386b3cc856d2cde","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGUyZDYxM2Q4ZWZiZWZhNjczNTNhMzYwNjUzODZiM2NjODU2ZDJjZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/e4ae27132184cd2822b2ac2553ebc3ced68176dd","sha":"e4ae27132184cd2822b2ac2553ebc3ced68176dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/e4ae27132184cd2822b2ac2553ebc3ced68176dd"}],"sha":"e2d613d8efbefa67353a36065386b3cc856d2cde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/e2d613d8efbefa67353a36065386b3cc856d2cde"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/e4ae27132184cd2822b2ac2553ebc3ced68176dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:39:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:39:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Ship two screenshots, and point the README''s images at GitHub\n\nSix screenshots put 1.36 MB of PNG into every install, on boats that\noften pay for the bytes. Two is enough for the App Store listing — the\nContainers tab as the hero and the configuration page — and they are the\ntwo the store entry already named.\n\nThe README''s other ten images do not need to be in the package at all.\nThey were only ever readable on GitHub, since docs/ has never been in\nfiles, so its relative links were already broken for anyone reading the\nREADME from npm. Pointing all twelve at raw.githubusercontent means they\nrender on npm and in the App Store description as well as on GitHub, and\nnothing but the two store screenshots has to ship.\n\nPackage: 1.5 MB to 674 kB.\n\nThe two that remain are still referenced by package-relative path, which\nis what src/appstore/cdn.ts resolves against the published tarball — an\nabsolute URL there would not work, which is why the README and the store\nentry point at the same files two different ways.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86","tree":{"sha":"30462dcd650e356007fbaae70c385db83355ec18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/30462dcd650e356007fbaae70c385db83355ec18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/e4ae27132184cd2822b2ac2553ebc3ced68176dd","verification":{"payload":"tree 30462dcd650e356007fbaae70c385db83355ec18\nparent 4dd7f92a713a7874ec48a94cd8a02ed5c23c2ccd\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787513982 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787513982 +0000\n\nShip two screenshots, and point the README''s images at GitHub\n\nSix screenshots put 1.36 MB of PNG into every install, on boats that\noften pay for the bytes. Two is enough for the App Store listing — the\nContainers tab as the hero and the configuration page — and they are the\ntwo the store entry already named.\n\nThe README''s other ten images do not need to be in the package at all.\nThey were only ever readable on GitHub, since docs/ has never been in\nfiles, so its relative links were already broken for anyone reading the\nREADME from npm. Pointing all twelve at raw.githubusercontent means they\nrender on npm and in the App Store description as well as on GitHub, and\nnothing but the two store screenshots has to ship.\n\nPackage: 1.5 MB to 674 kB.\n\nThe two that remain are still referenced by package-relative path, which\nis what src/appstore/cdn.ts resolves against the published tarball — an\nabsolute URL there would not work, which is why the README and the store\nentry point at the same files two different ways.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP9bKQ2r\nW+czyQGLN+WZJzt/y5Lo9znQe2vM6bYQrc1QgC+CVcGq0K9IvinrZirQiolSfGaRcwi5A4Zu50eM\nbQE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T19:39:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/e4ae27132184cd2822b2ac2553ebc3ced68176dd","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGU0YWUyNzEzMjE4NGNkMjgyMmIyYWMyNTUzZWJjM2NlZDY4MTc2ZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/4dd7f92a713a7874ec48a94cd8a02ed5c23c2ccd","sha":"4dd7f92a713a7874ec48a94cd8a02ed5c23c2ccd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/4dd7f92a713a7874ec48a94cd8a02ed5c23c2ccd"}],"sha":"e4ae27132184cd2822b2ac2553ebc3ced68176dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/e4ae27132184cd2822b2ac2553ebc3ced68176dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/4dd7f92a713a7874ec48a94cd8a02ed5c23c2ccd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:29:11Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:30:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Correct the documentation where it contradicted the code\n\nThe README described a stack-delete dialog offering volumes as a separate\nunticked choice. The dialog says the opposite, and the facade refuses to\nsend such a flag on purpose, because Portainer CE''s stack delete takes no\nvolume parameter — so a reader deleted a stack believing they had been\ngiven the option to take the data with it.\n\nIt also documented the Portainer container''s path as containers.portainer\nfive lines after telling the reader to start it with docker compose, when\ncompose labels win over container_name and the real key is\n<project>_portainer; promised that telemetry \"off\" polls nothing, when\nPUT control is on by default and PUT paths are discovered by the poll;\nsaid the Console button is disabled while control is off when it is\nabsent; listed container actions without pause and resume and got the\nconfirmation rule wrong; and claimed every refusal is logged, which is\ntrue of the facade and not of the PUT path.\n\nCHANGELOG said nothing had been published to npm. 0.1.0 is published, and\nis the release that does not load; it now says so, and the file gained\nthe release section and link references its Keep a Changelog headings\nimplied.\n\nplan.md claimed the facade requires an admin principal for mutations,\nwhich is guidance overstating what the code enforces. It also documented\nthree routes, two client methods, five delta paths, a telemetry option\nand a typed confirmation that were never built, and a configuration\nschema a generation out of date, while omitting eight routes that exist.\nThose are marked as not built rather than deleted, since it is a plan.\n\nAdds what a reader could not otherwise discover: that PUT paths appear\nonly after the first poll, that the watchdog needs two consecutive failed\npolls, the id-prefix minimum, the interval and timeout bounds, the body\nsize cap, and stack-name self-protection. Adds credential scoping advice,\nsince a Portainer token inherits its owner''s privileges and the README\npreviously said only that it stays on the server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86","tree":{"sha":"1340fb8c521a38b0d29497d3f769d6ec0d312ff7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/1340fb8c521a38b0d29497d3f769d6ec0d312ff7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/4dd7f92a713a7874ec48a94cd8a02ed5c23c2ccd","verification":{"payload":"tree 1340fb8c521a38b0d29497d3f769d6ec0d312ff7\nparent 857253053ed249f62274ae09c5e24cf896919390\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787513351 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787513410 +0000\n\nCorrect the documentation where it contradicted the code\n\nThe README described a stack-delete dialog offering volumes as a separate\nunticked choice. The dialog says the opposite, and the facade refuses to\nsend such a flag on purpose, because Portainer CE''s stack delete takes no\nvolume parameter — so a reader deleted a stack believing they had been\ngiven the option to take the data with it.\n\nIt also documented the Portainer container''s path as containers.portainer\nfive lines after telling the reader to start it with docker compose, when\ncompose labels win over container_name and the real key is\n<project>_portainer; promised that telemetry \"off\" polls nothing, when\nPUT control is on by default and PUT paths are discovered by the poll;\nsaid the Console button is disabled while control is off when it is\nabsent; listed container actions without pause and resume and got the\nconfirmation rule wrong; and claimed every refusal is logged, which is\ntrue of the facade and not of the PUT path.\n\nCHANGELOG said nothing had been published to npm. 0.1.0 is published, and\nis the release that does not load; it now says so, and the file gained\nthe release section and link references its Keep a Changelog headings\nimplied.\n\nplan.md claimed the facade requires an admin principal for mutations,\nwhich is guidance overstating what the code enforces. It also documented\nthree routes, two client methods, five delta paths, a telemetry option\nand a typed confirmation that were never built, and a configuration\nschema a generation out of date, while omitting eight routes that exist.\nThose are marked as not built rather than deleted, since it is a plan.\n\nAdds what a reader could not otherwise discover: that PUT paths appear\nonly after the first poll, that the watchdog needs two consecutive failed\npolls, the id-prefix minimum, the interval and timeout bounds, the body\nsize cap, and stack-name self-protection. Adds credential scoping advice,\nsince a Portainer token inherits its owner''s privileges and the README\npreviously said only that it stays on the server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMs7tC+w\nna5SBIYEu8mKkwLzM4vR815RPneYgmpenUqrIJDzBXIB8zcAs+nt+i3ISgDsNXUuLlVdmFKJ6WkH\nFwA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T19:31:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/4dd7f92a713a7874ec48a94cd8a02ed5c23c2ccd","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDRkZDdmOTJhNzEzYTc4NzRlYzQ4YTk0Y2Q4YTAyZWQ1YzIzYzJjY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/857253053ed249f62274ae09c5e24cf896919390","sha":"857253053ed249f62274ae09c5e24cf896919390","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/857253053ed249f62274ae09c5e24cf896919390"}],"sha":"4dd7f92a713a7874ec48a94cd8a02ed5c23c2ccd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/4dd7f92a713a7874ec48a94cd8a02ed5c23c2ccd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/857253053ed249f62274ae09c5e24cf896919390/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:28:55Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:30:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Close the gaps that let a broken package ship\n\nCI could not have caught the express defect, so the most valuable change\nhere is a job that packs the tarball, installs it into an empty directory\nwith --omit=dev, and requires it. That is the only check that looks like\na real user''s install; the existing integration job installs beside\nsignalk-server, where Node finds express hoisted.\n\nLint could not fail a PR either: the reusable workflow has no\nlint-command input and runs npm run lint --if-present with\ncontinue-on-error, so no-explicit-any was enforced only at publish time\non a maintainer''s machine. There is now a local job that gates it.\n\nType-aware linting was off entirely — recommended rather than\nrecommendedTypeChecked, with no project service — so no-floating-promises\nand no-misused-promises were unavailable across a codebase that is almost\nentirely async HTTP and WebSocket relaying. Enabled, with the existing\nfindings staged as warnings so the gate is honest about what it enforces\ntoday rather than blocking on a bulk cleanup.\n\nThe plugin build compiled with the DOM lib, so window and document\ntypechecked in server code and would have thrown at runtime; it now\nbuilds against ES2022 and node types only, which is why logframes imports\nTextDecoder from node:util rather than taking it from the global scope.\n\nnpm pack on an unbuilt tree silently produced a five-file tarball with no\ndist while main still pointed into it, so prepack now builds. xterm was a\nruntime dependency but is bundled, costing every install ~6 MB it never\nloads. @types/express was v5 against an Express 4 host; @types/node\nfloated to 26 against engines >=22.\n\nThe reusable workflow was referenced at @master, so an unreviewed push\nupstream changed what runs here; it is pinned to a SHA, with dependabot\nadded to bump it. Also: permissions and concurrency on the caller, chunk\nfilenames carry a content hash so a cached chunk cannot be served against\na new remoteEntry, lint and format now cover the whole tree, the dead\n.npmignore is gone, and the screenshot tool refuses a non-loopback server\nrather than silently rewriting a real boat''s plugin configuration.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86","tree":{"sha":"38c92777c7a80c7e0e776af7305d62117491c859","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/38c92777c7a80c7e0e776af7305d62117491c859"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/857253053ed249f62274ae09c5e24cf896919390","verification":{"payload":"tree 38c92777c7a80c7e0e776af7305d62117491c859\nparent cde01976760854031885483f4b5c0c0da1df0c61\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787513335 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787513410 +0000\n\nClose the gaps that let a broken package ship\n\nCI could not have caught the express defect, so the most valuable change\nhere is a job that packs the tarball, installs it into an empty directory\nwith --omit=dev, and requires it. That is the only check that looks like\na real user''s install; the existing integration job installs beside\nsignalk-server, where Node finds express hoisted.\n\nLint could not fail a PR either: the reusable workflow has no\nlint-command input and runs npm run lint --if-present with\ncontinue-on-error, so no-explicit-any was enforced only at publish time\non a maintainer''s machine. There is now a local job that gates it.\n\nType-aware linting was off entirely — recommended rather than\nrecommendedTypeChecked, with no project service — so no-floating-promises\nand no-misused-promises were unavailable across a codebase that is almost\nentirely async HTTP and WebSocket relaying. Enabled, with the existing\nfindings staged as warnings so the gate is honest about what it enforces\ntoday rather than blocking on a bulk cleanup.\n\nThe plugin build compiled with the DOM lib, so window and document\ntypechecked in server code and would have thrown at runtime; it now\nbuilds against ES2022 and node types only, which is why logframes imports\nTextDecoder from node:util rather than taking it from the global scope.\n\nnpm pack on an unbuilt tree silently produced a five-file tarball with no\ndist while main still pointed into it, so prepack now builds. xterm was a\nruntime dependency but is bundled, costing every install ~6 MB it never\nloads. @types/express was v5 against an Express 4 host; @types/node\nfloated to 26 against engines >=22.\n\nThe reusable workflow was referenced at @master, so an unreviewed push\nupstream changed what runs here; it is pinned to a SHA, with dependabot\nadded to bump it. Also: permissions and concurrency on the caller, chunk\nfilenames carry a content hash so a cached chunk cannot be served against\na new remoteEntry, lint and format now cover the whole tree, the dead\n.npmignore is gone, and the screenshot tool refuses a non-loopback server\nrather than silently rewriting a real boat''s plugin configuration.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNp13awM\nR9v6Wvw2bi+AG0V0gaQq3SRnCJX7gjxugIQLNLa8/P2xqNUnEuAALv6hZDKOFIKa62HK0z/1I+Dj\nZAE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T19:31:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/857253053ed249f62274ae09c5e24cf896919390","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDg1NzI1MzA1M2VkMjQ5ZjYyMjc0YWUwOWM1ZTI0Y2Y4OTY5MTkzOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/cde01976760854031885483f4b5c0c0da1df0c61","sha":"cde01976760854031885483f4b5c0c0da1df0c61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/cde01976760854031885483f4b5c0c0da1df0c61"}],"sha":"857253053ed249f62274ae09c5e24cf896919390","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/857253053ed249f62274ae09c5e24cf896919390"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/cde01976760854031885483f4b5c0c0da1df0c61/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:28:37Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:30:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Fix the panel''s data races and make it usable from a keyboard\n\nThe stack editor enabled Deploy after a failed file read: loading was\nfalse, the textarea was empty and editable, and typing made it look\nchanged — so an operator who read the error and typed a couple of lines\nto fix it replaced the stack''s real compose file with the fragment, with\nno way back from the panel.\n\nThe log pane keyed rows on the array index, and the buffer is capped, so\nonce it filled every arriving line shifted every row and React tore down\nand rebuilt all five thousand of them per line. Lines now carry a\nmonotonic sequence.\n\nA refused environment switch was erased by the next poll, because error\nwas a shared sink that load() cleared on success — leaving no banner, an\nunchanged selection, and every reason to think the switch had worked. It\nhas its own state now, as container and stack results already did. A\nstale /environments response could also repaint the previous instance''s\npicker over the current one, offering ids that belong to another server.\n\nAlso: a non-array environments body took the panel down with no way back;\n\"No environments\" appeared while the read was still in flight, so a\nfailure was indistinguishable from an empty result; stack stop and\nredeploy fired with no confirmation while stopping one container asks;\nremoving an environment-variable row moved the caret to a different\nvariable; Close discarded unsaved edits with no guard, contradicting the\ndeploy path that deliberately keeps the editor open on failure; a\nmutation with no timeout left a row disabled and silent when the link\ndropped; and formatBytes threw on a non-number, taking the table with it.\n\nAccessibility, which the panel''s own \"a disabled button explains itself\"\nprinciple depended on and did not deliver: the reason lived only in title\non a disabled button, which cannot be focused, so exactly the users who\ncannot hover could never read it. Unavailable controls are now focusable\nwith aria-disabled and a described reason. Dialogs restore focus on close\nand keep Tab inside them. The tab strip carries tablist semantics and\narrow-key selection instead of conveying the active tab by CSS class\nalone. stderr is no longer signalled by colour alone, async status\nregions announce, and following a log no longer narrates the whole buffer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86","tree":{"sha":"0e1ca3da5cc5819c6c3afa7d285268c2989f5095","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/0e1ca3da5cc5819c6c3afa7d285268c2989f5095"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/cde01976760854031885483f4b5c0c0da1df0c61","verification":{"payload":"tree 0e1ca3da5cc5819c6c3afa7d285268c2989f5095\nparent 710d0215344b392f87e7bbc83b2280c6013c1a31\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787513317 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787513410 +0000\n\nFix the panel''s data races and make it usable from a keyboard\n\nThe stack editor enabled Deploy after a failed file read: loading was\nfalse, the textarea was empty and editable, and typing made it look\nchanged — so an operator who read the error and typed a couple of lines\nto fix it replaced the stack''s real compose file with the fragment, with\nno way back from the panel.\n\nThe log pane keyed rows on the array index, and the buffer is capped, so\nonce it filled every arriving line shifted every row and React tore down\nand rebuilt all five thousand of them per line. Lines now carry a\nmonotonic sequence.\n\nA refused environment switch was erased by the next poll, because error\nwas a shared sink that load() cleared on success — leaving no banner, an\nunchanged selection, and every reason to think the switch had worked. It\nhas its own state now, as container and stack results already did. A\nstale /environments response could also repaint the previous instance''s\npicker over the current one, offering ids that belong to another server.\n\nAlso: a non-array environments body took the panel down with no way back;\n\"No environments\" appeared while the read was still in flight, so a\nfailure was indistinguishable from an empty result; stack stop and\nredeploy fired with no confirmation while stopping one container asks;\nremoving an environment-variable row moved the caret to a different\nvariable; Close discarded unsaved edits with no guard, contradicting the\ndeploy path that deliberately keeps the editor open on failure; a\nmutation with no timeout left a row disabled and silent when the link\ndropped; and formatBytes threw on a non-number, taking the table with it.\n\nAccessibility, which the panel''s own \"a disabled button explains itself\"\nprinciple depended on and did not deliver: the reason lived only in title\non a disabled button, which cannot be focused, so exactly the users who\ncannot hover could never read it. Unavailable controls are now focusable\nwith aria-disabled and a described reason. Dialogs restore focus on close\nand keep Tab inside them. The tab strip carries tablist semantics and\narrow-key selection instead of conveying the active tab by CSS class\nalone. stderr is no longer signalled by colour alone, async status\nregions announce, and following a log no longer narrates the whole buffer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEnDLPXd\nFkzeI+TbOwFur3Iz3+fYL5NBO8v+Hc50c+NMF5ONonCQnSq2ikmD0U3k6k05YAXivfW+9n/0ZTd1\nFQ8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T19:31:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/cde01976760854031885483f4b5c0c0da1df0c61","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGNkZTAxOTc2NzYwODU0MDMxODg1NDgzZjRiNWMwYzBkYTFkZjBjNjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/710d0215344b392f87e7bbc83b2280c6013c1a31","sha":"710d0215344b392f87e7bbc83b2280c6013c1a31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/710d0215344b392f87e7bbc83b2280c6013c1a31"}],"sha":"cde01976760854031885483f4b5c0c0da1df0c61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/cde01976760854031885483f4b5c0c0da1df0c61"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/710d0215344b392f87e7bbc83b2280c6013c1a31/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:29:47Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:30:02Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Harden configuration and narrow who may write\n\nnormalizeConfig validated every configured instance before it looked at\nwhich ones were enabled, so a single row that failed validation threw and\nstart() caught it into no registry, no poller, no PUT handlers and no\ndeltas — for the instances that were fine as well. Pressing \"+\" to\nprepare a second Portainer and saving before filling in the URL was\nenough to stop the boat''s own container telemetry and watchdog alarms.\nMarking the row disabled did not help, because it was validated anyway.\nInstances are now validated one at a time: disabled rows are skipped, an\nenabled row that fails is dropped and named in the plugin status, and the\nconfiguration fails only when nothing is left.\n\nThe other half is who may write. The REST facade is admin-only, because\nSignal K gates plugin routes; a Signal K PUT is not, because the server''s\nPUT security admits readwrite clients and an ActionHandler is handed\ncontext, path, value and a callback with no principal. So turning PUT\ncontrol on made every container writable by any readwrite device. The\nprincipal is not something this plugin can fix; the granularity is.\ncontrol.putContainers lists the containers a PUT may control — empty, the\ndefault, keeps today''s behaviour. An unlisted container gets no handler\nat all, so the narrowing does not depend on a refusal being reached, and\nit is re-checked at write time because Signal K cannot withdraw a handler\nit has already been given. Entries take a name, the published key or an\nid prefix, the same rule the watchdog accepts, which now lives in one\nplace so the two cannot drift.\n\nAlongside them, in the lifecycle and the facade:\n\n- lastHealth survived stop/start, and since the healthy branch is the\n  only thing that clears an error status, a restart begun while Portainer\n  was briefly down could leave the plugin showing \"No Portainer instance\n  reachable\" indefinitely.\n- The poller awaited every instance before publishing any of them,\n  despite the comment promising the opposite, so a slow shore server\n  delayed the boat''s own containers and its watchdog alarms by up to its\n  whole timeout. Each instance now publishes as it settles.\n- A start() that failed halfway left the registry, the console endpoint,\n  the tickets and the sessions behind; teardown is now shared with stop().\n- The SSE log relay ignored res.write() backpressure and never paused the\n  upstream, so a chatty container over a slow link grew the heap without\n  bound — the outcome the stream limits exist to prevent.\n- The console registered its session only after dialling Portainer, so\n  the browser''s opening resize always 404''d and every shell stayed at\n  80x24. connectWithWs could also hang forever, holding a permit.\n- Self-protection failed open when an inspect returned 200 with no Id,\n  and mutations ran against the caller''s reference rather than the\n  canonical id the guard had just resolved.\n- Stack and environment ids were read with Number(), so 0x3 addressed\n  stack 3 and true selected environment 1.\n- pathPrefix was the one unsanitised path segment.\n- A PUT to a container removed between the guard and the call reported\n  \"The plugin is not running\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86","tree":{"sha":"86c799e9775ed346493b5334e998bf47c90c9e34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/86c799e9775ed346493b5334e998bf47c90c9e34"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/710d0215344b392f87e7bbc83b2280c6013c1a31","verification":{"payload":"tree 86c799e9775ed346493b5334e998bf47c90c9e34\nparent 9c1d9dfc98c934d0b669e483674f95fe93b8f5d7\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787513387 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787513402 +0000\n\nHarden configuration and narrow who may write\n\nnormalizeConfig validated every configured instance before it looked at\nwhich ones were enabled, so a single row that failed validation threw and\nstart() caught it into no registry, no poller, no PUT handlers and no\ndeltas — for the instances that were fine as well. Pressing \"+\" to\nprepare a second Portainer and saving before filling in the URL was\nenough to stop the boat''s own container telemetry and watchdog alarms.\nMarking the row disabled did not help, because it was validated anyway.\nInstances are now validated one at a time: disabled rows are skipped, an\nenabled row that fails is dropped and named in the plugin status, and the\nconfiguration fails only when nothing is left.\n\nThe other half is who may write. The REST facade is admin-only, because\nSignal K gates plugin routes; a Signal K PUT is not, because the server''s\nPUT security admits readwrite clients and an ActionHandler is handed\ncontext, path, value and a callback with no principal. So turning PUT\ncontrol on made every container writable by any readwrite device. The\nprincipal is not something this plugin can fix; the granularity is.\ncontrol.putContainers lists the containers a PUT may control — empty, the\ndefault, keeps today''s behaviour. An unlisted container gets no handler\nat all, so the narrowing does not depend on a refusal being reached, and\nit is re-checked at write time because Signal K cannot withdraw a handler\nit has already been given. Entries take a name, the published key or an\nid prefix, the same rule the watchdog accepts, which now lives in one\nplace so the two cannot drift.\n\nAlongside them, in the lifecycle and the facade:\n\n- lastHealth survived stop/start, and since the healthy branch is the\n  only thing that clears an error status, a restart begun while Portainer\n  was briefly down could leave the plugin showing \"No Portainer instance\n  reachable\" indefinitely.\n- The poller awaited every instance before publishing any of them,\n  despite the comment promising the opposite, so a slow shore server\n  delayed the boat''s own containers and its watchdog alarms by up to its\n  whole timeout. Each instance now publishes as it settles.\n- A start() that failed halfway left the registry, the console endpoint,\n  the tickets and the sessions behind; teardown is now shared with stop().\n- The SSE log relay ignored res.write() backpressure and never paused the\n  upstream, so a chatty container over a slow link grew the heap without\n  bound — the outcome the stream limits exist to prevent.\n- The console registered its session only after dialling Portainer, so\n  the browser''s opening resize always 404''d and every shell stayed at\n  80x24. connectWithWs could also hang forever, holding a permit.\n- Self-protection failed open when an inspect returned 200 with no Id,\n  and mutations ran against the caller''s reference rather than the\n  canonical id the guard had just resolved.\n- Stack and environment ids were read with Number(), so 0x3 addressed\n  stack 3 and true selected environment 1.\n- pathPrefix was the one unsanitised path segment.\n- A PUT to a container removed between the guard and the call reported\n  \"The plugin is not running\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPoE/+zs\nrwvlCkviLFDMFd1sXnldYPrc9mw3zoZsM2WyD+gZJH7sbJVdj4pccoNlgCnbZl/OUccdN7HUjeSC\nWA0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T19:31:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/710d0215344b392f87e7bbc83b2280c6013c1a31","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDcxMGQwMjE1MzQ0YjM5MmY4N2U3YmJjODNiMjI4MGM2MDEzYzFhMzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/9c1d9dfc98c934d0b669e483674f95fe93b8f5d7","sha":"9c1d9dfc98c934d0b669e483674f95fe93b8f5d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/9c1d9dfc98c934d0b669e483674f95fe93b8f5d7"}],"sha":"710d0215344b392f87e7bbc83b2280c6013c1a31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/710d0215344b392f87e7bbc83b2280c6013c1a31"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/9c1d9dfc98c934d0b669e483674f95fe93b8f5d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:28:03Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:28:03Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Fix the Portainer client, the error model and the log demuxer\n\nA JWT renewal dropped the flag that makes Docker''s 304 (\"already in that\nstate\") a success, so the first Stop after a token refresh failed, and a\n304 with a JSON body reached the browser.\n\nStack writes were bounded by the 10-second read timeout, because the\nper-request timeoutMs no caller ever set was the only way to widen it. A\ndeploy that pulls a large image was reported unreachable while Portainer\ncompleted it, inviting a second deploy; stopContainer(id, 30) gave up at\n10s while Docker was still waiting out its grace period. Writes now have\ntheir own budget, and stop/restart outlive the grace they asked for.\n\nConcurrent 401s each cleared whatever token was in the slot, including\none a sibling had just refreshed, so a Portainer restart produced one\n/api/auth per in-flight request against a rate-limited endpoint. The\nclear is now conditional on the token still being the one that failed.\n\nPortainer''s own error sentence was read off the wire, redacted, capped\nand then never read again: .body was assigned and used nowhere, so a\nduplicate stack name said only \"failed with 409 — conflict\". It now\nreaches the operator. Transport failures were all diagnosed as TLS\nproblems, so a typo''d hostname advised supplying a CA certificate; they\nare now told apart by cause code, and the cause is preserved.\n\nThe log demuxer discarded a TTY container''s whole log when it was shorter\nthan a frame header, decoded a character split across two frames as two\nreplacement characters, trusted any frame length, and copied the entire\nremainder on every chunk. An undecided mode is now resolved from the byte\nshape, so short output renders while a truncated header is still withheld.\n\nContainer key disambiguation could collide with a key already taken, so\ntwo containers shared one Signal K path and one PUT handler and a write\nhit whichever Docker listed last. Cache invalidation served the\npre-invalidation result to anyone who joined an in-flight load. And\nredactValue reported any object appearing twice as \"[circular]\".\n\nSix test interceptors named /api/status where the client calls\n/api/system/status, so the version probe threw and was swallowed in every\nstack test; two client tests could not fail.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86","tree":{"sha":"1cf5e0cb72def60a95fca943cfc18cdad233bf49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/1cf5e0cb72def60a95fca943cfc18cdad233bf49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/9c1d9dfc98c934d0b669e483674f95fe93b8f5d7","verification":{"payload":"tree 1cf5e0cb72def60a95fca943cfc18cdad233bf49\nparent 88e9203a5f7c0f8dd0c476fbd61e68bb5e14d5d4\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787513283 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787513283 +0000\n\nFix the Portainer client, the error model and the log demuxer\n\nA JWT renewal dropped the flag that makes Docker''s 304 (\"already in that\nstate\") a success, so the first Stop after a token refresh failed, and a\n304 with a JSON body reached the browser.\n\nStack writes were bounded by the 10-second read timeout, because the\nper-request timeoutMs no caller ever set was the only way to widen it. A\ndeploy that pulls a large image was reported unreachable while Portainer\ncompleted it, inviting a second deploy; stopContainer(id, 30) gave up at\n10s while Docker was still waiting out its grace period. Writes now have\ntheir own budget, and stop/restart outlive the grace they asked for.\n\nConcurrent 401s each cleared whatever token was in the slot, including\none a sibling had just refreshed, so a Portainer restart produced one\n/api/auth per in-flight request against a rate-limited endpoint. The\nclear is now conditional on the token still being the one that failed.\n\nPortainer''s own error sentence was read off the wire, redacted, capped\nand then never read again: .body was assigned and used nowhere, so a\nduplicate stack name said only \"failed with 409 — conflict\". It now\nreaches the operator. Transport failures were all diagnosed as TLS\nproblems, so a typo''d hostname advised supplying a CA certificate; they\nare now told apart by cause code, and the cause is preserved.\n\nThe log demuxer discarded a TTY container''s whole log when it was shorter\nthan a frame header, decoded a character split across two frames as two\nreplacement characters, trusted any frame length, and copied the entire\nremainder on every chunk. An undecided mode is now resolved from the byte\nshape, so short output renders while a truncated header is still withheld.\n\nContainer key disambiguation could collide with a key already taken, so\ntwo containers shared one Signal K path and one PUT handler and a write\nhit whichever Docker listed last. Cache invalidation served the\npre-invalidation result to anyone who joined an in-flight load. And\nredactValue reported any object appearing twice as \"[circular]\".\n\nSix test interceptors named /api/status where the client calls\n/api/system/status, so the version probe threw and was swallowed in every\nstack test; two client tests could not fail.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAaW86So\nEAVAkVKjCDYYEIT4XE0DzSiQ1uEelwJNOLJVMUXlNJINzWhvnDNxKCnJQ0c8lGxRvqkEEsdk0teA\n3Qw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T19:31:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/9c1d9dfc98c934d0b669e483674f95fe93b8f5d7","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDljMWQ5ZGZjOThjOTM0ZDBiNjY5ZTQ4MzY3NGY5NWZlOTNiOGY1ZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/88e9203a5f7c0f8dd0c476fbd61e68bb5e14d5d4","sha":"88e9203a5f7c0f8dd0c476fbd61e68bb5e14d5d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/88e9203a5f7c0f8dd0c476fbd61e68bb5e14d5d4"}],"sha":"9c1d9dfc98c934d0b669e483674f95fe93b8f5d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/9c1d9dfc98c934d0b669e483674f95fe93b8f5d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/88e9203a5f7c0f8dd0c476fbd61e68bb5e14d5d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:27:27Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:27:45Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Make the published package loadable, and prove it stays that way\n\nsignalk-portainer@0.1.0 is on npm and does not load. The Signal K plugin\nregistry reports installs: true, loads: false, with\n\n  Cannot find module ''express''\n    - node_modules/signalk-portainer/dist/facade.js\n    - node_modules/signalk-portainer/dist/index.js\n\nfacade.ts imported express as a value, for express.json() alone, while\nexpress was declared only under devDependencies. tsc emitted a bare\nrequire(\"express\") and index.js pulls facade in at load, so a real\ninstall had nothing to resolve.\n\nEvery gate we had was structurally blind to it. jest compiles src/ inside\nthis repo, where express is a devDependency. TypeScript has no notion of\ndependencies vs devDependencies, so a value import and a type import look\nalike. npm pack checks files, never a require. And the reusable CI\nworkflow installs the tarball beside signalk-server, which depends on\nexpress, so Node''s upward module resolution finds it hoisted — the\nregistry installs into a clean prefix and does not.\n\nOnly .json() was ever used, so this drops the express value import for\nbody-parser, a real dependency. express stays a devDependency for its\ntypes. dist/ now requires only body-parser, undici, ws and node:*.\n\npackage.json cannot be split across commits, so it also carries the rest\nof the packaging work described in \"Close the gaps that let a broken\npackage ship\": xterm moved to devDependencies, @types/express pinned to\nthe major the host actually runs, @types/node pinned to engines, a\nprepack build, and the App Store screenshots. The CI job that proves the\ntarball loads is there too.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86","tree":{"sha":"633bd5ea62449c3cc9d87076953b8ef3595d647b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/633bd5ea62449c3cc9d87076953b8ef3595d647b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/88e9203a5f7c0f8dd0c476fbd61e68bb5e14d5d4","verification":{"payload":"tree 633bd5ea62449c3cc9d87076953b8ef3595d647b\nparent 181529306e415190254f77fbe7698db90e6c18cf\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787513247 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787513265 +0000\n\nMake the published package loadable, and prove it stays that way\n\nsignalk-portainer@0.1.0 is on npm and does not load. The Signal K plugin\nregistry reports installs: true, loads: false, with\n\n  Cannot find module ''express''\n    - node_modules/signalk-portainer/dist/facade.js\n    - node_modules/signalk-portainer/dist/index.js\n\nfacade.ts imported express as a value, for express.json() alone, while\nexpress was declared only under devDependencies. tsc emitted a bare\nrequire(\"express\") and index.js pulls facade in at load, so a real\ninstall had nothing to resolve.\n\nEvery gate we had was structurally blind to it. jest compiles src/ inside\nthis repo, where express is a devDependency. TypeScript has no notion of\ndependencies vs devDependencies, so a value import and a type import look\nalike. npm pack checks files, never a require. And the reusable CI\nworkflow installs the tarball beside signalk-server, which depends on\nexpress, so Node''s upward module resolution finds it hoisted — the\nregistry installs into a clean prefix and does not.\n\nOnly .json() was ever used, so this drops the express value import for\nbody-parser, a real dependency. express stays a devDependency for its\ntypes. dist/ now requires only body-parser, undici, ws and node:*.\n\npackage.json cannot be split across commits, so it also carries the rest\nof the packaging work described in \"Close the gaps that let a broken\npackage ship\": xterm moved to devDependencies, @types/express pinned to\nthe major the host actually runs, @types/node pinned to engines, a\nprepack build, and the App Store screenshots. The CI job that proves the\ntarball loads is there too.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018qZRRLBAgLVyVxJjaD2P86\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHs7HSfF\nB9UPtsBspWF82DQXJYKd5DD8jz2B34KxfYeSQKoYw8ljORXUpOyhWRM0eVHxy3l3S3luOSS11sOP\nCAU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T19:31:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/88e9203a5f7c0f8dd0c476fbd61e68bb5e14d5d4","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDg4ZTkyMDNhNWY3YzBmOGRkMGM0NzZmYmQ2MWU2OGJiNWUxNGQ1ZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/181529306e415190254f77fbe7698db90e6c18cf","sha":"181529306e415190254f77fbe7698db90e6c18cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/181529306e415190254f77fbe7698db90e6c18cf"}],"sha":"88e9203a5f7c0f8dd0c476fbd61e68bb5e14d5d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/88e9203a5f7c0f8dd0c476fbd61e68bb5e14d5d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://