:"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/bfc31aaa0dbeed1603657806597c180e0405dac7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T12:33:00Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T12:33:00Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Two documentation fixes from the review, and a sturdier stream teardown\n\nThe commented-out HTTP port would have published an unencrypted Portainer UI on\nevery interface if uncommented, one line under a comment explaining why the\nHTTPS one is bound to localhost. It now carries the same binding.\n\nThe tag paragraph called `lts` a pin. It is not: it moves to whatever the\ncurrent long-term release is, 2.39.6 today. It says so now, and names the exact\nversion or digest as what a machine that must come back identical needs.\n\nThe follow stream''s cleanup moves from the request to the response. The review\nreported that the request''s `close` fires early for a bodyless GET and cuts the\nstream short; on Node 22, this project''s floor, it does not — it fires when the\nclient disconnects, as the response''s does. The response is still the right\nthing to bind to, being what the interval writes to. Verified after the change:\na follow stream held open for seven seconds delivers its history and three live\nlines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NWDUpnG54LrxgomuLgHJNQ","tree":{"sha":"06d003a4c11e70b31f9b11f67af2090bd9292e51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/06d003a4c11e70b31f9b11f67af2090bd9292e51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/bfc31aaa0dbeed1603657806597c180e0405dac7","verification":{"payload":"tree 06d003a4c11e70b31f9b11f67af2090bd9292e51\nparent 390006c7fbd4471e2a51f85890d4c6c19e0ecc62\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787488380 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787488380 +0000\n\nTwo documentation fixes from the review, and a sturdier stream teardown\n\nThe commented-out HTTP port would have published an unencrypted Portainer UI on\nevery interface if uncommented, one line under a comment explaining why the\nHTTPS one is bound to localhost. It now carries the same binding.\n\nThe tag paragraph called `lts` a pin. It is not: it moves to whatever the\ncurrent long-term release is, 2.39.6 today. It says so now, and names the exact\nversion or digest as what a machine that must come back identical needs.\n\nThe follow stream''s cleanup moves from the request to the response. The review\nreported that the request''s `close` fires early for a bodyless GET and cuts the\nstream short; on Node 22, this project''s floor, it does not — it fires when the\nclient disconnects, as the response''s does. The response is still the right\nthing to bind to, being what the interval writes to. Verified after the change:\na follow stream held open for seven seconds delivers its history and three live\nlines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NWDUpnG54LrxgomuLgHJNQ\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF4ajf7M\ndG3OV5/98s46lvZeW47dzJhPuyODLsRLaAqVtydOn6mXnwL9ovVsFvsalfidPZn2d+fCauvb4HF3\ntgI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T12:33:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/bfc31aaa0dbeed1603657806597c180e0405dac7","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGJmYzMxYWFhMGRiZWVkMTYwMzY1NzgwNjU5N2MxODBlMDQwNWRhYzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/390006c7fbd4471e2a51f85890d4c6c19e0ecc62","sha":"390006c7fbd4471e2a51f85890d4c6c19e0ecc62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/390006c7fbd4471e2a51f85890d4c6c19e0ecc62"}],"sha":"bfc31aaa0dbeed1603657806597c180e0405dac7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits