red{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/c0c4bb42d619fc7b8f3ce49da0ec14c8b9065600","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGMwYzRiYjQyZDYxOWZjN2I4ZjNjZTQ5ZGEwZWMxNGM4YjkwNjU2MDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/177cc2aac7cdd509ca73309a0d31ab702077fbd0","sha":"177cc2aac7cdd509ca73309a0d31ab702077fbd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/177cc2aac7cdd509ca73309a0d31ab702077fbd0"}],"sha":"c0c4bb42d619fc7b8f3ce49da0ec14c8b9065600","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/c0c4bb42d619fc7b8f3ce49da0ec14c8b9065600"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/177cc2aac7cdd509ca73309a0d31ab702077fbd0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T12:16:52Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T12:16:52Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Show how to run Portainer itself, and why each line is what it is\n\nThe README asked for a Portainer address without ever saying how to have a\nPortainer. This adds the compose file, checked with `docker compose config`\nexactly as printed, and the four lines in it that are decisions rather than\nboilerplate: the LTS tag rather than latest, `./data` rather than `$PWD/data`,\n`unless-stopped` rather than `always`, and a port published to this machine\nrather than to the boat''s wifi.\n\nThe `$PWD` one is the trap worth the words: compose resolves a relative path\nagainst the compose file''s own directory, but `$PWD` against wherever the\ncommand ran, so `docker compose -f /opt/portainer/docker-compose.yml up -d`\nfrom a home directory puts Portainer''s database there — and the next run from\nelsewhere starts it with an empty one.\n\nAlso here: that the socket mount is root-equivalent control of the host, which\nis the reason this plugin''s destructive and self-management switches default\noff, and what to use as the address when Signal K is itself in a container.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NWDUpnG54LrxgomuLgHJNQ","tree":{"sha":"26dd7e1a9fa4a70617a2b9a32446d9b454416cbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/26dd7e1a9fa4a70617a2b9a32446d9b454416cbc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/177cc2aac7cdd509ca73309a0d31ab702077fbd0","verification":{"payload":"tree 26dd7e1a9fa4a70617a2b9a32446d9b454416cbc\nparent 14daadd71bd2b22cd070d9dd0bd047e669b48780\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787487412 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787487412 +0000\n\nShow how to run Portainer itself, and why each line is what it is\n\nThe README asked for a Portainer address without ever saying how to have a\nPortainer. This adds the compose file, checked with `docker compose config`\nexactly as printed, and the four lines in it that are decisions rather than\nboilerplate: the LTS tag rather than latest, `./data` rather than `$PWD/data`,\n`unless-stopped` rather than `always`, and a port published to this machine\nrather than to the boat''s wifi.\n\nThe `$PWD` one is the trap worth the words: compose resolves a relative path\nagainst the compose file''s own directory, but `$PWD` against wherever the\ncommand ran, so `docker compose -f /opt/portainer/docker-compose.yml up -d`\nfrom a home directory puts Portainer''s database there — and the next run from\nelsewhere starts it with an empty one.\n\nAlso here: that the socket mount is root-equivalent control of the host, which\nis the reason this plugin''s destructive and self-management switches default\noff, and what to use as the address when Signal K is itself in a container.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NWDUpnG54LrxgomuLgHJNQ\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDji6Ysb\nNK4ksiA0S0nl+5kTM3Pu2RgrL5B51qyBiWlAJCf0rLyHaJhJuNp2YayW/i44unmJy4S+NZMxPJUD\nsgc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T12:16:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://