aadd71bd2b22cd070d9dd0bd047e669b48780/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T12:08:43Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T12:08:43Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Say where the Instance selector in the screenshots comes from\n\nThe panel renders it only where more than one Portainer is configured, and the\nfixture configures two — so a reader with one Portainer, which is most of them,\nlooks at the header in these images and finds a control their own panel does\nnot have.\n\nNothing about the images changes; what changes is that the README now says so,\nwhere the reader meets it: in the note under the first screenshot, in the step\nthat adds a second server, and in the sentence describing what the panel is.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NWDUpnG54LrxgomuLgHJNQ","tree":{"sha":"4ba9cb0d066929c8c70697c8e26163207192f2f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/4ba9cb0d066929c8c70697c8e26163207192f2f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/14daadd71bd2b22cd070d9dd0bd047e669b48780","verification":{"payload":"tree 4ba9cb0d066929c8c70697c8e26163207192f2f2\nparent 219d7944d8a5bf870058ce9b991b178be7a1fdee\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787486923 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787486923 +0000\n\nSay where the Instance selector in the screenshots comes from\n\nThe panel renders it only where more than one Portainer is configured, and the\nfixture configures two — so a reader with one Portainer, which is most of them,\nlooks at the header in these images and finds a control their own panel does\nnot have.\n\nNothing about the images changes; what changes is that the README now says so,\nwhere the reader meets it: in the note under the first screenshot, in the step\nthat adds a second server, and in the sentence describing what the panel is.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NWDUpnG54LrxgomuLgHJNQ\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFOt9Stc\nsKLd6nk+/FGztNI+QxhdHvl6fp5HXi5JEpBdJTA+VAu+AiBBoRqkxaOvdIHrnpSTCubTdGY3MKAz\nogk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T12:08:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/14daadd71bd2b22cd070d9dd0bd047e669b48780","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDE0ZGFhZGQ3MWJkMmIyMmNkMDcwZDlkZDBiZDA0N2U2NjliNDg3ODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/219d7944d8a5bf870058ce9b991b178be7a1fdee","sha":"219d7944d8a5bf870058ce9b991b178be7a1fdee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/219d7944d8a5bf870058ce9b991b178be7a1fdee"}],"sha":"14daadd71bd2b22cd070d9dd0bd047e669b48780","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/14daadd71bd2b22cd070d9dd0bd047e669b48780"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/219d7944d8a5bf870058ce9b991b178be7a1fdee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T11:59:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T11:59:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Photograph the environment being chosen, not only the state after\n\nThe recent change is that a Portainer''s environment is chosen in the panel, by\npressing a row. The screenshots only had the after picture: a row already\ncarrying the \"selected\" badge, which is what the panel looks like once the\nquestion has been answered and never again.\n\nThe capture now answers it in front of the camera. It clears the choice through\nSignal K''s own plugin config API, shoots the first-run state — the notice\nsaying which Portainer this is and that a row has to be pressed, above three\nrows each offering Select — then presses the row and shoots what that leaves\nbehind. Two pictures of one thing, in the order an operator meets them, and\nrepeatable: without the clearing step the first state exists exactly once.\n\nClearing it costs the plugin an error, which its configuration page goes on\nshowing until it restarts, so the configuration shots moved after a save of the\noptions unchanged — which is that restart. The status line in them is the\nsteady state again rather than the tooling''s own mess.\n\nTen of the twelve images are byte-identical across consecutive runs; the two\nthat are not are the terminal''s cursor blink and the clock in the data browser.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NWDUpnG54LrxgomuLgHJNQ","tree":{"sha":"2b9c6604e83d72dcc3f916db2c3f2d238f9f143e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/2b9c6604e83d72dcc3f916db2c3f2d238f9f143e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/219d7944d8a5bf870058ce9b991b178be7a1fdee","verification":{"payload":"tree 2b9c6604e83d72dcc3f916db2c3f2d238f9f143e\nparent b987135a2eca3a39bf703a39878a44e68a092f30\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787486372 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787486372 +0000\n\nPhotograph the environment being chosen, not only the state after\n\nThe recent change is that a Portainer''s environment is chosen in the panel, by\npressing a row. The screenshots only had the after picture: a row already\ncarrying the \"selected\" badge, which is what the panel looks like once the\nquestion has been answered and never again.\n\nThe capture now answers it in front of the camera. It clears the choice through\nSignal K''s own plugin config API, shoots the first-run state — the notice\nsaying which Portainer this is and that a row has to be pressed, above three\nrows each offering Select — then presses the row and shoots what that leaves\nbehind. Two pictures of one thing, in the order an operator meets them, and\nrepeatable: without the clearing step the first state exists exactly once.\n\nClearing it costs the plugin an error, which its configuration page goes on\nshowing until it restarts, so the configuration shots moved after a save of the\noptions unchanged — which is that restart. The status line in them is the\nsteady state again rather than the tooling''s own mess.\n\nTen of the twelve images are byte-identical across consecutive runs; the two\nthat are not are the terminal''s cursor blink and the clock in the data browser.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NWDUpnG54LrxgomuLgHJNQ\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNfeCJnI\ng7NeMWYDF+PZDtIikf/h7aCxqAA5H1XkUEegaO2KYb0+YboODbR9nZhwMPMhOZpPuWPeIRQfHxWL\nFAU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T11:59:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude"