, the stacks table and its editor, the\nconfiguration page, and the Signal K paths the delta poller publishes.\n\nEvery image is a capture of this plugin running in a real Signal K admin UI,\nso what they show is what the code renders. Portainer is the one thing played\nby a stand-in: tools/screenshots/mock-portainer.js answers the Portainer 2.x\nAPI the client calls — environments, the Docker proxy, stacks, the log stream\nand the exec WebSocket — with a plausible boat behind it, and a second site so\nthe instance picker has something to pick. capture.mjs drives the admin UI the\nway a person would and crops each shot to what matters, so an image is retaken\nrather than edited when the panel changes.\n\nThe verification section says what that does and does not establish: the panel\nnow demonstrably loads in the admin UI, the facade answers it, and SSE and the\nconsole relay carry data end to end — against a Portainer that answers as\ndocumented, which is still not a real one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NWDUpnG54LrxgomuLgHJNQ","tree":{"sha":"82e16a7af0e1aba2d4b754b62a2b7ef0dd335016","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/82e16a7af0e1aba2d4b754b62a2b7ef0dd335016"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/827120c7980b738752c5437819d042526a864b14","verification":{"payload":"tree 82e16a7af0e1aba2d4b754b62a2b7ef0dd335016\nparent 51356982415ab3b2be7d98fb90e6decaabe501fe\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787481857 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787481857 +0000\n\nScreenshots in the README, and the fixture that makes them repeatable\n\nThe README described a panel nobody could see. It now shows one: the\nContainers tab, the confirmation dialog, the log viewer following a live\nstream, a shell in the console, the stacks table and its editor, the\nconfiguration page, and the Signal K paths the delta poller publishes.\n\nEvery image is a capture of this plugin running in a real Signal K admin UI,\nso what they show is what the code renders. Portainer is the one thing played\nby a stand-in: tools/screenshots/mock-portainer.js answers the Portainer 2.x\nAPI the client calls — environments, the Docker proxy, stacks, the log stream\nand the exec WebSocket — with a plausible boat behind it, and a second site so\nthe instance picker has something to pick. capture.mjs drives the admin UI the\nway a person would and crops each shot to what matters, so an image is retaken\nrather than edited when the panel changes.\n\nThe verification section says what that does and does not establish: the panel\nnow demonstrably loads in the admin UI, the facade answers it, and SSE and the\nconsole relay carry data end to end — against a Portainer that answers as\ndocumented, which is still not a real one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NWDUpnG54LrxgomuLgHJNQ\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHgzBrrP\nCIEmk+DRTst+qivtPcDXuBj6ii9yMzwghtxnTV0WmHU3QQMqXOawEIyG73G5kV/jvxPprHM630rp\nYwU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T10:44:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/c