hor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/718e1100b35aba659683476caa9eda3c186950eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T10:10:01Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T10:10:01Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"message":"fix: take edge environment health from Portainer''s own heartbeat\n\nThe panel badged healthy remote environments \"down\". For edge types (4\nand 7) the plugin recomputed the check-in window itself, from\nLastCheckInDate and EdgeCheckinInterval, and got it wrong twice over:\n\n- LastCheckInDate is stamped with Portainer''s clock, so any skew between\n  the Signal K host and the Portainer host counts straight against the\n  window.\n- An async edge agent checks in on Edge.PingInterval — 60s by default —\n  while EdgeCheckinInterval in the same payload still carries the 5s\n  standard-mode default. That gives a 30s window for an agent that is\n  meant to be quiet for 60s, so a perfectly healthy link reads as down\n  most of the time.\n\nPortainer already answers this question in Heartbeat, computed per\nrequest by the endpoint list handler with the async intervals it alone\nknows and on its own clock. It is what Portainer''s own UI shows, so it\nis what the panel shows now. The local computation stays as a fallback\nfor Portainer versions that do not publish the field, and is now\nasync-aware: it mirrors Portainer''s rule of taking the shortest of the\nping, command and snapshot intervals, capped at 60s.\n\nAlso stop painting \"unknown\" in the red badge that means down. Portainer\nomits Status entirely on an environment it has never snapshotted, and\ndeclining to say is not an outage.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vJFFCVJ6Yc2aKpVJAETwt","tree":{"sha":"10b441414bd9d4cb202073b75c81cfa3a2ede88a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/10b441414bd9d4cb202073b75c81cfa3a2ede88a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/718e1100b35aba659683476caa9eda3c186950eb","verification":{"payload":"tree 10b441414bd9d4cb202073b75c81cfa3a2ede88a\nparent 51356982415ab3b2be7d98fb90e6decaabe501fe\nauthor Karl-Erik Gustafsson <ke.gustafsson@gmail.com> 1787479801 +0000\ncommitter Karl-Erik Gustafsson <ke.gustafsson@gmail.com> 1787479801 +0000\n\nfix: take edge environment health from Portainer''s own heartbeat\n\nThe panel badged healthy remote environments \"down\". For edge types (4\nand 7) the plugin recomputed the check-in window itself, from\nLastCheckInDate and EdgeCheckinInterval, and got it wrong twice over:\n\n- LastCheckInDate is stamped with Portainer''s clock, so any skew between\n  the Signal K host and the Portainer host counts straight against the\n  window.\n- An async edge agent checks in on Edge.PingInterval — 60s by default —\n  while EdgeCheckinInterval in the same payload still carries the 5s\n  standard-mode default. That gives a 30s window for an agent that is\n  meant to be quiet for 60s, so a perfectly healthy link reads as down\n  most of the time.\n\nPortainer already answers this question in Heartbeat, computed per\nrequest by the endpoint list handler with the async intervals it alone\nknows and on its own clock. It is what Portainer''s own UI shows, so it\nis what the panel shows now. The local computation stays as a fallback\nfor Portainer versions that do not publish the field, and is now\nasync-aware: it mirrors Portainer''s rule of taking the shortest of the\nping, command and snapshot intervals, capped at 60s.\n\nAlso stop painting \"unknown\" in the red badge that means down. Portainer\nomits Status entirely on an environment it has never snapshotted, and\ndeclining to say is not an outage.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vJFFCVJ6Yc2aKpVJAETwt\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPS0jqxg\nadONhuWeotdoZH0FttiDDIPwjKUlqO+9P2u6nIyogmsJm9vWMZb/WnEgiSUSq55thl1aR6d1MYQK\nEQ4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"ht