n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T10:00:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/51356982415ab3b2be7d98fb90e6decaabe501fe","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDUxMzU2OTgyNDE1YWIzYjJiZTdkOThmYjkwZTZkZWNhYWJlNTAxZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/943397edd358c890d542c4c694edc75b0786d024","sha":"943397edd358c890d542c4c694edc75b0786d024","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/943397edd358c890d542c4c694edc75b0786d024"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/c14326443278b62bf2a77604de26a2d1d3eea423","sha":"c14326443278b62bf2a77604de26a2d1d3eea423","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/c14326443278b62bf2a77604de26a2d1d3eea423"}],"sha":"51356982415ab3b2be7d98fb90e6decaabe501fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/51356982415ab3b2be7d98fb90e6decaabe501fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/c14326443278b62bf2a77604de26a2d1d3eea423/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T09:49:25Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T09:49:25Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"message":"feat: choose the Portainer environment from the panel\n\nA Portainer managing several Docker hosts left the plugin unusable until an\noperator found the environment id and edited it into the plugin\nconfiguration by hand. Worse, the route that lists the environments called\nenvironment(), which throws on an ambiguous selection — so the panel could\nnot show what the choices were, precisely because no choice had been made.\n\nThe panel now offers a dropdown. Until something is picked the tabs stay\nempty behind a prompt rather than a red error, and the dropdown appears only\nwhen there is a real choice to make: one environment still resolves itself.\n\nThe choice is saved server-side rather than held in the browser. The delta\npoller and the watchdog run against the same client, so a selection only one\ntab knew about would leave telemetry publishing nothing while the panel\nlooked fine. Saving is also the point — it is what replaces editing the id\nin by hand.\n\n- client: environmentOrNone() separates an unmade choice from a wrong one.\n  An id naming nothing is still an error; only genuine ambiguity returns\n  undefined. selectEnvironment() repoints the client and drops every cached\n  read, which described the previous environment''s daemon.\n- facade: PUT /api/environment validates the id against Portainer before\n  storing it, so a typo cannot persist a selection that breaks the panel on\n  the next restart. A save that fails still selects, and says it will not\n  survive a restart.\n- index: writes environmentId back through savePluginOptions, into the\n  options as the server handed them over rather than the normalized config —\n  saving the normalized object would rewrite fields the operator set, their\n  host and port among them.\n\nStill refuses to auto-select when several exist. Silently picking the first\ncould restart a container on the wrong host before anyone noticed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e6f2a3a7512b04fb060ab549f6c7a23aa2f7d403","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/e6f2a3a7512b04fb060ab549f6c7a23aa2f7d403"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/c14326443278b62bf2a77604de26a2d1d3eea423","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/c14326443278b62bf2a77604de26a2d1d3eea423","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGMxNDMyNjQ0MzI3OGI2MmJmMmE3NzYwNGRlMjZhMmQxZDNlZWE0MjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/dfe68ce489f983c0229c0f56643901153acd7a49","sha":"dfe68ce489f983c0229c0f56643901153acd7a49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/dfe68ce489f983c0229c0f56643901153acd7a49"}],"sha":"c14326443278b62bf2a77604de26a2d1d3eea423","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/c14326443278b62bf2a77604de26a2d1d3eea423"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/dfe68ce489f983c0229c0f56643901153acd7a49/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T09:49:11Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T09:49:11Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"message":"fix: run clean on Windows shells, and stop tests timing out under load\n\n`npm run clean` used `rm -rf`, which only works where a POSIX shell runs it.\nnpm runs scripts through cmd.exe on Windows, so the script failed there.\nReplaced with a node one-liner using fs.rmSync, which needs no new dependency\nand behaves the same under bash, PowerShell and cmd.\n\nSeparately, two test timeouts that were never real hangs:\n\nLogViewer''s 5000-line test waited with findByText, which re-runs a\nwhole-document text query on every mutation batch. Committing 5010 rows\nproduces enough of them to spend 4.9s waiting for data that had already\narrived — the same query run once synchronously takes 116ms. It sat just\nunder the 5s default, so any load tipped it over. Flushed deterministically\ninstead; the suite went from 92s to 53s.\n\nThat shifted worker scheduling and exposed a StackEditor test doing the same\nthing at 1.8s. Rather than chase each one, testTimeout is now 30s: jsdom\nrenders and per-keystroke userEvent typing are slow enough that the 5s\ndefault turns worker contention into spurious failures.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1503997f314301899d8c6713ba2aaf418bc546e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/1503997f314301899d8c6713ba2aaf418bc546e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/dfe68ce489f983c0229c0f56643901153acd7a49","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/dfe68ce489f983c0229c0f56643901153acd7a49","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGRmZTY4Y2U0ODlmOTgzYzAyMjljMGY1NjY0MzkwMTE1M2FjZDdhNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/943397edd358c890d542c4c694edc75b0786d024","sha":"943397edd358c890d542c4c694edc75b0786d024","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/943397edd358c890d542c4c694edc75b0786d024"}],"sha":"dfe68ce489f983c0229c0f56643901153acd7a49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/dfe68ce489f983c0229c0f56643901153acd7a49"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/943397edd358c890d542c4c694edc75b0786d024/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T08:52:23Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T08:52:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Correct the API reference that caused the removeVolumes bug (#30)\n\nDocumentation only.\n\ndocs/portainer-api.md listed removeVolumes as a parameter of Portainer CE''s\nstack delete. It is not one, and that line is where the bug fixed in #29 came\nfrom: the plugin sent it, Go ignored the unknown query parameter, the request\nsucceeded, the volumes stayed, and the facade reported the removal. The entry\nnow says what the parameter actually was and points at the call that does take\na volume option — container delete, which was never wrong.\n\nAlso records Ctrl+] in the changelog''s terminal entry: it is the only way out\nof a shell reached by keyboard, since xterm captures Tab and Escape reaches\nthe shell once one is running.","tree":{"sha":"ad277e7ff95b1785878a54aaa1d7437e2d8167ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/ad277e7ff95b1785878a54aaa1d7437e2d8167ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/943397edd358c890d542c4c694edc75b0786d024","verification":{"payload":"tree ad277e7ff95b1785878a54aaa1d7437e2d8167ec\nparent 38e67bcdc1b3f015827b6424b2fdea17bbcbd4d9\nauthor Karl-Erik Gustafsson <ke.gustafsson@gmail.com> 1787475143 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787475143 +0300\n\nCorrect the API reference that caused the removeVolumes bug (#30)\n\nDocumentation only.\n\ndocs/portainer-api.md listed removeVolumes as a parameter of Portainer CE''s\nstack delete. It is not one, and that line is where the bug fixed in #29 came\nfrom: the plugin sent it, Go ignored the unknown query parameter, the request\nsucceeded, the volumes stayed, and the facade reported the removal. The entry\nnow says what the parameter actually was and points at the call that does take\na volume option — container delete, which was never wrong.\n\nAlso records Ctrl+] in the changelog''s terminal entry: it is the only way out\nof a shell reached by keyboard, since xterm captures Tab and Escape reaches\nthe shell once one is running.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqirTHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0ekQAGPh62SEQTMDkeo9o1odlJ0N\nf1guWbUxdqSBRj4QfCjdsIb6P/BdW4J+jae+RNgBb6MZFTxh+xypBtTb1J2NWQ8d\nGC0SPQI3bvxmWG8pI9cW3INpxWvGuTfDF1vEAxn3EqqWl86zVIZ9AL3Sfhx0kDXm\ncW7PlZSDEn7cwO+fiuiBTQrrWJYNAeFoc2jqSWeGNhTgmGt//SNLJ3xuUX6zXfbi\nFQmbVLvvHDrqAKGON4AjsxLKl8zR4AetmfPo12QUlcqpV8DAWNQRKCEU8x4bT4IK\nE72Jip8uzgiR5CsR2cyqL14tdFgo6AjznK2oF72SfO106ht/lxIgyPlR3xOTCnFY\nk+CjvIsxEp5Odu+v1bvVvCwio2DswYe/nMx1RjNOjTo9IF9ocyLSJMIftJhN+3n2\nAmerm8qZA3NPqMd2kMs1ypqov+NcsYWvp9zU7e66B5V+FsBhE3xkbsVzykbz/5TR\nO0dKgJ74KDfoth4xL1UXvFyAXpsyRAYmfkm3m2jG4np0elsO8PDT/JLH22vllJWv\nNe6