ers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/38e67bcdc1b3f015827b6424b2fdea17bbcbd4d9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T08:20:32Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T08:20:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix the review findings: the crash, the 304s, the volume lie, and the untested TLS chain (#29)\n\nActs on the eight-review audit, plus the review round on the PR itself.\n\nCritical: a malformed container list no longer ends the Signal K process;\nDocker''s 304 \"already in that state\" is success for lifecycle calls; stack\ndelete no longer claims to remove volumes Portainer CE cannot remove; the\nREST TLS chain is covered end to end.\n\nHigh: a same-origin guard on every mutating route; a status line the poller\nkeeps current; emitStats removed; the watchdog made configurable and its\ninstance names validated; prune gated on allowDestructive; stack creation\nself-protected by name; SSE frames and error responses redacted; log streams\nended on stop().\n\nMedium: a panel error boundary; every tab payload guarded; react/jsx-runtime\nshared as a singleton; dialogs dismissable while a request hangs; two failed\npolls before the unreachable alarm; poll interval and timeout bounded; Ctrl+]\nto leave the terminal; PUT control decoupled from the telemetry level.\n\n739 tests, 96.6% lines. Three tests on this branch passed while exercising\nnothing and were each caught by reverting the production line; two of them\nwere hiding real defects, including a Ctrl+] handler that did not exist.","tree":{"sha":"be07091638c6a326ae0fc5d4223b9d31608db6c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/be07091638c6a326ae0fc5d4223b9d31608db6c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/38e67bcdc1b3f015827b6424b2fdea17bbcbd4d9","verification":{"payload":"tree be07091638c6a326ae0fc5d4223b9d31608db6c4\nparent e11b938a466186ecfa059e79deb944695fda347e\nauthor Karl-Erik Gustafsson <ke.gustafsson@gmail.com> 1787473232 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787473232 +0300\n\nFix the review findings: the crash, the 304s, the volume lie, and the untested TLS chain (#29)\n\nActs on the eight-review audit, plus the review round on the PR itself.\n\nCritical: a malformed container list no longer ends the Signal K process;\nDocker''s 304 \"already in that state\" is success for lifecycle calls; stack\ndelete no longer claims to remove volumes Portainer CE cannot remove; the\nREST TLS chain is covered end to end.\n\nHigh: a same-origin guard on every mutating route; a status line the poller\nkeeps current; emitStats removed; the watchdog made configurable and its\ninstance names validated; prune gated on allowDestructive; stack creation\nself-protected by name; SSE frames and error responses redacted; log streams\nended on stop().\n\nMedium: a panel error boundary; every tab payload guarded; react/jsx-runtime\nshared as a singleton; dialogs dismissable while a request hangs; two failed\npolls before the unreachable alarm; poll interval and timeout bounded; Ctrl+]\nto leave the terminal; PUT control decoupled from the telemetry level.\n\n739 tests, 96.6% lines. Three tests on this branch passed while exercising\nnothing and were each caught by reverting the production line; two of them\nwere hiding real defects, including a Ctrl+] handler that did not exist.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiq1QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyQwQAFzNI5g2alYHXPSLhXS1/g8M\nPgFR6UgXE3Dfqj+UGEMVxy0TlEf9dQ069vlu07ec77q+JcAQn2cMP255TEIkYGqs\nhQ7XW9sky/c5v86hNV7i8/9kaYOdXtiCoMrK8lSLQ9R4QrI4tBFJ/sm5WGUV9lBL\nIN/olUDhTdJqHeUGwWFPbisWB4lBxs9IbxrNaZLva5UzkSPZ4c7PxvWpvyPnsI2X\nW6woFEBXQ9/rwz6PJxjETYfTn12dYixCx0/Mj/oudc3CAj31D2XBjNJ+B6kYh6HU\ncfmxWaNPGG2XGloOHTN0X+67tJsgmcIKIF/LKgOOCszymdm3EfowQytecr2ldUaE\nvGCNQTib2+YMPivtk1H5wH8p1h44nGS4i2B8NNyX60R6daTq6FcyWHzlp3E1r1ld\nnCkj0v5qfqulyzw/4tp/9mW604PzIFC9DDuThGYxULisnWJXfsNG62dcJ8FabMK4\nfXhcB4myhxY3AxpKUHvigXR/HQZm86kbtvKoP8KifLu0S35pTUjNGhFmhYhgVMSv\nUbktHzfpqeeCor9gnWpyaV36vFxYEtIhzZ2dtF+zUdSiM3oH57cu+0FsKNV0lFRa\n+uEOAEvRp0CWHmsSIjDfuyy4wWcJk8vtch3HsGhH0MlATi7kGVUD00t412KLfXH1\nSiPx2noSx8kvYX1vrlD6\n=ei3K\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T08:20:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/38e67bcdc1b3f015827b6424b2fdea17bbcbd4d9","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDM4ZTY3YmNkYzFiM2YwMTU4MjdiNjQyNGIyZmRlYTE3YmJjYmQ0ZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/e11b938a466186ecfa059e79deb944695fda347e","sha":"e11b938a466186ecfa059e79deb944695fda347e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/e11b938a466186ecfa059e79deb944695fda347e"}],"sha":"38e67bcdc1b3f015827b6424b2fdea17bbcbd4d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/38e67bcdc1b3f015827b6424b2fdea17bbcbd4d9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/e11b938a466186ecfa059e79deb944695fda347e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T03:40:26Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T03:40:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Release readiness: changelog, install and setup docs, and one dead dependency gone (#28)\n\nThree things standing between this and a first publish.\n\n`@signalk/server-admin-ui-dependencies` was a runtime dependency that nothing\nimported: the panel deliberately uses plain Bootstrap class names rather than\nreactstrap, because the admin UI already loads the CSS. It was also the only\nsource of the four high-severity advisories, through less and image-size, none\nwith a fix available. Removing it takes the audit from four to zero and leaves\nthe build and all 702 tests passing.\n\nAdds CHANGELOG.md, shipped in the tarball, written as Unreleased rather than\n0.1.0 because nothing has been published — and saying up front that none of it\nhas been exercised against a real Portainer.\n\nAdds sections on installing and setting up. The README explained the design at\nlength and never said how to point it at a Portainer: what goes in an instance,\nthe three ways to deal with Portainer''s self-signed certificate, and what each\nof the three control switches actually permits. Also drops a stale paragraph\nstill describing M2 and M3 as planned.","tree":{"sha":"76196cdb60d1d052b38cb263b86b89f00a0d0a7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/76196cdb60d1d052b38cb263b86b89f00a0d0a7f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/e11b938a466186ecfa059e79deb944695fda347e","verification":{"payload":"tree 76196cdb60d1d052b38cb263b86b89f00a0d0a7f\nparent 38b3f52b1b6a7b9eba5e046c6a1c735317b7ee4f\nauthor Karl-Erik Gustafsson <ke.gustafsson@gmail.com> 1787456426 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787456426 +0300\n\nRelease readiness: changelog, install and setup docs, and one dead dependency gone (#28)\n\nThree things standing between this and a first publish.\n\n`@signalk/server-admin-ui-dependencies` was a runtime dependency that nothing\nimported: the panel deliberately uses plain Bootstrap class names rather than\nreactstrap, because the admin UI already loads the CSS. It was also the only\nsource of the four high-severity advisories, through less and image-size, none\nwith a fix available. Removing it takes the audit from four to zero and leaves\nthe build and all 702 tests passing.\n\nAdds CHANGELOG.md, shipped in the tarball, written as Unreleased rather than\n0.1.0 because nothing has been published — and saying up front that none of it\nhas been exercised against a real Portainer.\n\nAdds sections on installing and setting up. The README explained the design at\nlength and never said how to point it at a Portainer: what goes in an instance,\nthe three ways to deal with Portainer''s self-signed certificate, and what each\nof the three control switches actually permits. Also drops a stale paragraph\nstill describing M2 and M3 as planned.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqimuqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVmgQAFsl1xsBZ4bNJFsl/nrQHgv6\njO5WAm+FZlAYpxAE6E7w6md9LhAESOyhY99WabhiGOKXJpBYKgAuIIMZNz1MMXZj\ndl/cxOVQzLxm/V+ObsJHgqQgViegOHg4FoFZw+OZOukh8B8aworUl8i8z0GVPG0Y\n2BF/TSBHwtoiFg4DCfQfkfrtyKhoy2lBnQHR/2I5LqdY+KAEPYjsPVd1Yz1x0nRt\narE2VkMUH9y2Ng9nafIwR9uc7m75t+OlOgzaUSANYPN5kwd/mVBbAwzlkfoKtO46\nd4SeVAquQmi0r59qWfQoPPbqVc6bgv43ckfN4tUIngSDYlok4JE09a1iR1vxqVlx\ngccYO2sBsJRDphWTEp+f7xxO9jnpJL5l9ry8wJbE637/QBTvLjwB0947+/TTZrBG\nPqsUtLsGl6R0jcH3hQMV5g7LbOC8tPVcGNmoafxYmALdc0tUUL0ophhdEtN6VrWP\nEoZuhvImBHiIylPjIuWWaCkHDgahvqY1vrGw5iMzsD9o8cl7EqLjtOIpa0jlq5JP\nwmLEXtHSRz7UAXvKPz6LaBKtYRtV2H4lnVV0rN6pME/qlEMXgmpIJ6munyvd9bpl\nXwOO9PhcEc4KpUhod+Q1Q9D+wIwQq88MAHTat8TT69yKs7IGWCXNWVqqVFOEq5q7\nIPxPaugxAAKQV3yhLB15\n=+Wqk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T03:40:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/e11b938a466186ecfa059e79deb944695fda347e","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGUxMWI5MzhhNDY2MTg2ZWNmYTA1OWU3OWRlYjk0NDY5NWZkYTM0N2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/38b3f52b1b6a7b9eba5e046c6a1c735317b7ee4f","sha":"38b3f52b1b6a7b9eba5e046c6a1c735317b7ee4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/38b3f52b1b6a7b9eba5e046c6a1c735317b7ee4f"}],"sha":"e11b938a466186ecfa059e79deb944695fda347e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/e11b938a466186ecfa059e79deb944695fda347e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/38b3f52b1b6a7b9eba5e046c6a1c735317b7ee4f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T01:57:57Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T01:57:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"M6b — a container console in the panel (#27)\n\nA terminal on the Containers tab, on top of the relay M6a built.\n\nConsole on a container row opens a shell in a dialog — /bin/sh, /bin/bash or\n/bin/ash, picked before it starts. The button is disabled with its reason as\nthe tooltip for a container that is not running, for the Signal K container,\nand while control is off; it is absent altogether on a server that cannot\nserve a console, since that is not something an operator can change.\n\nxterm.js is 83 KB gzipped against the panel''s own 18 KB, so it is fetched in\nits own chunk the first time somebody opens a shell rather than by every admin\nUI that shows a table of containers.\n\nAdds the resize path the terminal needs. The browser is the only end that\nknows how big the terminal is, and it cannot say so over the socket — a byte\npipe to the shell, where a control message is indistinguishable from a\nkeystroke. The POST that mints the ticket also mints a session handle, the\nsocket records what it refers to, and POST /console/resize tells Docker. The\nhandle travels only in bodies, never in a URL.\n\nOpening is three awaits — the POST, the terminal''s chunk, the socket — and\neach checks whether it is still wanted, closing what it built when it is not.\nSwitching Portainer closes the shell and the log viewer before the instance\nchanges, so neither asks the newly selected one about the old one''s container\nids. Output arriving after the dialog has gone is dropped rather than written\nto a disposed terminal.\n\nThis completes every milestone in docs/plan.md. Nothing has been run against a\nreal Portainer or driven by a person through the admin UI; see \"What has and\nhas not been verified\" in the README.","tree":{"sha":"2274f7ba91b506191c37c35ae17b3153a9586ac3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/2274f7ba91b506191c37c35ae17b3153a9586ac3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/38b3f52b1b6a7b9eba5e046c6a1c735317b7ee4f","verification":{"payload":"tree 2274f7ba91b506191c37c35ae17b3153a9586ac3\nparent a3bb93d8bab29fb50d19708264e013509c8f89d7\nauthor Karl-Erik Gustafsson <ke.gustafsson@gmail.com> 1787450277 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787450277 +0300\n\nM6b — a container console in the panel (#27)\n\nA terminal on the Containers tab, on top of the relay M6a built.\n\nConsole on a container row opens a shell in a dialog — /bin/sh, /bin/bash or\n/bin/ash, picked before it starts. The button is disabled with its reason as\nthe tooltip for a container that is not running, for the Signal K container,\nand while control is off; it is absent altogether on a server that cannot\nserve a console, since that is not something an operator can change.\n\nxterm.js is 83 KB gzipped against the panel''s own 18 KB, so it is fetched in\nits own chunk the first time somebody opens a shell rather than by every admin\nUI that shows a table of containers.\n\nAdds the resize path the terminal needs. The browser is the only end that\nknows how big the terminal is, and it cannot say so over the socket — a byte\npipe to the shell, where a control message is indistinguishable from a\nkeystroke. The POST that mints the ticket also mints a session handle, the\nsocket records what it refers to, and POST /console/resize tells Docker. The\nhandle travels only in bodies, never in a URL.\n\nOpening is three awaits — the POST, the terminal''s chunk, the socket — and\neach checks whether it is still wanted, closing what it built when it is not.\nSwitching Portainer closes the shell and the log viewer before the instance\nchanges, so neither asks the newly selected one about the old one''s container\nids. Output arriving after the dialog has gone is dropped rather than written\nto a disposed terminal.\n\nThis completes every milestone in docs/plan.md. Nothing has been run against a\nreal Portainer or driven by a person through the admin UI; see \"What has and\nhas not been verified\" in the README.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqilOlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKs4QAK+SinRpR0QtSeilp+x4Gpnj\nsoSzrtHB0uGqL3h3QSABieRFLj+BZkGDzwhAsqof89A3Pz+GG0XHpsinMZT5LvC8\nFFcOjpiZ6i3MZAaweA6mnkCGyTNU/wkZ7Enk/PkiB0azV6YvCXg5Xwg/0Xw9trke\nAVIQtrq27g+h5JFN7wvZeNekIwHOVt0bqM1SKClVsEPswOqmX+8OsRbh+p2mU0E8\nOzrJdZ4CeNx5JCsIugd10vl4U5dYPEfuHfA0UQ0qvWn7Vi9WYICPJp4UGLZvsgOw\nDuJMtoUVt+RD/fHNhP9+/qA5kByx7NH0j2vMJ5NOoh8UX8kzoXnDtVRHVhardjze\nBrn2Wt80pM7OdnViZsrN2+f28niK+pQi8W9vef19bSU2BrGf6IEDnYZosnaFofo7\nqO0y5xiqsLaBeCBY3kwGBPnhXVViRFKcW3OJcDfx7g9PDQKm9WiDuoZDzRebEetO\nW6+mz3Bn1HQunJdhvefJVD232d6FJXy8I2CikuweMrVKqYlIuelsagv2wI2MgXDh\nogBYXg3WkNVm8ApNq9SWzT4n9/QF3SKk43gpirmIoUYx4wK3HrPBQqssij/SgB3v\nxp74OyGRYFakMbqKuCHzvocLoXYZrEXb6iEPFKxlcBZKnoJqRHfk/zY0JGZOgY/x\nH5YTkZS9SIhg8Iblrz1u\n=iS10\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T01:57:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/38b3f52b1b6a7b9eba5e046c6a1c735317b7ee4f","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDM4YjNmNTJiMWI2YTdiOWViYTVlMDQ2YzZhMWM3MzUzMTdiN2VlNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/a3bb93d8bab29fb50d19708264e013509c8f89d7","sha":"a3bb93d8bab29fb50d19708264e013509c8f89d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/a3bb93d8bab29fb50d19708264e013509c8f89d7"}],"sha":"38b3f52b1b6a7b9eba5e046c6a1c735317b7ee4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/38b3f52b1b6a7b9eba5e046c6a1c735317b7ee4f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/a3bb93d8bab29fb50d19708264e013509c8f89d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T00:58:47Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T00:58:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"M6a — a container console, server side (#26)\n\nAn authenticated WebSocket relay that opens a shell in a container.\n\nAn admin POST creates the Docker exec instance and returns a single-use,\n30-second ticket; the browser presents it on the upgrade. The cookie is not\ntrusted, because WebSocket upgrades are not subject to CORS. The relay carries\nbytes both ways, ends both sockets however either side ends, times out an idle\nshell, and is bounded to three shells overall and two per container. The\nSignal K container itself is refused, as everywhere else.\n\nIncludes the review fixes: an in-flight accept can no longer outlive shutdown\nor a browser that gave up; the instance TLS settings reach the WebSocket as\nwell as the REST calls; and ticket capacity is reserved before the exec\ninstance is created, so a full store cannot orphan one.","tree":{"sha":"e4db7befbf9fbfc8b437712c4193d0e8d7235dc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/e4db7befbf9fbfc8b437712c4193d0e8d7235dc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/a3bb93d8bab29fb50d19708264e013509c8f89d7","verification":{"payload":"tree e4db7befbf9fbfc8b437712c4193d0e8d7235dc3\nparent 811e511e991542157b3740357d268209fe807c04\nauthor Karl-Erik Gustafsson <ke.gustafsson@gmail.com> 1787446727 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787446727 +0300\n\nM6a — a container console, server side (#26)\n\nAn authenticated WebSocket relay that opens a shell in a container.\n\nAn admin POST creates the Docker exec instance and returns a single-use,\n30-second ticket; the browser presents it on the upgrade. The cookie is not\ntrusted, because WebSocket upgrades are not subject to CORS. The relay carries\nbytes both ways, ends both sockets however either side ends, times out an idle\nshell, and is bounded to three shells overall and two per container. The\nSignal K container itself is refused, as everywhere else.\n\nIncludes the review fixes: an in-flight accept can no longer outlive shutdown\nor a browser that gave up; the instance TLS settings reach the WebSocket as\nwell as the REST calls; and ticket capacity is reserved before the exec\ninstance is created, so a full store cannot orphan one.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqikXHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArUQQAGnPnhjzFTe9WeWrprIKfvS6\nZwoVJ6APql81XROBvrUy8skTOMoHJDy2ZSPgkdkL5yr6JMF8J6hkKVOCCg1WfHKb\nLqnHdqx17ebshpmKFn6Iuv2jWVItohMMPpIfbQ9XcoPoE19yOFo1r2Xryf+novoN\ndl2umCKGMmdAiU4MvCICfjdPXpeQox9AHmXDLzbeRUiNeTIBRjly7YzuSXzWaIlc\ne1IstFEhgXGjL4NTJlkKuKG7UNWnAI3WThiGPYGCk7X7UeGXpTdt5tsUojUT7+M1\nFwjxdJV/+91JHq1jJCurMUy8hvibLFcImMiUDxtfnrhUInt4dI2DrwxNic06WXH6\nG75XEt/FjvD6NyEOp46yGO/ofFX6HJZzKR2hSey2DDdgdGxKh0SVMCiCY+hleEAj\nL0D7MNFYe8mWY+Qe5nfI5A1bOKE31qLgnKY6EMZi4zEJ4xgixmXfx3r+hiS8do3R\nbMHJhYveQfRAgd/PFEM0HNBupLJy+7fLx1UgRMPS5XqM47tAOfUEjqtudpytYPUW\nDh3ZJOhDQCUa1iQ3oh+ejQcEq5cPVjVfcGwD0QZn6mJyy5HVqggLz7B3Be1u0Vox\nJ/xH+RUZh6MQQac03QVk5f6N5e38qt0Tavv463YXnDJN0/E8Va5ivFAsC882MkvZ\nVeTt9PCSmStT78LCUaLU\n=G0k5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T00:58:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/a3bb93d8bab29fb50d19708264e013509c8f89d7","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKGEzYmI5M2Q4YmFiMjlmYjUwZDE5NzA4MjY0ZTAxMzUwOWM4Zjg5ZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/811e511e991542157b3740357d268209fe807c04","sha":"811e511e991542157b3740357d268209fe807c04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/811e511e991542157b3740357d268209fe807c04"}],"sha":"a3bb93d8bab29fb50d19708264e013509c8f89d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/a3bb93d8bab29fb50d19708264e013509c8f89d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/811e511e991542157b3740357d268209fe807c04/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T23:21:36Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T23:21:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"M5b — stacks in the admin panel (#25)\n\nThe Stacks tab can act, using the routes M5a added.\n\nEach row offers what applies to it: a running stack is stopped and a\nstopped one started, never both; Redeploy only where there is a repository\nto redeploy from; Delete only when the configuration allows destructive\noperations, and disabled it carries the setting that would enable it. Edit\nstays available even with control disabled, because reading a compose file\nis a read.\n\nThe editor puts the compose file and the stack''s environment side by side,\nwith Deploy disabled until something actually changed, and prune and\nre-pull as separate unticked toggles rather than Portainer''s defaults. A\nstack deployed from a repository is read-only, with its repository named\nand Redeploy pointed at: the server refuses a file deploy over such a\nstack, and an editable box that ends in a refusal says that worse.\n\nNew stack creates from a compose file or a repository, and a token given\nwith no username is still sent — several git hosts take it that way, and\ndropping it would clone anonymously and fail on a private repository with\nnothing saying why.\n\nDeleting asks first, naming the stack rather than asking \"are you sure?\",\nand treats volumes as a separate unticked choice that says what it\ndestroys.\n\nA failed deploy leaves the editor open with the file still in it. The\neditor and the delete dialog close when the instance changes, and the\nstack list is normalized before it is rendered, since those ids are what a\ndelete is sent with.\n\n547 tests.","tree":{"sha":"827ab07a2a323b614cce6323b7911995132677be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/827ab07a2a323b614cce6323b7911995132677be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/811e511e991542157b3740357d268209fe807c04","verification":{"payload":"tree 827ab07a2a323b614cce6323b7911995132677be\nparent 18446de18ad592600748f4c5aed9392b23120b42\nauthor Karl-Erik Gustafsson <ke.gustafsson@gmail.com> 1787440896 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787440896 +0300\n\nM5b — stacks in the admin panel (#25)\n\nThe Stacks tab can act, using the routes M5a added.\n\nEach row offers what applies to it: a running stack is stopped and a\nstopped one started, never both; Redeploy only where there is a repository\nto redeploy from; Delete only when the configuration allows destructive\noperations, and disabled it carries the setting that would enable it. Edit\nstays available even with control disabled, because reading a compose file\nis a read.\n\nThe editor puts the compose file and the stack''s environment side by side,\nwith Deploy disabled until something actually changed, and prune and\nre-pull as separate unticked toggles rather than Portainer''s defaults. A\nstack deployed from a repository is read-only, with its repository named\nand Redeploy pointed at: the server refuses a file deploy over such a\nstack, and an editable box that ends in a refusal says that worse.\n\nNew stack creates from a compose file or a repository, and a token given\nwith no username is still sent — several git hosts take it that way, and\ndropping it would clone anonymously and fail on a private repository with\nnothing saying why.\n\nDeleting asks first, naming the stack rather than asking \"are you sure?\",\nand treats volumes as a separate unticked choice that says what it\ndestroys.\n\nA failed deploy leaves the editor open with the file still in it. The\neditor and the delete dialog close when the instance changes, and the\nstack list is normalized before it is rendered, since those ids are what a\ndelete is sent with.\n\n547 tests.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqii8ACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOr8QAISY3aPveHWOk6x45zqKVQNx\nYsY+aRHB0ufZa94/Qab8XgE0og1LJa4HbbA3alZZmGrci3wPZ9EbdqHKMYBcnq8f\niLrvpF/bRuFaEu0jGbQICc/b11Blqo1X+G4k789f3gySOcor6F2VsMVAqoR6Lnis\nFnQ69fKIC8EhXGIKxVXxjaFCGm/2UESnu54vOtbudESzplFu/v11N+FxaV5EpZCa\n1qz6sdQU8ENIqe+nXHS4th+jQbGFOPff7lJJ8EmfIBEVII9XPd5weZT0TssINILQ\nu9U6u3rzAv+B55kL/3K58n4XfEE3h/AXqUuz5C3WRXSBjxCJ9g1TNuBjmhA2ZBal\nspdC1i8wDuB1kyc/cQUC22Hi4TA/5PgLfQAz7OQyuPgBLKlv5V5IWBotFRvmwHDJ\nxNnem9Ioh8TZILa1kxy3Jqx724XEf4rCJMgoMgOMrWfhMAcTpwlFGa/z2AKSYLNl\nioXhpHa9KVEc2L3nP/twOzdZz80OdK4Knrdt6tUyQkqkALB/Fcld8/inmh+r3dim\nIR3+HMt6W6YELos5ld5WJ+bPXJ+3qrNu1qMtPh2U9CBiDlg7j+qvtvjjuXPhd5Xb\nNqPcLdjM1WLWeeHf1cdDFI6JOFBoTJ5NfC1Lp3ga6yfdSEE2IBWZWrNb6Znm7a3l\nkAy96kMy3R69XSjVE1kX\n=tigc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T23:21:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/811e511e991542157b3740357d268209fe807c04","node_id":"C_kwDOR829YtoAKDgxMWU1MTFlOTkxNTQyMTU3YjM3NDAzNTdkMjY4MjA5ZmU4MDdjMDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commit/18446de18ad592600748f4c5aed9392b23120b42","sha":"18446de18ad592600748f4c5aed9392b23120b42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/18446de18ad592600748f4c5aed9392b23120b42"}],"sha":"811e511e991542157b3740357d268209fe807c04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/811e511e991542157b3740357d268209fe807c04"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/commits/18446de18ad592600748f4c5aed9392b23120b42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T22:00:33Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T22:00:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"M5a — stack writes over the API (#24)\n\nStart, stop, update, git redeploy, create from a compose file or a\nrepository, and delete. The compose editor in the panel is M5b.\n\nEvery call that names a stack id resolves it against this environment''s\nstacks first: Portainer will act on any stack the configured credential can\nreach, including one belonging to a different environment.\n\nWhat is sent is stated rather than defaulted. Prune is off unless asked\nfor, an update with no environment keeps the one the stack already had, and\nvolumes survive a delete unless removal is asked for. A create picks the\nswarm or standalone route from the environment and carries the SwarmID\nswarm requires.\n\nTwo things Portainer does quietly are refused here. A redeploy needs a\nrepository, and an update must not touch a stack that has one: Portainer''s\nupdate handler detaches such a stack from git and clears its auto-update\nsettings, so it silently stops being what the repository describes. For a\nfile-based stack that had auto-update, the answer carries a warning, since\nno field in the request could have kept it.\n\nStack-level self-protection is the guard that matters most. Container\nself-protection catches \"stop this container\"; stopping, updating,\nredeploying or deleting the stack around it reaches the same outcome by\nnaming something one level up. The check reads the compose project and\nswarm namespace labels off the containers themselves and counts a Signal K\nthat is currently stopped. Starting a stack is left alone.\n\nBodies are parsed rather than trusted, bounded at 512kb, and their failures\nanswer in the same { error, hint } shape as everything else. TLS\nverification is never disabled by a request.\n\n497 tests.","tree":{"sha":"126d3bf941875693e2cc3027bfb5b18ee6d8fea1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/trees/126d3bf941875693e2cc3027bfb5b18ee6d8fea1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KEGustafsson/signalk-portainer/git/commits/18446de18ad592600748f4c5aed9392b23120b42","verification":{"payload":"tree 126d3bf941875693e2cc3027bfb5b18ee6d8fea1\nparent 296bd9ce6bebcfaeaa6347dbf19d806fa5be3452\nauthor Karl-Erik Gustafsson <ke.gustafsson@gmail.com> 1787436033 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787436033 +0300\n\nM5a — stack writes over the API (#24)\n\nStart, stop, update, git redeploy, create from a compose file or a\nrepository, and delete. The compose editor in the panel is M5b.\n\nEvery call that names a stack id resolves it against this environment''s\nstacks first: Portainer will act on any stack the configured credential can\nreach, including one belonging to a different environment.\n\nWhat is sent is stated rather than defaulted. Prune is off unless asked\nfor, an update with no environment keeps the one the stack already had, and\nvolumes survive a delete unless removal is asked for. A create picks the\nswarm or standalone route from the environment and carries the SwarmID\nswarm requires.\n\nTwo things Portainer does quietly are refused here. A redeploy needs a\nrepository, and an update must not touch a stack that has one: Portainer''s\nupdate handler detaches such a stack from git and clears its auto-update\nsettings, so it silently stops being what the repository describes. For a\nfile-based stack that had auto-update, the answer carries a warning, since\nno field in the request could have kept it.\n\nStack-level self-protection is the guard that matters most. Container\nself-protection catches \"stop this container\"; stopping, updating,\nredeploying or deleting the stack around it reaches the same outcome by\nnaming something one level up. The check reads the compose project and\nswarm namespace labels off the containers themselves and counts a Signal K\nthat is currently stopped. Starting a stack is left alone.\n\nBodies are parsed rather than trusted, bounded at 512kb, and their failures\nanswer in the same { error, hint } shape as everything else. TLS\nverification is never disabled by a request.\n\n497 tests.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqihwBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdUkQABhdqysm+DEQuNTfQAbVCHFB\nlpTGNwhcPJtZMCE5RzPc6K2ft6ZV4GkAgXuYjgKAVw9Q1Y99l62XPz8EIWzplyGT\nNy/40k6PvtxYhnaANCqPO2j17aMimJh2UsqKXO73GRv4S8fypc0ORvRBzha2Myo+\nSR7+CUJwhsRzBIL/Y9+A2yMtJayPitWkMHIleBtUQ5HShkS230MC8hvxlq5kbLfP\n6rR1mqITob/izohY/JHaahRxsGigeinvxM8y4OF79dy4PBhF86OI+2gYrQP5yAKX\nacHjSA7nPN1gdZaPFrEZjou5H2lQQFeQwjNo68aqZzcEZcJ3BqFPhXNsjDfd0lns\nnXn+UNNqMgd8gsi/9kLyo472IuJ0AJE+VvSErgftXG6o+ObQBjeHx0Z0rvts21Ag\nKMYmNNCk+AUATc4ziiW2Na24oDVnL1lh6LTwGuNuQ4KaYAnok5G4vE9M9PdnwazI\nn21gvoaQ2fzakyAgLWIcE1QuIbzE3IDKpiHoP8A6VYIFuzV2BdettVqCs0Z9DbA4\ndieC5hiwo3s3bqGhMhsEOMnXvttKUf++GtjBqjGihKc5HrRCXiuMo/ofvnTsdYde\nfJcy4TeA0TlDVYSI1fT4z4ZlEbZLPZtza39Lw7bPDxAAWhN+FT54ujghqJiJT9yk\nw55rO6a7gfvTJtkGIzNl\n=W0eq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T22:00:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-