m/users/sreevsr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/commits/c614857550c8817b02b1133fd8778c4c8668f193/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-10T11:26:16Z","email":"srinidhi.ts@gmail.com","name":"srinidhi sreevatsa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-10T11:26:16Z","email":"srinidhi.ts@gmail.com","name":"srinidhi sreevatsa"},"message":"Fix stale README: architecture diagram, project structure tree, utils\n\nThe architecture diagram still showed locators/ nested under\ntest-data/ and was missing new core/config entries (Tracker, safety\nguard). The project structure tree had the same locators path error,\nlisted deleted files (login-page.locators.json naming), and was\nmissing 5 recently-added utils (auth, rate-limiter, contract, logger,\ns3), production-safety-guard.ts, test-resource-tracker.ts,\nglobal-teardown.ts, and .dockerignore.\n\nAll three sections now match the actual repo state. A new engineer\nfollowing this tree will find every file exactly where it claims to be.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d01a37bbaa51bea63e132a287f5b9771e6aadb8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/git/trees/d01a37bbaa51bea63e132a287f5b9771e6aadb8a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/git/commits/c614857550c8817b02b1133fd8778c4c8668f193","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113003078?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sreevsr","id":113003078,"login":"sreevsr","node_id":"U_kgDOBrxKRg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sreevsr/playwright-framework/commit/c614857550c8817b02b1133fd8778c4c8668f193","node_id":"C_kwDOR9Wx_toAKGM2MTQ4NTc1NTBjODgxN2IwMmIxMTMzZmQ4Nzc4YzRjODY2OGYxOTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sreevsr/playwright-framework/commit/d72a333c06a78450ca3068227dae7e001877967c","sha":"d72a333c06a78450ca3068227dae7e001877967c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/commits/d72a333c06a78450ca3068227dae7e001877967c"}],"sha":"c614857550c8817b02b1133fd8778c4c8668f193","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/commits/c614857550c8817b02b1133fd8778c4c8668f193"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113003078?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sreevsr","id":113003078,"login":"sreevsr","node_id":"U_kgDOBrxKRg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/commits/d72a333c06a78450ca3068227dae7e001877967c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-10T09:29:40Z","email":"srinidhi.ts@gmail.com","name":"srinidhi sreevatsa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-10T09:29:40Z","email":"srinidhi.ts@gmail.com","name":"srinidhi sreevatsa"},"message":"Fix Windows compatibility: CSV line endings, lock file deletion, /tmp/ paths\n\nTwo code bugs that would break on Windows:\n\n1. core/test-data-loader.ts: CSV parser used .split(''\\n'') which leaves\n   \\r attached to field values on Windows. Changed to .split(/\\r?\\n/)\n   to handle both Unix and Windows line endings.\n\n2. core/shared-state.ts: stale lock file deletion via unlinkSync fails\n   on Windows with EACCES when another process holds the handle (Unix\n   allows unlinking open files; Windows does not). Added a 3-attempt\n   retry loop with short pauses to cover the Windows case.\n\nDocumentation fixes:\n- Replaced all /tmp/ paths in README examples and s3-helpers JSDoc\n  with relative paths (downloads/). /tmp/ does not exist on Windows\n  and engineers copying these examples would get ENOENT errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"68e076cb16c6f2a07bb184c4d75068cf9cb46217","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/git/trees/68e076cb16c6f2a07bb184c4d75068cf9cb46217"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/git/commits/d72a333c06a78450ca3068227dae7e001877967c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113003078?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sreevsr","id":113003078,"login":"sreevsr","node_id":"U_kgDOBrxKRg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sreevsr/playwright-framework/commit/d72a333c06a78450ca3068227dae7e001877967c","node_id":"C_kwDOR9Wx_toAKGQ3MmEzMzNjMDZhNzg0NTBjYTMwNjgyMjdkYWU3ZTAwMTg3Nzk2N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sreevsr/playwright-framework/commit/330111e463b4cad80ece1c7519529f52744b4315","sha":"330111e463b4cad80ece1c7519529f52744b4315","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/commits/330111e463b4cad80ece1c7519529f52744b4315"}],"sha":"d72a333c06a78450ca3068227dae7e001877967c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/commits/d72a333c06a78450ca3068227dae7e001877967c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113003078?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sreevsr","id":113003078,"login":"sreevsr","node_id":"U_kgDOBrxKRg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/commits/330111e463b4cad80ece1c7519529f52744b4315/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-10T05:07:07Z","email":"srinidhi.ts@gmail.com","name":"srinidhi sreevatsa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-10T05:07:07Z","email":"srinidhi.ts@gmail.com","name":"srinidhi sreevatsa"},"message":"Add utility catalog, quick-lookup table, and recipes section to README\n\nReplace the flat Utilities Reference table with three discovery layers:\n\n1. Utility Quick Lookup — \"I need to...\" table mapping problems to\n   solutions. Engineers scan this first to find the right module.\n\n2. Utility Catalog — one-paragraph-per-module reference with what it\n   does, when to use it, and a 3-5 line code example. Covers all 16\n   built-in utility modules.\n\n3. Recipes — copy-pasteable patterns for common needs that don''t\n   warrant a built-in utility (PDF text extraction, PDF comparison,\n   image comparison with pixelmatch, Excel parsing via exceljs, XML\n   parsing via fast-xml-parser, OCR via tesseract.js). Each recipe\n   names the library, shows the install command, and gives a complete\n   working test.\n\nThe recipes section makes the framework''s boundaries explicit: we ship\nutilities when the framework adds real value beyond the raw library;\nwe document recipes when the library''s own API is already clean\nenough. This signals professional maturity without bloating the\ncodebase.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"36faa3faeb22e100e2e47fa76d3a19f282fddc32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/git/trees/36faa3faeb22e100e2e47fa76d3a19f282fddc32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/git/commits/330111e463b4cad80ece1c7519529f52744b4315","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113003078?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sreevsr","id":113003078,"login":"sreevsr","node_id":"U_kgDOBrxKRg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sreevsr/playwright-framework/commit/330111e463b4cad80ece1c7519529f52744b4315","node_id":"C_kwDOR9Wx_toAKDMzMDExMWU0NjNiNGNhZDgwZWNlMWM3NTE5NTI5ZjUyNzQ0YjQzMTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sreevsr/playwright-framework/commit/a23481b4aba6255a7dec52e8f77f478755cd90b8","sha":"a23481b4aba6255a7dec52e8f77f478755cd90b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/commits/a23481b4aba6255a7dec52e8f77f478755cd90b8"}],"sha":"330111e463b4cad80ece1c7519529f52744b4315","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/commits/330111e463b4cad80ece1c7519529f52744b4315"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113003078?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sreevsr","id":113003078,"login":"sreevsr","node_id":"U_kgDOBrxKRg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sreevsr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/commits/a23481b4aba6255a7dec52e8f77f478755cd90b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-10T04:44:22Z","email":"srinidhi.ts@gmail.com","name":"srinidhi sreevatsa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-10T04:44:22Z","email":"srinidhi.ts@gmail.com","name":"srinidhi sreevatsa"},"message":"Add harvested utilities: auth, rate limiter, safety guard, logger,\nresource tracker, contract validation, S3 helpers\n\nUtility harvest from gaia-test-suite and WebMD-playwright-API, filtered\nto only genuinely generic, gap-filling code. Domain-specific and\nduplicate utilities were rejected.\n\nWave 1 — standalone utilities:\n- utils/auth-helpers.ts: generateBasicAuth, generateBearerToken,\n  generateApiKeyHeader. Pure functions, no I/O.\n- utils/rate-limiter.ts: token-bucket throttler with concurrency cap\n  and adaptive mode. Serialized acquisition queue eliminates decrement\n  races; semaphore-style permit transfer eliminates concurrency-cap\n  races (both bugs caught and fixed by the unit tests during build).\n- config/production-safety-guard.ts: detects production-shaped\n  environments via configurable regex, warns loudly, does NOT block.\n  Wired into global-setup.ts as step 0. Customers who want a hard\n  block can check the result and exit(1) themselves.\n- utils/logger.ts: structured logger with optional pino backend and\n  console fallback. LOG_LEVEL env var controls verbosity. Replaces all\n  console.log calls in framework files (global-setup, global-teardown,\n  base-fixtures). Lifecycle demo console.logs intentionally preserved.\n\nWave 2 — core capabilities:\n- core/test-resource-tracker.ts: tracks resources created during a\n  test, cleans them up in LIFO order in fixture teardown even on\n  failure. Errors aggregated, never mask real test result. New\n  resourceTracker fixture in base-fixtures.ts.\n- utils/contract-helpers.ts: zod-powered API response schema\n  validation. zod added as devDependency. validateContract() parses\n  response JSON, validates against a schema, returns typed result or\n  throws readable field-level errors.\n\nWave 3 — AWS:\n- utils/s3-helpers.ts: generatePresignedUrl, copyS3Object,\n  s3ObjectExists, downloadS3Object. Uses @aws-sdk/client-s3 v3 as\n  optional peer dep (dynamic require, clear install error).\n\nWave 4 — documentation:\n- README: three new sections (Production Safety, Test Data Cleanup,\n  Logging), five new entries in Utilities Reference, two new Roadmap\n  items (#7 TMS integration, #8 message broker helpers), Snowflake\n  added to Roadmap #2.\n- CLAUDE.md: architecture section updated with new core/utils/config.\n\nTests: 23/23 pass (5 auth + 4 rate-limiter + 3 contract + 3 resource-\ntracker + 3 original API + 5 UI). Typecheck clean. Smoke 4/4.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bdb92843a861b13f7f6630100e7050aa08a64fb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/git/trees/bdb92843a861b13f7f6630100e7050aa08a64fb7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sreevsr/playwright-framework/git/commits/a23481b4aba6255a7dec52e8f77f478755cd90b8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"ht